2862332f357328ba5d6b.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_112.png[/img]{%employer% shoves a sizeable crate into your hands before he or you even says a word.%SPEECH_ON%Look at that, the cargo I need delivering has already found someone to ship it off! What wonder!%SPEECH_OFF%He drops the theatrics.%SPEECH_ON%I need that taken to %objective% where a man by the name of %recipient% is waiting for it. It may look small, but I'm willing to pay good crowns to be sure it gets there safe and sound. You interested? Or is it a little too heavy for your arms?%SPEECH_OFF% | You find %employer% closing a box up. He quickly glances up, as though he's been caught with his pants down.%SPEECH_ON%Sellsword! Thank you for coming.%SPEECH_OFF%He locks the latches with a few quick snaps. Then he pats the crate a few times, even leans on it as though it needed one more, fat latch.%SPEECH_ON%This here cargo has to be delivered safely to %objective%. A man by the name of %recipient% is waiting for it. I do not believe the task will be easy, as the cargo is rather precious to certain people who'd go to great lengths to acquire it, which is why I'm turning to a man of your... experiences. Are you interested in doing this for me?%SPEECH_OFF% | As you enter %employer%'s room he and one of his servants are nailing a box shut.%SPEECH_ON%Good seeing you, sellsword. One moment, please. No, idiot, hold the nail that way! I know I hit your thumb before, but I won't do it again.%SPEECH_OFF%His servant reluctantly holds a nail while the man hammers it home. Finished, he wipes the sweat off his brow and looks to you.%SPEECH_ON%I need this here crate delivered to %objective% about %days% %direction% by road. It's going to %recipient%, you know. Him. Alright, maybe you don't know him. What I do know is that this may not ordinarily be your line of work, but I'm willing to pay some serious crowns for you to see it through. That's your real business, right? Earning some crowns?%SPEECH_OFF% | %employer% folds his hands together when he sees you.%SPEECH_ON%This might be a strange question, but how interested are you in making a delivery for me?%SPEECH_OFF%You explain that, for the right price, such a journey would be a welcome departure from the usual killing and dying that goes on around you. The man claps his hands together.%SPEECH_ON%Excellent! Unfortunately, I don't expect it to be quite like that. It's of enough import to garner unsavory attention, which is why I'm looking to hire sellswords in the first place. It's going to %objective%, %days% or so %direction% of here by road, where a man by the name of %recipient% is waiting for it to fall into his hands. So, you see, this won't be the 'departure' you speak of, but it can be a fine payday if you're interested.%SPEECH_OFF% | %employer%'s men are standing around a bit of cargo. Their employer shoos them away when he sees you.%SPEECH_ON%Welcome, welcome. Good seeing you. I'm in need of armed guards to have this here package delivered to a man by the name of %recipient% in %objective%. I reckon it's about %days% of travel for a company as your. How interested would you be in doing that for me?%SPEECH_OFF% | %employer%'s got his feet up on his table when you enter. He puts his hands behind his head, looking a little too relaxed for your tastes.%SPEECH_ON%Good tidings, captain. What say you take a leave from all that killing and dying.%SPEECH_OFF%He raises an eyebrow at your response, which is precisely none at all.%SPEECH_ON%Huh, I figured you'd jump on that opportunity. No matter, it was a lie: I need you to take a certain package to %recipient%, a fellow residing in %objective%. This cargo has undoubtedly garnered some ill-intentioned eyes which is why I need your men watching it for me. If you're interested, which you should be, let's talk numbers.%SPEECH_OFF% | %employer% welcomes you, waving you in.%SPEECH_ON%Very well, now that you're here, would you please shut the door behind you?%SPEECH_OFF%One of the man's guards pokes his head around the corner. You smile as you slowly shut him out. Turning around, you find %employer% walking toward a window. He stares out as he talks.%SPEECH_ON%I need something... it's a, uh, well you don't need to know what it is. I need this 'something' delivered to a fellow called %recipient%. He's waiting for it in %objective%. It's important that it actually gets there, important enough for an armed escort for %days% of travel, which is why I'm turning to you and your company. What say you, mercenary?%SPEECH_OFF% | Dim candles barely light the room enough for you to see, it's %employer% sitting behind his desk while his shadows dance on the walls by the tune of flickering lights.%SPEECH_ON%Would you lend your swords to me if I paid you good coin? I need {a small chest | something dear to me | something valuable} delivered safely to %recipient% in %objective%, about %days% of travel %direction% of here. Men have killed each other over this, so you must be ready to defend it with your life.%SPEECH_OFF%He takes a pause, measuring your response.%SPEECH_ON%I will write a sealed letter with instructions to pay you as you deliver the item to my contact in %objective%. What say you?%SPEECH_OFF% | A servant bids you to wait for %employer%, who, he says, will be right with you. And so you wait, and wait, and wait. And finally, as you are about to leave for the second time, %employer% throws open the doors and rushes towards you.%SPEECH_ON%Who's this, again? The mercenary?%SPEECH_OFF%His assistant nods and %employer% sets on a smile.%SPEECH_ON%Oh most fortuitous to have you in %townname%, good captain!

It is imperative that some precious commodities of mine reach %objective% as safely and quickly as possible. You are precisely who I need, for no common brigand would dare attack you and your men.

Yes, I'd like to hire you for escort. Make sure the items are delivered to %recipient%, no detours of course. Can we come to an understanding?%SPEECH_OFF%}

2862332f357328ba5d6b.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_112.png[/img]{你们谁都还没开口，%employer%就将一只不小的木箱塞进你手里。%SPEECH_ON%瞧瞧！这批正愁没人送的货，已经自己找着送货人了！真是奇妙！%SPEECH_OFF%他收起了夸张的腔调。%SPEECH_ON%我要把它送到%objective%，一个叫%recipient%的人正等着收。东西看着不大，但我愿意出好价钱，保证它完好送达。有兴趣吗？还是说，你的胳膊扛不动它？%SPEECH_OFF% | 你找到%employer%时，他正在合上箱盖。他飞快抬头，那神情仿佛没穿裤子就被人撞了个正着。%SPEECH_ON%佣兵！多谢你来。%SPEECH_OFF%他咔嗒几声扣好锁扣，又拍了拍箱子，甚至把身子压在上面，像是还要加上一道肥硕的锁。%SPEECH_ON%这批货必须安全送到%objective%，交给一个叫%recipient%的人。我不觉得这事轻松。有些人十分看重它，会不择手段把它弄到手。所以我才找上你这种……见过世面的人。愿意替我跑一趟吗？%SPEECH_OFF% | 你走进%employer%的房间时，他正和一个仆人往箱盖上钉钉子。%SPEECH_ON%见到你真好，佣兵。稍等一下。不对，蠢货，钉子要那样拿！我知道上次砸中了你的拇指，这回不会了。%SPEECH_OFF%仆人勉强扶住钉子，他将钉子锤了进去。忙完后，他抹去额头的汗，转向你。%SPEECH_ON%我要把这个箱子送到%objective%，沿路向%direction%走，大约%days%的路程。交给%recipient%，你知道，就是他。好吧，也许你不认识。我知道，这平常可能不是你们干的活，但只要办妥，我愿意出一大笔克朗。你们真正的行当，不就是挣钱吗？%SPEECH_OFF% | %employer%见到你，将双手交握起来。%SPEECH_ON%这问题也许有点奇怪，你愿不愿意替我送一趟货？%SPEECH_OFF%你解释，只要价钱合适，走一趟路，离那些打打杀杀远些，倒也不错。他拍了拍手。%SPEECH_ON%太好了！可惜，我不指望这事能那么清静。东西足够重要，会招来些不怀好意的目光，所以我才要找佣兵。送到%objective%，沿路向%direction%走，大约%days%就到，一个叫%recipient%的人正等着收。你看，这恐怕不是你说的那种“清闲差事”，不过只要愿意接，报酬会很不错。%SPEECH_OFF% | %employer%的手下围着一批货物。他一见你来，便挥手将他们赶开。%SPEECH_ON%欢迎，欢迎，见到你真好。我需要武装护卫，将这个包裹送给%objective%的%recipient%。像你们这样的队伍，我估计走上%days%就到了。愿意替我办吗？%SPEECH_OFF% | 你进门时，%employer%正把双脚翘在桌上。他双手枕着后脑勺，悠闲得让你看着不太舒服。%SPEECH_ON%你好啊，团长。想不想从那些杀人送命的事里歇一歇？%SPEECH_OFF%见你毫无反应，他挑起眉毛。%SPEECH_ON%嗯，我还以为你会迫不及待呢。无妨，刚才那话是骗你的：我要你将一个包裹交给住在%objective%的%recipient%。这批货毫无疑问已经被歹人盯上，所以需要你的手下替我守着。你要是有兴趣，当然，你理应有兴趣，咱们就谈谈价钱。%SPEECH_OFF% | %employer%挥手请你进来。%SPEECH_ON%很好，既然来了，劳烦把身后的门关上？%SPEECH_OFF%一名卫兵从拐角探出头。你笑了笑，慢慢将他关在门外。转过身，%employer%正走向窗边，望着外面开口。%SPEECH_ON%我有件东西……是个，呃，你不必知道是什么。我要将这“东西”交给一个叫%recipient%的人，他在%objective%等着。它必须送到，重要到值得安排武装护送，走上%days%。这就是我来找你和战团的原因。怎么样，佣兵？%SPEECH_OFF% | 昏暗烛光只勉强照亮房间。%employer%坐在书桌后，影子随着火苗在墙上摇曳。%SPEECH_ON%若我出个好价钱，你愿意为我效劳吗？我要把{一只小箱子 | 一件心爱之物 | 一件贵重物品}安全送给%objective%的%recipient%，沿路向%direction%走，大约%days%就到。已有不少人为它自相残杀，你们必须做好以性命守护它的准备。%SPEECH_OFF%他停顿片刻，观察你的反应。%SPEECH_ON%我会写一封封好的信，吩咐我在%objective%的接头人，收到货就付钱。如何？%SPEECH_OFF% | 仆人请你稍候，说%employer%马上就来。于是你等啊等，等了又等。终于，在你第二次打算起身离开时，%employer%猛地推开门，快步走来。%SPEECH_ON%这位是谁来着？那个佣兵？%SPEECH_OFF%助手点头，%employer%便堆起笑容。%SPEECH_ON%好团长，你能到%townname%来，实在再好不过！

我有些珍贵货物，必须尽快安全送到%objective%。你正是我需要的人，寻常强盗绝不敢招惹你和你的手下。

没错，我想雇你护送。请务必将东西交给%recipient%，当然，不许绕路。我们能谈拢吗？%SPEECH_OFF%}

5b9a1858b718a7299629.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_20.png[/img]{%employer% angrily shakes his head.%SPEECH_ON%Brigands have been tearing up these parts for far too long! I sent a lad, %randomname%'s son, to go find them. And you know what? Only his head came back. Of course, the idiot brigands sent one of their own to deliver it. We captured and interrogated him... so now we know where they're at.%SPEECH_OFF%The man leans back, pedaling his thumbs over one another in thought.%SPEECH_ON%I do not have the men, but I do have the crowns - what say I slip some your way, and you slip a sword theirs?%SPEECH_OFF% | %employer% pours himself a drink, stares at the cup, and pours himself some more. He seems to drain it in one gulp before belching his news.%SPEECH_ON%Brigands killed %randomname% and his whole family. Can you believe that? I know you don't know who they are, but they were a well-liked family in these parts. I'm sure you can already imagine, but I want these brigands done with. I spent half my men just finding their camp, now I'm ready to spend ha... some of my crowns for you to go kill them. Are you interested?%SPEECH_OFF% | %employer% is looking out a window, dancing a finger along the rim of a drink as he weighs his thoughts.%SPEECH_ON%Brigands have been taking off with precious livestock. They come in the night, the brigands I mean, and cut the bells to make off all quiet like. I'm sure livestock aren't important to you, but one calf, one cow, one bull? That's a fortune to some people around these parts.

So the other day I have a lad follow the animal tracks out of town and now he's told me exactly where those brigands are. As I'm sure you could guess, I don't have the men to spare to take these vagabonds on, but crowns... crowns I am not short on. If I were to cross your palms with copper, would you be willing to cross these brigands with steel?%SPEECH_OFF% | %employer% sighs as if he's tired of all these troubles, as though he's about to start a conversation he's already had many times before.%SPEECH_ON%%randomname%, a man of some import here, states that brigands made a pass on his daughters. Now he's worried what they'll do the next time. Luckily, that man is of some wealth and could easily track these brigands down. If I were to pay you a decent sum, how earnestly could you drive one of them swords of yours through a brigand or two?%SPEECH_OFF% | %employer% takes a seat in a chair big enough to be comfortable for two. He bandies a mug back and forth.%SPEECH_ON%Brigands have been harrying us for weeks now and just yesterday they tried to set fire to a pub. Can you believe that? Who sets fire to such a thing? Luckily we put it out just in time, but things are getting bad around here. If they threaten our precious drink, what will they do next? Luckily, we managed to find where these vagrants are hiding. So... yes I see your look. It's a simple task, sellsword: we want you to go kill every last brigand there. Are you willing to work with us?%SPEECH_OFF% | As you settle into the room, %employer% finishes a goblet of cobra wine and heaves the cup out a window. You hear the din of it clattering hollow far, far away. He turns to you.%SPEECH_ON%While walking the roads, brigands swarmed my wagon and made off with all my goods! They left me my life, which is fine, but the gall of what they did keeps me up at night. I see their sneering faces... hear their laughter... I believe it was a message, to go after me, because I refused to pay their 'tolls'. Well, now I am ready to pay a toll - to you, sellsword. If you go and slaughter these vagabonds, I'll pay a tidy toll indeed. What say you?%SPEECH_OFF% | As you begin to take a seat, %employer% throws a scroll at you. It unfurls just as you catch it. You begin to read, but %employer% starts in with the news anyway.%SPEECH_ON%Traders from %randomtown% have all agreed to no longer patronize %townname% until our little brigand problem is done away with. The history of it is pretty simple, as I'm sure you're aware of the brigands' methods, but these damn vagabonds have been harrying the roads, pillaging caravans and killing merchants.

I know exactly where they are, I just need a man of guts and in need of glory - or gold! - to go and kill them. So what say you, mercenary? Name a price and we can talk.%SPEECH_OFF% | %employer% is shaking when you greet him. He's practically frothing with anger - or maybe he's just really drunk.%SPEECH_ON%Citizens of this fine town are starving. Why? Because brigands keep sneaking in during the night to raid the granaries! And if we catch them, they burn the buildings down! Now we can't defend ourselves by sitting back... Now... I want to defend myself by killing them all.%SPEECH_OFF%The man teeters for a moment, as if about to spill himself across his desk. He steadies before continuing.%SPEECH_ON%I want you to go kill these vagrants, obviously. All you have to do is be interested and... -hic-... name your price.%SPEECH_OFF% | %employer% looks solemnly at the ground. He unfurls a scroll, showing you a face.%SPEECH_ON%This is %randomname%, a brigand at large who we captured the other day. He once lead an outfit of vagrants that used to harry and raid our town day and night. Problem is, he's not really the head of a snake, but one head of a hydra. Kill one criminal head, another takes its place. So what's the answer? Why, kill them ALL of course. And that's exactly what I want you to do, sellsword. Are you interested?%SPEECH_OFF% | %employer% turns to you as you look for somewhere to sit.%SPEECH_ON%Hoy, mercenary, how long has it been since you've slaked your sword with the blood of evil, cruel men?%SPEECH_OFF%He drops the sarcasm and you figure you'll be standing now.%SPEECH_ON%We here at %townname% are having a bit of a tiff with some local brigands. Local to us, that is, with their little rat's hole not far from here. Obviously, I think the answer to this issue is to hire some finely armed men such as your little company of goodfellas. So, does that pique your interest, mercenary, or do I need to find sturdier men for this task?%SPEECH_OFF%}

5b9a1858b718a7299629.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_20.png[/img]{%employer%愤怒地摇着头。%SPEECH_ON%那些强盗祸害这里太久了！我派了个小伙子去找他们，是%randomname%的儿子。结果你猜怎么着？只送回来一颗脑袋。当然，那群蠢强盗还派了自己人来送。我们抓住他，审了一番……所以，现在知道他们躲在哪儿了。%SPEECH_OFF%男人向后靠去，两根拇指绕着圈，若有所思。%SPEECH_ON%我手里没兵，但有克朗。不如这样，我给你送钱，你给他们送一剑，如何？%SPEECH_OFF% | %employer%给自己倒了杯酒，看看杯子，又添了一些。他仿佛一口就将酒喝干，打着嗝说出消息。%SPEECH_ON%强盗杀了%randomname%一家，满门一个不剩。你能相信吗？我知道你不认识他们，不过，那家人在这里很受喜欢。你应该也猜得到，我要让这些强盗彻底完蛋。光是找到他们的营地，就耗掉我一半人手。现在，我准备花掉半……花些克朗，请你去杀了他们。你有兴趣吗？%SPEECH_OFF% | %employer%望着窗外，一根手指沿杯沿轻划，斟酌着心事。%SPEECH_ON%强盗一直在偷宝贵的牲畜。他们趁夜来，我说的是强盗，割掉牲口的铃铛，悄无声息地牵走。我知道，你大概不把牲畜当回事，可一头牛犊、一头母牛、一头公牛，对这里某些人而言，就是整副家当。

前几天，我让个小伙子沿着牲畜的蹄印追出镇子。他回来了，也告诉我那些强盗究竟藏在哪儿。你想必猜得到，我腾不出人手去对付这些流寇，不过钱……我可不缺钱。若我把铜钱交到你掌中，你愿不愿意把钢剑送进他们身体里？%SPEECH_OFF% | %employer%叹了口气，仿佛已被这些麻烦磨得精疲力尽，又要开始一场重复过无数次的谈话。%SPEECH_ON%%randomname%在这里有些地位。他说，强盗调戏了他的女儿们，如今正担心那些人下次会干什么。幸好，他颇有家财，没费多少工夫就查出了强盗的下落。要是我出一笔像样的报酬，你愿意多卖力地把剑捅进几个强盗的身子里？%SPEECH_OFF% | %employer%坐进一张大椅子，宽得足够两个人舒舒服服地挤着。他将酒杯来回晃动。%SPEECH_ON%强盗已经骚扰我们好几个星期。就在昨天，他们竟想放火烧酒馆！你能相信吗？什么人才会烧那种地方？幸好我们及时扑灭了火，不过，情况越来越糟。他们连宝贵的酒都敢动，下一步还想干什么？好在，我们找到了这些流寇的藏身处。所以……是，我看见你的表情了。差事很简单，佣兵：去那里，把每一个强盗都杀光。你愿意跟我们合作吗？%SPEECH_OFF% | 你刚在房间里站定，%employer%便喝干杯中的眼镜蛇酒，顺手将酒杯扔出窗外。空杯碰撞的声响从很远、很远的地方传来。他转向你。%SPEECH_ON%我走在路上，一群强盗扑上货车，把货物全抢走了！他们倒是留了我一条命，这还算好，可那副放肆劲儿，让我夜夜睡不着。我看得见他们嘲笑的脸……听得见他们的笑声……我想，特意找上我，就是为了传个话，因为我不肯交他们的‘过路费’。好，现在我愿意交了——交给你，佣兵。你若去把这些流寇杀光，这笔过路费，我会给得相当丰厚。如何？%SPEECH_OFF% | 你刚要坐下，%employer%就扔来一卷卷轴。你接住时，它正好展开。还没读几行，%employer%已经开始说明情况。%SPEECH_ON%%randomtown%的商人全都说好了，在我们解决这点强盗麻烦之前，谁也不来%townname%做买卖。事情的经过很简单，你肯定知道强盗那套手段。这些该死的流寇霸着道路，洗劫商队，杀害商人。

我很清楚他们在哪儿，只差一个有胆量、想求名声的人——或者想求财的人！去把他们杀了。佣兵，你怎么说？开个价，我们谈谈。%SPEECH_OFF% | 你向%employer%问好，他却浑身发抖，几乎气得口吐白沫，也可能只是醉得厉害。%SPEECH_ON%这么好的镇子，百姓却在挨饿。为什么？因为强盗每晚偷偷溜进来，抢粮仓！一旦被发现，就放火烧房子！现在，我们不能再干坐着自保了……现在……我要把他们全杀了，这才叫自保。%SPEECH_OFF%男人晃了晃，险些整个人扑上桌，好不容易站稳，才继续说道：%SPEECH_ON%明摆着，我要你去杀掉这些流寇。你只需要愿意……嗝……再报个价。%SPEECH_OFF% | %employer%神色凝重地望着地面。他展开一卷卷轴，上面画着一张脸。%SPEECH_ON%这是%randomname%，一个曾经逍遥法外、前几天才被我们抓住的强盗。他带过一伙流寇，日夜骚扰、劫掠镇子。问题是，他不是什么一砍就死的蛇头，而是多头蛇的一颗脑袋。除掉一个头目，又会冒出另一个。那该怎么办？当然是把他们全杀光。这正是我要你做的事，佣兵。有兴趣吗？%SPEECH_OFF% | 你正寻找坐处，%employer%转过身来。%SPEECH_ON%喂，佣兵，你的剑有多久没饮过邪恶残暴之徒的鲜血了？%SPEECH_OFF%他收起讥诮的口气，你估计自己还是站着算了。%SPEECH_ON%我们%townname%和本地一伙强盗，有点小摩擦。所谓本地，就是说，他们的小鼠窝离这儿不远。显然，我认为解决办法，就是雇一群武装精良的人，比如你这支好汉云集的小战团。那么，佣兵，有兴趣了吗？还是说，这活儿得另找些更硬气的汉子？%SPEECH_OFF%}

497a069f59f45295c515.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_60.png[/img]{You spit and clear you throat, then you quickly clear your sword of its sheath and strike the caravan guard down. %randombrother% sees this and quickly barks out an order for the rest of the %companyname% to follow suit. There's a brief, confused carnage, the caravan guards unsure of what's going on as your men set upon them.

 Freeing the prisoner, he thanks you profusely then tells you to lead the way.%SPEECH_ON%Once we get to %noblesettlement%, and they see my lively and grinning face, you will be washed in crowns!%SPEECH_OFF% | You draw your sword and slash the guard across the face. He spins around and you crash the blade of your weapon through his brainpain, his organ frothing between slanted boneshards like a burst souffle. %randombrother% sees this and calls the rest of the company to combat. They make short work of the rest of the caravan guards. When you free %noble%, he points down the road.%SPEECH_ON%To %noblesettlement% where my family shall reward you like you cannot believe!%SPEECH_OFF% | As the caravan guard turns around, you take a dagger and jam it beneath his arm pit and directly into his heart. He muffles something, then falls to the ground. Another guard comes around, sees this, then sees your sword disembowel him. His cries, however, are not muffled. A battle soon commences, though it is completely lopsided as the %companyname% makes short work of the caravan guards.

 Once it is all said and done, %noble% is freed. Rubbing his purpled wrists, he points you toward %noblesettlement%.%SPEECH_ON%Onward, return me to my family so that I can fill your pockets for this incredible bravery!%SPEECH_OFF%}

497a069f59f45295c515.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_60.png[/img]{你啐了一口，清清嗓子，随即拔剑，将商队护卫砍倒。%randombrother%见状，立刻大声命令%companyname%的其余人一同动手。杀戮短促而混乱，弟兄们已经扑到面前，商队护卫还没弄清发生了什么。

你解开囚犯的锁链。他千恩万谢，随即让你带路。%SPEECH_ON%只要到了%noblesettlement%，让他们看见我这张活蹦乱跳、笑容满面的脸，你就等着被克朗淹没吧！%SPEECH_OFF% | 你拔剑划过护卫的脸。他转过身，你又一剑劈开他的头颅，脑浆从斜插的碎骨之间涌出，像破裂的酥点。%randombrother%看见这一幕，立刻招呼其余弟兄投入战斗。他们很快解决了剩下的商队护卫。你放开%noble%时，他指向大路。%SPEECH_ON%去%noblesettlement%！我的家人会给你难以想象的重赏！%SPEECH_OFF% | 商队护卫刚转过身，你便把匕首从他腋下捅入，直刺心脏。他含混地哼了一声，倒在地上。另一个护卫绕过来，看见这一幕，紧接着便被你的长剑开膛破肚。他的惨叫可一点也不含糊。战斗很快打响，却完全一边倒，%companyname%轻易便杀光了商队护卫。

尘埃落定后，%noble%恢复了自由。他揉着青紫的手腕，指向%noblesettlement%。%SPEECH_ON%出发吧，送我回家！你们如此英勇，我一定要把你们的钱袋塞得满满的！%SPEECH_OFF%}

00c9b512f03dbe799580.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_07.png[/img]{While on your way, a group of armed men emerge seemingly out of nowhere to stand in your way. Amongst them is the shady figure you'd seen earlier. They announce their intention to take the envoy off your hands. In return, you'll get a large sum of money - %bribe% crowns.

Otherwise, well, they'll have to take him by force... | You're just getting into the swing of things - listening to the envoy's banter, ignoring it, wishing he'd just go off into the woods alone to never return - when suddenly a group of armed men surprise you. Standing with them is the stranger that met you earlier. They state that the envoy must be handed over. In return, you'll get the sum of %bribe% crowns. If you refuse, well, they'll just go ahead and use more violent methods.

As you mull your options the envoy is, for once, completely silent. | Marching on the road, a group of armed men come out to stop you. You recognize the stranger from earlier is standing with them. They ask you hand over the envoy, gesturing toward a very large satchel of crowns, the sum of %bribe% crowns they claim. They're also gesturing toward their weapons, suggesting they've come prepared to use other means in case you refuse.}

00c9b512f03dbe799580.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_07.png[/img]{赶路途中，一群武装人员仿佛凭空冒出，拦住了去路。你先前见过的那个鬼祟人影也在其中。他们开门见山，要你把使者交出来，作为交换，愿付一大笔钱——%bribe%克朗。

若是不肯，那就只好动手抢了…… | 你正渐渐习惯这趟差事的节奏：听使者絮叨，充耳不闻，再盼着他自己钻进树林，从此别再回来。就在这时，一群武装人员突然现身，打了你个措手不及。先前见过的陌生人也站在他们中间。他们要你交出使者，答应付给你%bribe%克朗。要是拒绝，他们便只好换些粗暴的手段。

你权衡着该如何应对，而使者这回总算彻底安静了。 | 你们沿路行进，一群武装人员出来拦住了去路。你认出先前那个陌生人也在其中。他们要求你交出使者，指了指一只鼓鼓囊囊的钱袋，说里面装着%bribe%克朗。随后，他们又示意你看看各自的武器：显然，你若不肯，他们也备好了别的办法。}

100fa32ad9ddc811da85.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_53.png[/img]{The ambush defeated, you head into the greenskins' camp to find the prisoners caged and blindfolded. You order the mercenaries to start freeing them. Thinking themselves already dead, most of the prisoners break down in tears and thank you for rescuing them. All in a day's work, really. | The greenskins' ambush failed and so you head into their camp. Any lurking greenskins quickly run off, abandoning everything. You find the prisoners in a tent, huddled together with no clothes. %randombrother% goes and gets some blankets to cover them up for the return trip to %employer%. The freedmen can hardly speak, but their eyes tell a lot about the horrors they've experienced. | The ambush has been dealt with, now you and your men start picking through the greenskins' abandoned camp. You immediately hear people start screaming from a tent. %randombrother% opens the flap to see a goblin waving a hot iron in front of a group of huddled, naked men. The sellsword cuts the creature's head off in a single swipe. The prisoners cry out, thanking you for the rescue. %employer% should be most pleased that at least some of his men will be coming home. | The ambush defeated, you and the %companyname% rush into the greenskins' encampment. There you find a goblin poking and prodding a man who has ostensibly died from torture. %randombrother% grabs the unwitting goblin and pummels it to death. You search a nearby tent to find a group of blindfolded men huddled in a corner. They skirt away from your voice, but you quickly make it clear that you're here to help them. The poor souls have been through a lot. Returning them to %employer% and their homes should make for a good recovery. | Any thought the greenskins' had about coming out ahead in that fight have been put to rest: those savages are thoroughly dead.

You order the men to start searching through their encampment to try and find the prisoners. It isn't long until %randombrother% finds the men huddled underneath a tent. They've been beaten and tortured, but they'll live. A few thank you, and most others thank the old gods. Damn deities stealing your thunder yet again. Anyway, %employer% will be most pleased. | The %companyname% dispatches with the ambush and quickly rushes into the greenskins' abandoned encampment. You find a man on a spit roasting over a fire. Another is hanging from a tree with his feet cut off. Screaming carries your attention to a nearby tent where you find the rest of the men huddled together and begging for water. Your men start handing out water and tending to their wounds. They'll need to be able to walk to get back to %employer% and their homes. | The ambush destroyed, you quickly sweep through the greenskins' camp. You find a few stragglers, including a goblin trying to make off with a bundle of trophy skulls. %randombrother% makes the savage pay for its gruesome greed with its own head.

It's not long until you find the prisoners huddled together under a sheepskin tent. One cries out.%SPEECH_ON%I knew the old gods would answer our prayers!%SPEECH_OFF%You ask if the old gods will also undo their bindings. The curious, philosophical question goes unanswered when %randombrother% rushes in and frees the prisoners. Ultimately, %employer% will be happy to see them no matter who or whatever is responsible for their rescue. | The greenskins' laid low, you and the %companyname% sweep through their encampment, slaughtering every straggler you find. The prisoners are freed from a pit in the ground where they had to piss and shit for days, it seems. They kiss the ground and thank you for the rescue. %employer% should be most pleased with this result. | The ambush has been taken care of, but what of the prisoners? You quickly rush into the abandoned greenskin encampment to find the prisoners tied to a series of posts. Unfortunately, the man at the far end has already been tortured to death. Judging by his still leaking wounds, you were just a bit too late. The rest of the prisoners scream out in ecstasy, though. One after the other kisses the earth before your feet. However, now is not the time to feel good about yourself. %employer% will be expecting you with his own thanks: a big pile of crowns.}

100fa32ad9ddc811da85.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_53.png[/img]{伏兵已被击败，你进入绿皮营地，发现俘虏们蒙着双眼，被关在笼中。你命令佣兵开始放人。大多数俘虏本以为必死无疑，此刻泣不成声，感谢你救了他们。其实，不过是一天的活罢了。 | 绿皮的伏击失败，你随即进入它们的营地。还躲着的绿皮立刻丢下一切，仓皇逃走。你在一顶帐篷里找到俘虏，他们赤身裸体，挤作一团。%randombrother%去拿来毯子，给他们裹上，好启程返回%employer%那里。获救的人几乎说不出话，可眼神已经诉尽了经历的恐怖。 | 伏击已被化解，你和弟兄们开始搜查绿皮遗弃的营地。很快，一顶帐篷里响起惊叫。%randombrother%掀开帘子，看见一只地精正拿着烧红的烙铁，在一群赤裸、挤作一团的男人面前晃动。佣兵一刀斩下那东西的脑袋。俘虏们哭喊着，感谢你来救他们。至少还有一些人能回家，%employer%应该会很高兴。 | 击败伏兵后，你带着%companyname%冲进绿皮营地。一只地精正在戳弄一个男人，那人显然已被折磨致死。%randombrother%抓住毫无察觉的地精，活活打死。你搜查附近的帐篷，发现一群蒙着双眼的人缩在角落。他们听见你的声音便往后躲，你连忙说明，自己是来救人的。这些可怜人受了太多苦，带他们回%employer%那里、回自己的家，应该能让他们慢慢恢复。 | 绿皮想赢下这场战斗的任何念头，都已彻底终结：这些蛮子死得干干净净。

你命令弟兄们搜查营地，寻找俘虏。没过多久，%randombrother%就在一顶帐篷下找到挤作一团的人。他们遭过殴打和酷刑，不过还能活下去。有几个人向你道谢，更多的人却在感谢旧神。该死的神明，又抢了你的功劳。不管怎样，%employer%会很高兴。 | %companyname%解决伏兵，迅速冲入绿皮遗弃的营地。你发现一个人被串在烤架上，架在火上炙烤；另一个人吊在树上，双脚已被砍掉。附近帐篷里的惨叫吸引了你。剩下的人挤在那里，哀求给点水喝。弟兄们开始分水、照料伤口。他们得能走路，才能回到%employer%那里，回到家中。 | 伏兵被消灭后，你迅速扫过绿皮营地，找出几个没逃掉的家伙。其中一只地精还想带走一捆充作战利品的头骨。%randombrother%砍下它自己的脑袋，让这蛮子为可怖的贪婪付了账。

不久，你便在羊皮帐篷下找到挤作一团的俘虏。其中一人喊道。%SPEECH_ON%我就知道，旧神会回应我们的祈祷！%SPEECH_OFF%你问，旧神是不是也会替他们解开绳子。这个奇特而富有哲理的问题没得到回答，因为%randombrother%已经冲进去，把俘虏们放了出来。说到底，不管救他们的是谁、是什么，%employer%见到他们都会高兴。 | 绿皮被击溃后，你带着%companyname%扫过营地，杀掉每个没逃走的家伙。俘虏从地坑里被救出，看样子，他们几天来吃喝拉撒都困在里面。他们亲吻大地，感谢你相救。%employer%应该会对这个结果十分满意。 | 伏击解决了，可俘虏呢？你急忙冲进绿皮遗弃的营地，发现他们被绑在一排木桩上。不幸的是，最远处的那个人已被折磨致死。伤口还在流血，看来你们只晚了一点。其余俘虏却狂喜地叫喊，一个接一个亲吻你脚前的土地。不过，现在还不是自我陶醉的时候。%employer%正等着用自己的方式道谢：一大堆克朗。}

994022e799f3ad3288c8.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_53.png[/img]{You run into the greenskins' encampment with weapons raised, but find the whole place abandoned. Pots of stew are turned over and there's fresh fires they were quickly left behind. %randombrother% opens a goatskin tent to find the prisoners huddled together. They praise the old gods at the very sight of you. %employer% will be happy with this result, and you're happy that the greenskins gave up without a fight. | The greenskins' camp is abandoned. You find the charred remains of a pig left over as pit and some stews kicked over. They definitely left in a hurry.

%randombrother% calls you over. The prisoners are in a hole in the ground with water up to their waists. A spiked wooden gate is stopping them from getting out, though its tangled with bloodied clothes which suggests at least one man tried. You quickly raise the cover and help them out. You look down to see one body floating in the water. They're not all coming back, but %employer% should be more than happy about these few lucky souls. | You rush into the greenskins' encampment to find the tents all spilt over and a great rush of footsteps leading away from it. They abandoned in it a quick hurry. %randombrother% laughs.%SPEECH_ON%Looks like they knew the %companyname% was coming.%SPEECH_OFF%Suddenly, a voice breaks out of one of the tents, screaming and hollering. You rush over to find a man in hysterics, splayed out on the ground while a bunch of blindfolded men huddle in the corner. The prisoners. Missing fingers, toes, eyes, noses, limbs, the tick tock of time spent in the company of greenskins. You shake your head and order the men to start handing out care. %employer% will be happy about their being alive, but these men are most certainly forever broken. | The greenskins' camp is empty. A few black birds squawk and fight over some spilt stew while feral dogs scamper at the very sight of you. Your men start searching through the goatskin tents left behind. There's nothing to be found until your foot suddenly depresses a little further into the ground than it should. You crouch down and swipe the camouflage away to reveal a trapdoor. Lifting it, you find a well chute the greenskins' had converted into a very vertical jail cell. The prisoners are squeezed together like tinder and look up at the light with withered, water-worn faces. %randombrother% looks down and grunts.%SPEECH_ON%Well, they're alive. I'll go get some rope.%SPEECH_OFF% | Footprints trail away from the camp. Judging by the spacing and littering of rubbish, they were in a hurry. %randombrother% calls out to you. He's standing outside a tent holding the flap open. When you get there, you see that it was used to house the prisoners. They're all naked and on the ground, ears plugged with twigs and eyes blindfolded. Looks like they've been beaten into not moving unless asked. There's a pile of human limbs in a corner and it looks like something had taken to using their skulls for primitive artwork. You shake your head.%SPEECH_ON%Free them and give them water. %employer% was probably hoping for the best with getting these men back, but this is just about what I expected.%SPEECH_OFF% | The greenskins' had abandoned their camp. You're not sure why, but most likely their scouts sighted your company and made a business decision to get out while they still could.

The men are ordered to look for the prisoners and it's not long until they're found: a goatskin tent with the men huddled beneath a pole with their hands bound and faces literally buried in the dirt. They've been given straws to breathe. %randombrother% hurries over and starts taking their heads out of the ground. Each man's face is purpled and gasping for air, but they're alive and the torture over. %employer% should be happy to see them coming back. | The encampment is found empty. %randombrother% picks up a spilt cauldron which leaks more sewage than stew. He drops it and shakes his head.%SPEECH_ON%Fire's still crackling. They left in a hurry.%SPEECH_OFF%You nod and order the men to fan out and look for the prisoners. No sooner than the words leave your lips do you hear someone screaming from a nearby tent. Inside, you find the prisoners - or those who have survived. On one side of the room the living are naked and huddled. On the other you see a pool of blood, an execution block, a red-stained mallet, and a couple of bodies pinched off at the heads like flowers used for bookmarks. %employer% won't be getting all his men back. | Entering the greenskins' encampment, {you find a goblin shoveling bones into a knapsack. It quickly drops its belongings. %randombrother% runs it down and puts a blade through it. | you find a wounded orc leaning against a pole. He's breathing heavy, but with a quick stab of his blade %randombrother% make sure he's not breathing at all.} The rest of the camp has been seemingly abandoned, this greenskin the last to remain. You find the prisoners in a tent. They've been blindfolded and a few are missing fingers or toes. %employer% will be most pleased. | The encampment has been abandoned, but the prisoners left behind. You rescue them, or what's left of them: some have had their fingers and toes removed, others breathe through holes where their noses used to be. But they're alive. That's what matters, right? | You come into an encampment which has been abandoned in a hurry. The greenskins most likely saw the %companyname% coming and made a smart decision to leave while they still could. The prisoners are, thankfully, found alive. They thank the old gods and bow before you like paupers before an oracular sage. You get the poor survivors water and prepare a return to %employer%. | A single orc is found at the encampment. It's resting against a cage where the prisoners are housed. One of the prisoners has a chain around the greenskin's neck and is pulling it against the bars, warden and prisoner clasped in a most ironic struggle. %randombrother% rushes over and puts a blade through the orc's eye and frees the men. The prisoners rush out of the cage kissing the earth and jumping for joy. A giddy man explains that the greenskins left in a hurry and it seems they were mighty scared. You nod and thumb over your shoulder at the sigil of the %companyname%.%SPEECH_ON%They were right to be.%SPEECH_OFF%}

994022e799f3ad3288c8.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_53.png[/img]{你们举着武器冲进绿皮营地，却发现这里早已空无一人。炖锅被掀翻在地，新生的火堆还在燃烧，显然走得十分匆忙。%randombrother%掀开一顶山羊皮帐篷，发现俘虏正蜷缩在一起。他们一见到你，就开始赞颂旧神。%employer%会对这个结果感到高兴，而绿皮不战而逃，也让你很满意。 | 绿皮营地空了。火坑边剩着一头烧焦的猪，几锅炖食被踢翻在地。它们显然走得很急。

%randombrother%叫你过去。俘虏被关在土坑里，水一直淹到腰间，带尖刺的木栅盖在上头，堵住了出口。木栅上挂着染血的衣物，看来至少有一个人试着往外爬过。你们赶紧抬起盖子，把人拉上来。低头望去，水里还漂着一具尸体。并不是所有人都能回去，但这几个幸运儿能活下来，已经足够让%employer%欣慰了。 | 你们冲进绿皮营地，只见帐篷东倒西歪，无数杂乱的脚印向外延伸。它们匆匆弃营逃走了。%randombrother%笑道。%SPEECH_ON%看来它们知道%companyname%要来了。%SPEECH_OFF%突然，一顶帐篷里传出凄厉的叫喊。你赶过去，发现一个人四肢摊开躺在地上，正歇斯底里地尖叫，角落里则挤着一群蒙住眼睛的人。是俘虏。他们失去了手指、脚趾、眼睛、鼻子或肢体，每一处残缺，都记着落入绿皮手中后的时日。你摇摇头，命令弟兄们开始救护。%employer%会庆幸他们还活着，可这些人受到的摧残，已永远无法弥合。 | 绿皮营地空无一人。几只黑鸟嘎嘎叫着，争抢洒落的炖食；野狗见到你们便四散逃窜。弟兄们开始搜查留下的山羊皮帐篷，却一无所获。忽然，你脚下的地面陷得比正常情况更深。你蹲下身，扫去伪装，露出一扇暗门。掀开后，下面是一口井，绿皮把它改成了深竖的牢房。俘虏像引火柴般紧紧塞在一起，消瘦浮肿、被水泡得发皱的脸仰望着光亮。%randombrother%往下看了一眼，哼了一声。%SPEECH_ON%好歹还活着。我去拿绳子。%SPEECH_OFF% | 一串脚印从营地向外延伸。看那步幅和沿途丢弃的杂物，绿皮走得很急。%randombrother%站在帐篷外，掀着帘子叫你过去。你走近一看，里面关着俘虏。他们全都赤身躺在地上，耳朵塞着细枝，眼睛蒙着布。看来，他们已经被打怕了，不等吩咐便不敢动弹。角落里堆着人的残肢，还有谁拿头骨做起了粗陋的装饰。你摇摇头。%SPEECH_ON%给他们松绑，喂点水。%employer%也许还盼着他们完完整整地回来，但我猜到的，大抵就是这副模样。%SPEECH_OFF% | 绿皮已经弃营而去。你不确定原因，但多半是它们的斥候发现了战团，权衡利弊后，决定趁还能跑赶紧跑。

你命令弟兄们寻找俘虏，很快便有了结果：一顶山羊皮帐篷里，一群人被绑着手，挤在木杆下，脸竟被埋进了土里，只能靠几根草管呼吸。%randombrother%赶过去，开始把他们的头从土中刨出来。每个人都憋得满脸青紫，拼命喘气，但他们还活着，折磨也终于结束了。%employer%见他们回来，应该会很高兴。 | 营地里空无一人。%randombrother%扶起一口翻倒的大锅，淌出来的东西与其说是炖食，倒更像污水。他扔下锅，摇摇头。%SPEECH_ON%火还在噼啪响。它们走得很急。%SPEECH_OFF%你点头，命令弟兄们散开寻找俘虏。话音未落，附近帐篷里便传来尖叫。进去后，你找到了俘虏——或者说，活下来的俘虏。帐篷一侧，活人赤身挤作一团；另一侧，是一滩血、一座行刑墩、一把染红的木槌，以及几具断头尸体，脑袋仿佛用来夹作书签的花朵般被掐了下来。%employer%等不到所有人回来了。 | 进入绿皮营地后，{你看见一个地精正把骨头往背囊里装。它立刻丢下东西，拔腿就跑。%randombrother%追上去，一刀刺穿了它。 | 你看见一个受伤的兽人靠着木杆，呼吸沉重。%randombrother%迅速一刀刺下，让它彻底没了呼吸。}其余绿皮似乎早已弃营而去，只剩下这个。你在帐篷里找到了俘虏。他们都蒙着眼睛，有几个人少了手指或脚趾。%employer%一定会十分满意。 | 营地已被放弃，俘虏却被留了下来。你救出了他们，或者说，救出了他们残存的躯体：有些人被切掉了手指和脚趾，有些人只能靠原本长着鼻子的地方留下的孔洞呼吸。但他们还活着。这才重要，对吧？ | 你进入一座匆匆遗弃的营地。绿皮多半看见%companyname%赶来，明智地决定趁还能逃，赶紧离开。谢天谢地，俘虏都还活着。他们感谢旧神，在你面前躬身行礼，仿佛穷人拜见能传达神谕的圣贤。你给这些可怜的幸存者送去清水，准备返回%employer%那里。 | 营地里只剩一个兽人，正靠在关押俘虏的笼子上。一名俘虏把铁链套住它的脖子，拼命往笼栏上勒。狱卒与囚犯纠缠在一起，这场搏斗透着莫大的讽刺。%randombrother%冲过去，一刀刺穿兽人的眼睛，随后把人放了出来。俘虏们冲出笼子，有人亲吻大地，有人高兴得直跳。一个兴奋不已的人说，绿皮走得仓皇，看起来害怕极了。你点点头，用拇指指了指肩后的%companyname%徽记。%SPEECH_ON%它们怕得有道理。%SPEECH_OFF%}

e17522d322d2ec7cba6a.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_167.png[/img]{The fortress is both familiar and unusual. Despite being broken apart and sliding into piles of rubble, you can't help but get a sense of eminence in its walls. Further inside, about the dilapidated armories and abandoned mess halls, there are more cursory constructs: hastily erected defenses, signs of last stands made far away from where they should be. There is no telling what happened here, or even when, but for now it will serve as the %companyname%'s temporary home.

 You walk to the crenelated walls and look out. It seems you have taken the position just in time: the northerners are already on the approach, a line of silhouettes marching just over the horizon like ants to their hill. | The fortress being a lost vestige of an ancient empire seems right: its constructs are as familiar as they are alien. You understand what walls are for, but you're not sure what to make of some of the symbols carved into them. Even the architecture of some of the rooms, the way the corners sweep in incredible bricked swirls, is not like anything you've seen. You're not sure if there is some tactical advantage there or perhaps its builders intended the designs to be of other import.

But there is no time to dally on the matter of its history, you're here to simply use it as a chokepoint. And it seems the time is at hand: a wave of northerners is crashing over the horizon and charging directly for you!}

e17522d322d2ec7cba6a.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_167.png[/img]{这座要塞既熟悉，又陌生。尽管墙体崩裂、坍成瓦砾，残墙间仍透着一种不凡的威仪。再往深处走，破败的军械库与废弃的食堂周围，还留有一些草草搭成的工事：临时防线、最后抵抗的痕迹，却远离本应死守的位置。没人知道这里发生过什么，甚至不知发生于何时。不过眼下，它将是%companyname%暂时的家。

你走到垛墙旁，向外望去。看来你们来得正及时：北方人已在逼近，一线身影越过地平线，如蚂蚁归巢般行来。 | 说这座要塞是古老帝国的失落遗存，确有道理：建筑处处似曾相识，又处处透着异样。墙的用处你明白，墙上雕刻的符号却让你摸不着头脑。就连一些房间的结构，也从未见过，墙角的砖石竟砌出奇异的旋弧。你不知道这是否有利于作战，还是建造者另有深意。

但眼下没工夫考究历史，你来这里只为扼守这处要道。而且，时候已经到了：北方人的队伍正如潮水般越过地平线，直朝你们冲来！}

23b1813bdaf1009428a6.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_110.png[/img]{The nest of webknechts is a pit of earth wreathed in white. At its rim are thin filaments which list about at even the slightest suggestion of a breeze. Marching your company inward, the webbing begins to take a sort of civilized shape, as though you were walking in from wintery hinterland, the recency of its creation apparent in its tight trappings: deer, dogs, man-sized cocoons which show no sign of life, all bound snug in the hangars of white silos and planes like morsels lost upon a pale rug. A black shadow saunters up behind the veiled domicile, coming to the fore with its legs squatting defilade, its head crouched beyond them as though the foul cretin were gated by its own stride. A human hand sucks in and out from its mandibles like some macabre pacifier. You've come to the right place. | The webknecht nest is silent and the clatter of the company's arrival seems apocryphal, with the chink and clink of metals distinctly sharp in their trespass.

 You find a man hanging upside down from a tree, his whole body cocooned save his face which is stretched and pulled by the filaments. He asks you cut his eyelids free of the webbing which you oblige. His lids slowly close, the crust of the dry eyes crackling closed for the first time in possibly days. But then they snap open and the man screams. The cocoon bubbles at his waist and rips apart, a sputtering of tiny black spiders flooding out. The man's body jolts violently around as the swarm consumes him, his gargled screams rife with the skittering of spiderlings which fill his lungs and which he coughs out in dying fits. Horrified, you step back only to see a throng of much larger spiders emerging from around the trees! | The nest is an easy spot, a stretch of winterscape where there's no cold, the white webbing patchy and listing from every tree, every copse, every inch of the place. You march the company right in, weapons drawn, and there you come across the wrapped bodies, their centers blown open and blackened, a spawn of spiderlings sucking on the organs.

  Staring up, you see red eyes flare between the branches of the surrounding trees, the whole arachnidian arboretum come alive, its wardens perched there amongst the brush with their squatted legs indistinguishable from the branches, the enemy hiding in plain sight. You damn near shit yourself when a supposed tree unfolds entirely, every wooden stalk but a spider leg, the arborous sleight descending on the company chittering and chamfering for a bite!}

23b1813bdaf1009428a6.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_110.png[/img]{巨蛛巢穴是一处被白丝裹住的土坑。坑沿垂着细丝，哪怕只有一丝微风，也会随之飘摇。你率战团向内走，蛛网渐渐显出一种居所般的形态，仿佛正从寒冬的荒野步入屋舍。那些紧紧裹住的猎物，说明巢穴结成未久：鹿、狗，还有不见动静的人形茧囊，全都严严实实地悬在层层白网之间，像散落在苍白地毯上的食屑。一道黑影从这座披着薄纱的居所后缓缓走出，屈起的长腿挡在身前，头颅伏在其后，仿佛这丑恶的东西被自己的步足关进了栅栏。一只人手在它口器间一进一出，活像一枚骇人的奶嘴。你们找对地方了。 | 巨蛛巢穴一片死寂，战团到来时的响动却显得格格不入。金属叮当碰撞，在这不该有人踏足的地方，分外刺耳。

你发现一个男人倒吊在树上，全身裹在茧里，只有脸露在外头，也被蛛丝拉扯得变了形。他求你割开粘住眼皮的蛛网，你照做了。他慢慢合上眼睑，干涸的眼睛带着结痂的脆响闭起，或许是几天来头一次。可下一瞬，双眼猛然睁开，男人尖叫起来。他腰间的茧囊鼓胀、撕裂，无数细小的黑蜘蛛喷涌而出。蛛群吞食着他，身体剧烈抽搐，含混的惨叫中混着幼蛛窸窣爬动的声音。它们钻满了他的肺，又被他在濒死的痉挛中咳出。你惊骇地后退，却看见树丛四周，又涌出了一大群体形庞大得多的蜘蛛！ | 巢穴很好找：一片没有寒意的冬日景象，白色蛛网成片垂挂，每棵树、每丛灌木、每一寸地方都被覆盖。你率战团拔出武器，径直走入，随即发现那些裹住的尸体。它们腹部爆开，黑成一片，成群幼蛛正吸吮其中的内脏。

抬头望去，周围树枝间亮起猩红的眼睛，整片蛛林仿佛活了过来。巢穴的守卫蹲伏在灌木间，弯曲的长腿与枝条难分彼此。敌人一直藏在眼皮底下。一棵你以为是树的东西突然整个展开，每一根所谓的木枝，竟都是蜘蛛腿，你吓得险些失禁！这只伪装成树的怪物朝战团扑下，口器咔哒作响，磨动着准备撕咬！}

a2cdaa51e1f6a8c4bcf3.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_57.png[/img]{The location is as gruesome as you imagined, an affair with the irreproachable, the acme of profligate putridity. You haven't yet spotted the necromancer so it'd be best if you make your advance most carefully... | %necromancer_location% is right where %employer% said it would be. You find a trail of bones leading the way. Some of them are still ripe with flesh, perhaps half-borne necromantic mistakes that didn't quite make it from death to undeath. Ignoring the horrors, you begin planning your attack... | A place like %necromancer_location% is so overgrown with tall grass, weeds, and blackened trees that it needn't even have a 'keep out' sign. But it does anyway. It comes in the form of a skeletonized puzzle, a horror of bones patched together from all manner of man and beast, glaring from a crucifix to ward off any would-be adventurers. Slugs crawl through its eye sockets and arteries of army ants pulsate along its limbs.

 %randombrother% walks up, a little perturbed at the sight, and asks how you wish to attack. | First you find a rodent, limbs splayed, each little hand or foot nailed with a pin to a wooden board. Then there's the dog, its head replaced by a cat's. You swear the monstrosity moved when you approached, but maybe you're just seeing things. And then... the people. You've no words to describe what's happened to them, but it is a towering wonder of gore, an acme of atrocity.

%randombrother% steps to your side.%SPEECH_ON%Let's put an end to this madman.%SPEECH_OFF%Aye, let's. The question is, how first to attack?}

a2cdaa51e1f6a8c4bcf3.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_57.png[/img]{这里和你想的一样可怖，腐败与堕落到了极致，惨得无以复加。你还没看见亡灵法师，接下来最好步步小心…… | %necromancer_location%就在%employer%说的地方。一路骸骨为你指引方向，有些还带着腐肉，或许是亡灵法术留下的失败之作，没能从死亡彻底跨入不死。你不去理会这些恐怖景象，开始筹划进攻…… | %necromancer_location%这样的地方，长草、杂草和焦黑的树木盘根错节，本来根本不需要再挂一块禁止靠近的牌子。可这里偏偏还是有。那是一副用各种人兽骨骸拼凑的可怕骨架，钉在十字架上，瞪着来路，警告胆敢靠近的冒险者。蛞蝓穿过眼窝，一股股行军蚁沿着四肢涌动，像搏动的血脉。

 %randombrother%走过来，显然也被这景象弄得有些不安，问你准备如何进攻。 | 你先发现一只啮齿动物，四肢摊开，每只小爪都被细钉钉在木板上。再往前，是条狗，脑袋却换成了猫头。你敢发誓，走近时那怪物动了一下，不过也许只是眼花。然后……便是人。你找不到词来形容他们的遭遇，只见血肉堆砌出骇人的奇观，残暴已到了极致。

%randombrother%来到身边。%SPEECH_ON%把这个疯子了结吧。%SPEECH_OFF%好，就这么办。问题是，先从哪里攻进去？}

757ea88b8015792dd644.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_29.png[/img]{The wait is about to kill you when something else appears to do the job: the undead! %objective%'s bells start ringing and the guards rush to action with a sort of unhinted liveliness. You order the %companyname% to prepare for battle. | As you watch a game of cards between the brothers, bells start ringing. You glance at the local monastery as see the sickly shape of an old man tolling his heart out. Guards respond to the ringing with renewed energy. One calls from the gatehouse.%SPEECH_ON%Here they come, to arms, to arms!%SPEECH_OFF% | Just when you think you've joined the townsfolk in standing around and dying a slow death, the front gates open and a scout shoots through on a horse. The exhausted animal collapses and slides across the mud, its rider bailing and rolling free. He gets to his feet and shouts.%SPEECH_ON%The dead are coming! We have to get ready!%SPEECH_OFF% | A man atop one of the watch houses calls out.%SPEECH_ON%Message incoming, watch yer heads!%SPEECH_OFF%You look up to see an arrow arcing across the sky, twisting to come down right into the mud no more than a few feet from you. The lieutenant breaks a scroll off the arrow. His lips purse white the more he reads and he throws the paper aside.%SPEECH_ON%Time to get ready, mercenary, the dead are comin'.%SPEECH_OFF%He turns to his fellow soldiers.%SPEECH_ON%Defenders of %objective%! To arms!%SPEECH_OFF% | One of the guards calls out.%SPEECH_ON%Gates opening, refugees comin'!%SPEECH_OFF%A scattering of children sputter through the lurching doors. One explains that a horde of pale men are coming. The lieutenant stares at you.%SPEECH_ON%You'd best get your men ready, sellsword.%SPEECH_OFF%The undead are heading this way, prepare for battle! | A scout enters %objective% and dismounts from a horse with bloodied legs and a missing tail. The rider's cradling a handless arm and his face has been carved free of an ear and eye. The lieutenant rushes over and the two talk before the scout passes out. Sighing, the lieutenant comes to stand.%SPEECH_ON%The undead are attacking, prepare yourselves! And put that steed out of its misery!%SPEECH_OFF%You nod and order the %companyname% to ready itself for battle. As the sellswords ready themselves, a man with a butcher's garb walks over and hacks the horse to death with a cleaver. The lieutenant claps you on the shoulder.%SPEECH_ON%Hey, at least now we'll have something good to eat if we make it through.%SPEECH_OFF% | You set down next to the lieutenant. He breaks bread.%SPEECH_ON%It's been awfully quiet since you got here.%SPEECH_OFF%Taking a bite, you ask if he's suggesting you're a double-agent for the dead. He laughs.%SPEECH_ON%Can't be too sure these days.%SPEECH_OFF%Just then, a bell tower tolls and guards rush the walls. Yelling and screaming erupt. The undead are attacking!

 The lieutenant throws his helmet on and helps you up.%SPEECH_ON%Time to prove your worth, sellsword.%SPEECH_OFF% | One of the guardsman takes a long-glass wrapped in leather and starts peering through the walls crenelations. His hands begin to shake and the glass wobbles out of the leather strappings and shatters against the stones. He points and screams.%SPEECH_ON%Th-the undead are here! T-to arms! Ring the bells!%SPEECH_OFF%You look over the walls, but don't need a spyglass to see the wave of pale coming your way. You tell the guardsman to calm down, and then rush to get the %companyname% prepared for battle. | A pack of dogs has come to %objective% and are howling to get inside. The hungry townspeople oblige their wish and the second the mutts enter they're set upon with knives and scythes. Despite the butchering, the dogs keep coming, fighting and gnashing to find safety in a slaughterhouse. You look over the walls to see just why they're willing to take the risk: the undead are coming! Shambling, shuffling, trundling over the horizon.

 You whistle at a man standing in a bell tower and point to the sighting. He straightens up so fast his metal cap falls off and clanks down the stone tower. He hurriedly rings the bell, the great bongs silencing the cruel canine commotion below. Man and mongrel stop to look up, a dreary silence settling over them all. Slowly, the din of death, groaning and growling, seeps into the very air. The lieutenant of the guards jumps into the scene, weapon already drawn out.%SPEECH_ON%To arms, men! To arms!%SPEECH_OFF% | One undead corpse shambles outside the wall of %objective%. The guards take turns trying to shoot it with arrows.%SPEECH_ON%Take a look at that, got 'im in the foot!%SPEECH_OFF%Another guard readies his shot.%SPEECH_ON%He's still walking. Aim for the head ya fool.%SPEECH_OFF%This shot lands true and there's a soft -tok- of the arrow piercing into a hollow brainpain. The corpse's balance shifts momentarily, pausing, then continues on as though it just remembered what it set out to do. Another guardsman shakes his head and readies his shot. He closes one eye, then slowly opens it. His hands start to shake and the arrow shaft rattles against the wooden bow.%SPEECH_ON%T-t-to... uh, to arms! Ring the alarms!%SPEECH_OFF%You look over the walls and see a sea of grey surfacing on the horizon, bobbing and trundling. The undead are attacking! | The town is quiet, the soft crackles and pops of a fire filling the muted air. You watch as men burn a rat on a spit and start slicing off chunks to share. Seeing enough, you go up the walls to find the lieutenant of the guards eyeing the horizon with a scope. He lowers it grimly.%SPEECH_ON%Well fark me arseways, they're coming.%SPEECH_OFF%He hands you the glass and you take a look. A throng of fish-eyed, warped-looking undead are shambling toward %objective%. The lieutenant takes his scope back.%SPEECH_ON%Time to earn your pay, sellsword.%SPEECH_OFF% | A woman's shriek draws you to look over your shoulder. You stare just in time to see a man leap off a tower and snap his neck at the length of a rope. The body sways, bumping and twisting against the stonewalls. The lieutenant of the guards angrily purses his lips and spits.%SPEECH_ON%Goddammit, he was supposed to be watching the horizon. %randomname%! Get up there, cut him free, and take his post!%SPEECH_OFF%Another guardsman grunts and does as told, but when he gets atop the guard he stops following any orders. Instead, he starts hysterically calling out.%SPEECH_ON%Sir! Sir! They're coming! All them pale folk, they're comin'!%SPEECH_OFF%The lieutenant yells at his men to prepare for battle, and you yours. The man turns to you with a look of hopefulness.%SPEECH_ON%Whatever they're paying ya, I hope yer worth every crown, sellsword.%SPEECH_OFF% | One of the guards has found a den of rats which is cause for depressingly incredible celebration. As the townsfolk cheer and weep, and the shrill cries of the rodents go into spits and fires, the lieutenant of the guards comes over. He observes the scene with a smile, but it fades when a high-pitched scream breaks the air. Everyone turns to the walls where one of the guards is pointing toward the horizon. Even from where you're standing you can see the whites in his frightened eyes.%SPEECH_ON%The dead are comin'! They're comin' to kill us all! We ain't have enough men!%SPEECH_OFF%The lieutenant tells the man to grow some balls, then quietly turns to you.%SPEECH_ON%Prepare your men, sellsword, and prove you're worth whatever they're paying ya.%SPEECH_OFF% | A guard was caught trying to desert. He's on his knees while the lieutenant of the guards marches back and forth with disappointed appraisal.%SPEECH_ON%We can't spare a man, and you choose to do this to us?%SPEECH_OFF%One of the townsman throws a clop of mud which sails wide, but the intention is clear.%SPEECH_ON%Bury 'im alive! One less mouth to feed!%SPEECH_OFF%Just as the peasants start to get rowdy, the town bell starts bonging. A man atop one of the watchtowers shouts as hard as he can.%SPEECH_ON%They're coming! The undead, they're on the horizon!%SPEECH_OFF%The lieutenant looks down at the deserter.%SPEECH_ON%You want to earn back your honor, do it now. Will you fight?%SPEECH_OFF%The man quickly nods. The lieutenant turns to you, but you put a hand up.%SPEECH_ON%You need not ask the %companyname% such questions.%SPEECH_OFF%}

757ea88b8015792dd644.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_29.png[/img]{漫长的等待几乎要了你的命，正巧，真想要你命的东西出现了：亡灵！%objective%的警钟响起，守卫们忽然迸发出活力，奔向各自的位置。你命令%companyname%准备战斗。 | 你正看着弟兄们打牌，钟声忽然响起。抬眼望向当地修道院，一个病恹恹的老人正使出浑身力气敲钟。守卫们闻声振作，门楼上传来一声呼喊。%SPEECH_ON%它们来了！拿起武器，拿起武器！%SPEECH_OFF% | 你正觉得自己已经和镇民一样，只会站着慢慢等死，正门忽然打开，一名斥候策马冲进。精疲力竭的马倒地，在泥中滑出一段，骑手跳下，翻滚脱身。他站起来大喊。%SPEECH_ON%死人来了！我们得准备迎战！%SPEECH_OFF% | 一座岗楼上的人喊道。%SPEECH_ON%传信箭来了，小心脑袋！%SPEECH_OFF%你抬头，看见一支箭在空中划过弧线，翻转着落下，扎进离你只有几尺的泥地。副官从箭上取下文书。越往下读，他抿紧的嘴唇便越发苍白，最后把纸扔到一旁。%SPEECH_ON%佣兵，该准备了，死人要来了。%SPEECH_OFF%他转向其他士兵。%SPEECH_ON%%objective%的守军！拿起武器！%SPEECH_OFF% | 一名守卫高喊。%SPEECH_ON%开门，难民来了！%SPEECH_OFF%门扇摇晃着打开，几个孩子跌跌撞撞地跑进来。其中一个说，有一大群脸色惨白的人正在赶来。副官盯着你。%SPEECH_ON%佣兵，你最好让手下做好准备。%SPEECH_OFF%亡灵正朝这里来，准备战斗！ | 一名斥候进入%objective%，从四腿染血、尾巴不见了的马上下来。他抱着失去手掌的胳膊，脸上也被剜掉一只耳朵和一只眼睛。副官赶过去，两人说了几句，斥候便昏倒了。副官叹口气，站直身子。%SPEECH_ON%亡灵要进攻了，准备迎战！还有，让那匹马解脱！%SPEECH_OFF%你点头，命令%companyname%备战。佣兵们忙碌起来，一个穿着屠夫衣服的人走到马旁，用砍刀结束了它的性命。副官拍了拍你的肩。%SPEECH_ON%嘿，至少现在有点好吃的了，只要我们能撑过这一关。%SPEECH_OFF% | 你在副官身边坐下，他掰开面包。%SPEECH_ON%自从你来了，这里就安静得出奇。%SPEECH_OFF%你咬了一口，问他是不是暗示你是亡灵派来的双面间谍。他笑了。%SPEECH_ON%这年头，谁说得准呢。%SPEECH_OFF%就在这时，钟楼响起，守卫奔向城墙，喊叫与尖叫此起彼伏。亡灵进攻了！

副官戴上头盔，把你拉起来。%SPEECH_ON%佣兵，证明你本事的时候到了。%SPEECH_OFF% | 一名守卫拿起包着皮革的长筒望镜，从城墙垛口向外张望。他的双手开始发抖，镜筒晃出皮带，摔在石头上，碎了。他伸手指着前方，尖叫起来。%SPEECH_ON%亡、亡灵来了！拿、拿起武器！敲钟！%SPEECH_OFF%你越过城墙看去，根本用不着望镜，就能看见涌来的惨白浪潮。你叫守卫冷静，随后赶紧召集%companyname%，准备迎战。 | 一群狗来到%objective%，嗥叫着要进城。饥肠辘辘的镇民满足了它们的愿望，可杂毛狗刚进来，刀子和镰刀便迎了上去。尽管遭到屠杀，狗仍不断涌入，撕咬争抢，竟想在屠宰场里寻得安全。你望向城外，终于明白它们为何愿意冒险：亡灵来了！它们踉跄、拖行、蹒跚着，漫过地平线。

你朝钟楼上的人吹响口哨，指向远方。他猛地挺直身子，动作太急，铁帽都掉了下来，沿石塔叮当坠落。他赶紧敲钟，洪亮的钟声压住了下面虐杀犬群的喧嚣。人和狗都停下动作，抬头望去，一片阴沉的寂静笼罩下来。渐渐地，死亡的呻吟与低吼渗入空气。守卫副官冲进人群，武器已经出鞘。%SPEECH_ON%弟兄们，拿起武器！拿起武器！%SPEECH_OFF% | 一具行尸在%objective%的城墙外蹒跚。守卫们轮流放箭，拿它练手。%SPEECH_ON%看见没有，射中脚了！%SPEECH_OFF%另一名守卫搭箭准备。%SPEECH_ON%它还在走。瞄脑袋，笨蛋。%SPEECH_OFF%这一箭正中目标，箭头刺入空荡的脑壳，发出轻轻一声“笃”。尸体晃了一下，停了片刻，又继续前行，仿佛刚想起自己本来要做什么。又一名守卫摇着头，准备射击。他闭起一只眼，随后慢慢睁开。双手开始颤抖，箭杆在木弓上磕得直响。%SPEECH_ON%拿、拿、拿……呃，拿起武器！拉警报！%SPEECH_OFF%你越过城墙，看见地平线上浮出一片灰色的海洋，起伏着，蹒跚而来。亡灵进攻了！ | 镇上一片寂静，只有火堆轻微的噼啪声填着沉闷的空气。几个人正把老鼠架在火上烤，随后切成小块分食。你看够了，便登上城墙，发现守卫副官正用望镜观察地平线。他神情阴沉地放下镜筒。%SPEECH_ON%真他妈操蛋，它们来了。%SPEECH_OFF%他把望镜递来，你举起一看，一大群瞪着死鱼眼、形体扭曲的亡灵，正向%objective%蹒跚而来。副官收回望镜。%SPEECH_ON%佣兵，该挣你的工钱了。%SPEECH_OFF% | 一个女人的尖叫让你回头。你恰好看见一名男子从塔上跃下，绳索骤然绷紧，拗断了他的脖子。尸体摇摆着，撞在石墙上，慢慢扭转。守卫副官愤怒地抿紧嘴，啐了一口。%SPEECH_ON%该死，他本该盯着远处！%randomname%！上去，把他割下来，接替他的岗位！%SPEECH_OFF%另一名守卫应了一声，照做了。可一登上岗楼，他便顾不上命令，开始歇斯底里地呼喊。%SPEECH_ON%长官！长官！它们来了！那些惨白的家伙，全来了！%SPEECH_OFF%副官大喊着命令士兵准备战斗，你也向自己的弟兄下令。他转向你，眼里带着希冀。%SPEECH_ON%佣兵，不管他们付了你多少，但愿每一枚克朗都花得值。%SPEECH_OFF% | 一名守卫发现了一窝老鼠，竟引来一场热烈得令人心酸的庆祝。镇民们又笑又哭，啮齿动物尖叫着被串上烤叉，送向火焰。守卫副官走了过来，微笑着看着这一幕，可一声尖叫划破空气，他的笑容顿时消失。所有人转向城墙，一名守卫正指着地平线。即使隔着这么远，你也能看见他惊恐瞪出的眼白。%SPEECH_ON%死人来了！它们要来杀光我们！我们人手不够！%SPEECH_OFF%副官叫那人拿出点胆量，随后低声对你说道。%SPEECH_ON%佣兵，让手下做好准备。证明给我看，不管他们付了你多少，都没白花。%SPEECH_OFF% | 一名守卫企图逃跑，被抓了回来。他跪在地上，副官在面前来回踱步，满眼失望。%SPEECH_ON%我们一个人都少不得，你却偏要这样对我们？%SPEECH_OFF%一个镇民掷来一块泥巴，虽没砸中，意思却很明白。%SPEECH_ON%活埋了他！少一张吃饭的嘴！%SPEECH_OFF%农民们正要闹起来，镇上的钟忽然响了。岗楼上的人拼命高喊。%SPEECH_ON%它们来了！亡灵，就在地平线上！%SPEECH_OFF%副官低头看向逃兵。%SPEECH_ON%想把荣誉挣回来，就趁现在。你肯打吗？%SPEECH_OFF%那人连忙点头。副官转向你，你却抬起一只手。%SPEECH_ON%这种问题，用不着问%companyname%。%SPEECH_OFF%}

ccab63c2d09ea779ab2f.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_83.png[/img]{For being such small gits, the goblins sure know how to put up a good fight! Your employer, %employer%, shall be pleased with the work you've accomplished here today. | You've heard people scoff at the size of the goblins. Well, they may have been small but they gave it their all.

Take count of your men and prepare a return to your employer, %employer%, for your payday. | The gobbos fought like starving mutts. Starving, crafty, murderous mutts. Unfortunate that their savviness couldn't be put to better use. Ah well, %employer% will appreciate the news of what was done here. | You're not sure if it was a good thing your employer, %employer%, wasn't entirely sure if there were goblins afoot. Had he known, would he have paid you less? The goblins sure seem ineffectual when you look at them, but goddam do they know how to put up a fight.

 Regardless, it's time to take account of your company and return to your employer. | The goblins lay dead. What a nuisance. Your employer, %employer%, should be pleased with what you've done here today. | A stack of dead goblins is still not tall enough to reach the overwhelming height of an orcish berserker. And yet... they put up just as good of a fight! A shame their efforts are wasted in such tiny bodies. Then again, if their wits and craftiness were fitted to an orc's body... by the old gods, it is a scary thought!}

ccab63c2d09ea779ab2f.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_83.png[/img]{地精个头虽小，打起仗来可真不含糊！雇主%employer%想必会对你们今天的战绩十分满意。 | 你听过有人嘲笑地精的个头。它们确实小，却打得拼命。

清点弟兄们，准备回去见雇主%employer%，领报酬吧。 | 那些地精崽子打起仗来，像一群饿疯的野狗。饥饿、狡诈，而且嗜杀。可惜，这点机灵没能用在更好的地方。罢了，%employer%听见这里的消息会很高兴。 | 雇主%employer%先前并不确定，作乱的是不是地精，你也不知这是好事还是坏事。他若知道，会不会反而少付点钱？地精看起来确实没什么威胁，打起来却他妈的难缠。

 无论如何，该清点战团，返回雇主那里了。 | 地精都死了。这些家伙真够烦人的。雇主%employer%应该会对你们今天的战绩很满意。 | 一堆地精尸体垒起来，仍够不上兽人狂战士那骇人的身高。然而……它们打起仗来却丝毫不差！可惜，一身本事困在了这么小的躯壳里。话又说回来，要是把它们的机智狡诈装进兽人的身躯……旧神在上，想想都吓人！}

4c7609e767e9c8dbbe6d.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_59.png[/img]{The %location% is full of people, alright, but they aren't brigands. Refugees clutter the place like moving trash looking for somewhere to rest. The disgusting men and women and even children walk meekly around the premise, altogether too weak to pay mind to the mercenary band before them. %randombrother% comes to your side and asks what should be done.

 If they are left to stay, %employer% won't be very happy and you'll probably not be seeing any pay. On the other hand... just look at the miserable lot. They deserve a rest from whatever troubles drove them here. | You take the spyglass from your eye and shake your head. The %location% is filled - or perhaps infested - with refugees. Better than brigands, you suppose, but still an issue. %employer% won't be very happy about them, you know that much. On the other hand, the people down there... ragged... looking more bone than flesh... tired... they don't deserve to be put out on the road again, do they? | %randombrother% turns and spits. He's got his fists to his hips and shakes his head.%SPEECH_ON%Goddammit.%SPEECH_OFF%Standing before you and the rest of the company is a motley group of refugees. Twenty, thirty maybe. Mostly men. You figure the rest of the group, the women and the children, are hiding in the hinterlands for now. The tired lot seems too exhausted to really communicate with you. They just exchange glances and the occasional, subservient shrug.

 A brother speaks to one side of you.%SPEECH_ON%We gotta kick them out if we want %employer%'s money...%SPEECH_OFF%But then another brother pipes in from your other side...%SPEECH_ON%Yeah, but look at these people. Can we really send them back out into the world? Let 'em stay, I say.%SPEECH_OFF% | Refugees have taken to the %location%, presumably survivors from some wayward war. They've scoured the area for resources and now seem rather entrenched. You know %employer% won't be happy about their presence - they don't seem particularly local. %randombrother% comes to your side and nods toward the ragged band of tired strangers.%SPEECH_ON%I could take a few men and drive them out, sir. It'd be real easy.%SPEECH_OFF% | There's not a bandit in sight. Instead, you've come to find a large group of refugees has occupied the %location%. A throng of tired souls has taken to the place quite well: they've got a few stewpots cooking over crackling fires and seem rather happy about their new 'home.' But %employer% will not be happy about their being there. Not at all. You don't want to believe it, but the cold truth here is that if you want to get paid these people have got to go.}

4c7609e767e9c8dbbe6d.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_59.png[/img]{%location%里确实挤满了人，可他们不是强盗。难民像四处移动、只求找个角落堆下的垃圾一样塞满这里。肮脏的男人、女人，甚至孩子，都怯怯地在屋舍间走动，虚弱得根本顾不上眼前的佣兵队伍。%randombrother%来到你身旁，问该怎么办。

 要是让他们留下，%employer%肯定不高兴，你多半也拿不到报酬。可另一方面……看看这些可怜人吧。无论什么苦难把他们赶到了这里，他们都该歇一歇了。 | 你放下望远镜，摇了摇头。%location%已经挤满——或许该说被难民占满了。你想，总比强盗好，可依旧是个问题。%employer%不会高兴，这点你很清楚。可再看看下面那些人……衣衫褴褛……瘦得皮包骨头……疲惫不堪……他们不该再次被赶上流亡之路，对吧？ | %randombrother%转头啐了一口，双拳抵腰，摇着脑袋。%SPEECH_ON%他妈的。%SPEECH_OFF%你和战团面前站着一群形容狼狈的难民，二十人，也许三十人，大多是男人。你猜，剩下的女人和孩子，暂时藏在附近的偏僻地方。这些人累得几乎无力交谈，只是交换眼神，偶尔卑顺地耸耸肩。

 一名弟兄在你一侧开口。%SPEECH_ON%想拿%employer%的钱，就得把他们赶出去……%SPEECH_OFF%另一名弟兄却从另一侧插话……%SPEECH_ON%是，可看看这些人。我们真能再把他们赶回那片凶险的世道？要我说，就让他们留下。%SPEECH_OFF% | 难民占据了%location%，想来是某场祸乱战争的幸存者。他们已搜遍附近的资源，如今似乎打定主意扎根下来。你知道，%employer%不会乐意见到他们——这些人显然不像本地居民。%randombrother%来到你身旁，朝那群衣衫褴褛、疲惫不堪的陌生人点了点头。%SPEECH_ON%团长，我带几个人就能把他们赶走，轻而易举。%SPEECH_OFF% | 这里看不见一个强盗。相反，你发现大批难民占据了%location%。这些疲惫的人似乎已经安顿得不错：几口炖锅架在噼啪作响的火上，他们对新“家”显得颇为满意。可%employer%不会喜欢他们待在这里，一点也不会。你不愿相信，可冰冷的事实就是：想拿钱，这些人就必须走。}

3cfa8e6df11eaedb4f1e.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_60.png[/img]{You stumble across a corpse in the grass. Ordinarily, the dead aren't that much of a surprise, there are people everywhere so it's only a matter of time until you see a body here and there. Except this one has huge gash marks down the back and its organs missing.

%helpfulbrother% walks up.%SPEECH_ON%The organs are gone cause of wolves, or maybe even rabbits. What, you ain't ever heard of a really hungry rabbit?%SPEECH_OFF%He spits and chews on a fingernail.%SPEECH_ON%Anyhow, the markings, that ain't the work of no rabbit or hound or whatever. That's something... bigger... more dangerous.%SPEECH_OFF%You thank the man for his astute observations and tell him to rejoin the ranks. | A peasant comes up to you with his clothes in shredded rags about him. With fair modesty, he's got his hands covering his groin.%SPEECH_ON%Please, sirs, come take a look at this... horror.%SPEECH_OFF%When you question what he's talking about, he throws his hands up, thrusting his hips at you. He turns afoot like a puppet spun about and takes off running, hooting and hollering. A woman walks up to you in the wake of the man's madness. She's got her hands against her bosom.%SPEECH_ON%He's gone mad on account of his brother being torn apart by the beasts.%SPEECH_OFF%You turn to her, half-expecting the lady to rip off her clothes and wobble her shapes in whatever direction she pleases. Instead, she simply stares at you.%SPEECH_ON%I know %townname% has hired some men to take care of these beasts and you certainly look the part of a hired hand. Please, sir, protect us from these evils... and the evils that they spread...%SPEECH_OFF% | You come across an eviscerated cow with half of it cast atop a fenceline and the other half scattered a good distance across the grass, about as far apart as its entrails would allow. An attachment of gore if there ever was one.

A farmer approaches, tipping his hat up out of his eyes.%SPEECH_ON%Beasts done that. I didn't see them, if you was wondering, but I did hear this goatfark of a fiasco before you. Hearing it was good enough for me to stay low and out of sight. Please, if you are here to find those creatures, do so quickly because I can't afford to lose anymore livestock like this.%SPEECH_OFF% | A peasant hacking firewood straightens up before you.%SPEECH_ON%By the gods it is nice to see ya, sirs. I thought I heard word of some sellswords stomping about looking for the beasts terrorizing these parts.%SPEECH_OFF%You ask if he's seen anything that might help. He pitches his hands over the pommel of his axe.%SPEECH_ON%Can't say I have, no. But I've heard some things. I know a man and woman not far from here got taken. Well, they disappeared together. Word has it they dead in the woods now. Barnacled up in the trees, hanging loosely by the gut, ya know? Or, wait, maybe they just gone off on their feetsies to shack up together! Hell... hell! That gal hated her father and the kid was just a nobody with a flair of good looks and a charming tongue. Yeah, that makes sense.%SPEECH_OFF%He pauses and then glances at you.%SPEECH_ON%Anyhow, I'm certain those monsters are afoot. Keep an eye out, sellsword.%SPEECH_OFF% | A woman runs out of her hut to stop you. Almost out of breath, she asks if you've seen a boy. You shake your head no. She puts her hand out.%SPEECH_ON%He's about yeigh big. Mop of brown hair. Not naturally, but the kid sure likes his mud. When he smiles his teeth are like the stars, bright and scattered.%SPEECH_OFF%You shake your head no a second time.%SPEECH_ON%He can throw a good rock. Throws it far. I told him to not show his strength when the lord's men were 'round, lest they take him into the army.%SPEECH_OFF%She huffs, blowing a loose strand of hair out of her eyes.%SPEECH_ON%Well shite, anyway, if you see him, let me know. I think he's mine. Also, beware the dark. Beasts be bushwhacking folks around here.%SPEECH_OFF%Before you can say anything, the woman picks up her long clothes and trundles back to her hut. | You come across a man kneeling over a thoroughly destroyed dog. You take a knee next to him.%SPEECH_ON%Did the beasts do this?%SPEECH_OFF%He shakes his head no.%SPEECH_ON%Hell, I did this. Finally. Damned thing ain't gonna keep me up anymore.%SPEECH_OFF%Just then, a hut across the way opens up and a man sprints out of it screaming.%SPEECH_ON%Is that my damned dog you sonuvabitch?%SPEECH_OFF%The dogkiller quickly stands up.%SPEECH_ON%The beasts! They visited again last night!%SPEECH_OFF%You quietly leave the dispute where the dog lies.}

3cfa8e6df11eaedb4f1e.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_60.png[/img]{你在草丛里发现了一具尸体。死人本不稀奇，毕竟到处都是活人，早晚会在这里或那里撞见一具尸首。但这一具的后背有几道巨大的撕裂伤，内脏也不见了。

%helpfulbrother%走过来。%SPEECH_ON%内脏没了，是狼吃的，也可能是兔子。怎么，你没听说过饿急眼的兔子？%SPEECH_OFF%他啐了一口，啃起指甲。%SPEECH_ON%不过那些伤痕，可不是兔子、猎犬之类能弄出来的。那东西……更大……也更危险。%SPEECH_OFF%你谢过他敏锐的观察，叫他回到队伍里去。 | 一个农民走到你面前，衣服已经碎成布条挂在身上，倒还知道用双手遮住下身。%SPEECH_ON%求求您，老爷们，来看看这个……可怕的东西。%SPEECH_OFF%你问他在说什么，他却举起双手，朝你挺出胯部。随后，他像被人拧转的木偶一样原地一旋，边喊边叫地跑开了。他疯闹着离开后，一个女人走上前来，双手紧贴着胸口。%SPEECH_ON%他弟弟被野兽撕碎了，他就此发了疯。%SPEECH_OFF%你转身看她，心里已有几分准备，以为她也会扯掉衣服，随心所欲地晃动身子。可她只是望着你。%SPEECH_ON%我知道%townname%雇了人对付那些野兽，而您看着确实像个受雇来的战士。求您了，老爷，保护我们，别再让这些邪物害人……也别再让它们带来的灾祸蔓延下去……%SPEECH_OFF% | 你遇到一头被开膛破肚的牛。半截身子挂在篱笆上，另半截散落在远处的草地里，中间连着的肠子几乎绷到了尽头。若要说什么叫血肉相连，眼前就是活生生的例子。

一个农夫走近，把遮住眼睛的帽檐往上抬了抬。%SPEECH_ON%野兽干的。您要问，我没看见，不过眼前这场狗娘养的惨事，我可听得一清二楚。光那动静，就够让我趴着躲好，不敢露头了。求您，要是您是来找那些东西的，赶紧动手吧。我可经不起再这么损失牲畜了。%SPEECH_OFF% | 一个正在劈柴的农民见到你，直起身来。%SPEECH_ON%诸神在上，见到各位可太好了，老爷们。我好像听人说，有些佣兵正在这附近搜寻祸害人的野兽。%SPEECH_OFF%你问他有没有见到什么有用的线索。他把双手搭在斧柄末端。%SPEECH_ON%没见到什么，真没有。不过倒听说过些事。离这儿不远，有一男一女被掳走了。嗯，就是一起失踪了。人家说他们已经死在林子里了，挂在树上，像攀在船底的藤壶，靠着肠子晃晃悠悠，您懂吧？不，等等，也许他们只是自个儿跑出去，找地方同居了！见鬼……见鬼！那姑娘恨透了她爹，那小子又是个一无所有的家伙，就靠一张好脸和一张甜嘴。对，这就说得通了。%SPEECH_OFF%他停了停，又看向你。%SPEECH_ON%总之，我敢肯定外头有怪物。多留神，佣兵。%SPEECH_OFF% | 一个女人从小屋里跑出来，拦住你。她几乎喘不过气，问你有没有看见一个男孩。你摇头。她伸手比划。%SPEECH_ON%他大概这么高，一头乱蓬蓬的棕发。倒不是天生那颜色，是这孩子太爱玩泥巴。一笑起来，那牙齿就像星星，又白又稀。%SPEECH_OFF%你再次摇头。%SPEECH_ON%他很会扔石头，扔得老远。我告诉他，领主的人在附近时，可别卖弄力气，免得被拉去当兵。%SPEECH_OFF%她呼了口气，吹开挡住眼睛的一缕散发。%SPEECH_ON%唉，该死。总之，见着他就告诉我一声。我想，那是我家的孩子。还有，天黑了当心点，这附近有野兽埋伏着袭击人。%SPEECH_OFF%没等你开口，她便提起长衣的下摆，匆匆赶回小屋。 | 你遇到一个男人，正跪在一条被打得稀烂的狗身边。你在他身旁单膝蹲下。%SPEECH_ON%野兽干的？%SPEECH_OFF%他摇头。%SPEECH_ON%屁，我干的。总算解决了。这该死的东西再也别想吵得我睡不着。%SPEECH_OFF%就在这时，对面一间小屋的门打开，一个男人冲了出来，扯着嗓子大喊。%SPEECH_ON%那他妈是我的狗吗，你个狗娘养的？%SPEECH_OFF%杀狗的人连忙站起来。%SPEECH_ON%野兽！昨晚它们又来了！%SPEECH_OFF%你悄悄离开，任那两人围着死狗争吵。}

80b3c998a15caca4e3d7.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_162.png[/img]{You enter %employer%'s place to find him standing over a fancy rug littered with human body parts. He looks up at you.%SPEECH_ON%These were beast slayers, allegedly, and now here they are, recovered from the task at which they were directed.%SPEECH_OFF%The Vizier nods and a few helpers come over and roll up the rug. Flesh and guts flop and squeeze together and gush out the sides. The servants tilt the rug up, throw it onto their shoulders and march it out, with one dismembered hand flopping lazily from one end. %employer% claps his hands.%SPEECH_ON%In the desert lives my problem, a collection of cruel beasts that are harvesting the locals. I've stared into the Eternal Fires and found guidance to seek a Crownling to help resolve this monstrous issue. Do you, Crownling, find %reward% crowns a suitable allotment to purchase your temporary allegiance?%SPEECH_OFF% | You walk into %employer%'s domicile, but a veritable wall of guards stop you from approaching any closer. He stands at the base of a throne with a short staircase descending from it. He walks down it with deliberation at every step, coming to the landing. A man looks back at him, and the Vizier nods. The man looks back at you and hands you a scroll. It reads that creatures of an undetermined sort are wreaking havoc within the protectorate of %townname%. If you find and destroy said monsters you are to be rewarded in a manner suitable to the task, %reward% crowns. | %employer% is found surrounded by a harem of half-naked women. He is holding up a severed hand which, surprisingly, the women seem more fascinated with than disgusted. As he sees you, the Vizier drops the hand and wipes his hand on the shoulder of one of the women, this time garnering a fair bit of disdain, albeit slavenly muted.

%employer% snaps his fingers at a servant who rushes over with a jar of wine. The Vizier sighs and shoos the servant away and snaps his fingers once more. A second servant realizes he's been called and comes forward, hurriedly handing you a scroll and speaks its words aloud: monsters have been spotted near %townname% and they are to be destroyed posthaste.

 The reward for this is not spoken quite so loudly. Instead, the servant taps the page where a number has been written: %reward% crowns. | %employer% is standing over a map so enormous that it cannot fit on any table, but is instead parceled out and spread across the marbled floor. It seems unnecessary, as a map could be easily contained in proper resolution, but you keep this observation to yourself. The Vizier walks over the paper and points at a location.%SPEECH_ON%Beasts have set upon this part of the realm and are seeing to its destruction in a manner that I have not agreed to. I've more important matters to attend to there.%SPEECH_OFF%He points to another area of the map which just looks like a bunch of empty desert. He continues.%SPEECH_ON%So I need a man such as yourself, Crownling, to see these roaming monsters. Particular to your success, you will be rewarded %reward% crowns which should be more than suitable.%SPEECH_OFF%}

80b3c998a15caca4e3d7.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_162.png[/img]{你走进%employer%的住处，发现他正站在一张华贵地毯旁，上面满是人体残肢。他抬头看你。%SPEECH_ON%这些人，据说是猎兽者。如今，他们执行差事后能带回来的，就都在这里了。%SPEECH_OFF%维齐尔点点头，几个帮手上来卷起地毯。血肉和内脏挤作一团，从两侧淌出。仆人把毯子竖起，扛上肩头运走，一只断手从末端垂下，随着步子懒懒摇晃。%employer%拍了拍手。%SPEECH_ON%我的麻烦就在沙漠里，一群凶残的野兽正在收割当地人的性命。我凝望永恒之火，得到指引，要找一名克朗客解决这桩怪物之患。克朗客，你觉得%reward%克朗，够不够买下你暂时的效忠？%SPEECH_OFF% | 你走进%employer%的居所，一道人墙般的卫兵拦住去路，不许再靠近。他站在宝座前，下方连着一段短阶梯。他一步一步缓缓走下，来到阶前。一个男人回头望他，得到维齐尔的点头示意，便转向你，递来一卷文书。上面写着，不明种类的怪物正在%townname%的辖地内肆虐。若你能找到并消灭它们，就可得到与差事相称的报酬：%reward%克朗。 | %employer%被一群半裸的姬妾围着，正举起一只断手。奇怪的是，那些女人似乎更多是好奇，而非恶心。看见你，维齐尔便扔下断手，在一名女人肩上擦了擦自己的手。这回倒招来不少嫌恶，只是碍于奴仆身份，她们不敢表露。

%employer%朝仆人打了个响指，一个人抱着酒罐赶来。维齐尔叹气，将他挥退，又打了个响指。另一个仆人这才意识到是在叫自己，连忙上前把文书塞给你，并高声宣读：%townname%附近发现怪物，须立即予以剿灭。

至于报酬，他就没念得那么响，只用手指点了点纸上写着的数字：%reward%克朗。 | %employer%站在一幅巨大的地图上。地图大得任何桌子都放不下，只好拆成数块，铺满大理石地面。只要比例合适，本可以画得小些，这排场实在多余，不过你把这想法留在心里。维齐尔踩着纸，指向一处。%SPEECH_ON%野兽袭扰了这片领地，正在用我不曾准许的方式破坏它。我还有更重要的事情要在那边处理。%SPEECH_OFF%他指向地图另一处，看着无非是一片空旷的沙漠，随后继续说道。%SPEECH_ON%所以，我需要你这样的人，克朗客，去处置那些游荡的怪物。事成之后，奖赏你%reward%克朗，应该绰绰有余了。%SPEECH_OFF%}

145e8f78d1aa807785a4.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_162.png[/img]{%employer% is welcomes you into his throne room. It is filled to the brim with what look like very important people, yet you are brought in anyway. Pausing briefly because you're not sure if the crowd can take it, you shrug and then spill out the nachzehrers' remains. The froth of blood and guts and heads puddles across the floor, but not a peep comes from the onlookers.

All you can hear is the soft steps of the Vizier walking over. He stares at the remains, hands clasped before him like some scientist, then he snaps his fingers and a horde of servants come over and clean up the mess. One man with a quill pen and papers makes notations. When all is said and done the Vizier returns to this throne and sits in silence. The only other sound you hear is the chinky-chank of a treasure chest being dragged over. All %reward% crowns are handed to you as promised, then you are quietly urged to leave the room.

 Looking back, you see the crowd return their attention to the Vizier who starts into prayers. | A man stops you outside %employer%'s room. He has with him a few scrawny men with quill pens and ledgers. They descend upon your collection of nachzehrers and make attributions accordingly to their papers. Each one finishes and tears the page away and hands it to the first man who compares his notes. Satisfied, he hands you a purse of %reward% crowns.%SPEECH_ON%May your road be ever gilded, Crownling.%SPEECH_OFF%}

145e8f78d1aa807785a4.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_162.png[/img]{%employer%准你进入他的觐见厅。厅里挤满了看似身居高位的人，你却仍被带了进去。你迟疑片刻，不知道这些人受不受得了，随即耸肩，将食尸鬼的残骸全倒了出来。鲜血、内脏和头颅在地板上摊成一滩，旁观者却连一声都没出。

你只听见维齐尔走近的轻微脚步声。他双手交握在身前，像个学者似的端详那些残骸，随后打了个响指，一群仆人赶来收拾狼藉。旁边有人拿着羽毛笔和纸，逐一记录。一切收拾妥当后，维齐尔回到宝座，默默坐下。厅里只剩下一只钱箱拖过来的叮当声。说好的%reward%克朗分文不少地交到你手里，接着有人低声催你离开。

你回头时，看见众人重新将目光投向维齐尔，而他已开始祈祷。 | 一个人在%employer%的房间外拦下你，身旁跟着几个瘦削的男人，各持羽毛笔和账册。他们围住你带回的食尸鬼，逐一辨认，在纸上记下。每人写完便撕下纸页，交给领头的那人对照核查。他满意地点头，递给你装着%reward%克朗的钱袋。%SPEECH_ON%愿你前路永镀金光，克朗客。%SPEECH_OFF%}

404d683f96ec273eff2d.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_46.png[/img]{The evil in the place has been extinguished. You take a breath that feels like the first in years, as though the air itself had warmed to your victory. Only the so-called %objective2% remains now. | As the last of the undead are put to rest, you get a sense that the air is clearing up, like a fog of smoky air giving way to crisp, springtime aromas. The quick change in scents no doubt means you've cleaned whatever evil dwelled there. Now to cleanse %objective2% and be done with this contract. | The evil of the place has been put to rest. Your next target awaits. | With the horrid place cleansed of evil, only %objective2% remains on the contract. | As the last wiederganger is put to rest, you feel a sudden change in the air. Cleanliness punches your lungs with unexpected clarity as you stand in a world of muck and mire. %randombrother% wipes his brow.%SPEECH_ON%Must be the end of it. On our way to %objective2% then?%SPEECH_OFF% | You entered a domain of evil, but with the last wiederganger slain you see the light of the world brighten and the smell of the earth beneath your feet returns to the natural order. With this place laid to rest, it's time to go on to %objective2%. | The victory was hard fought. Wiedergangers and the oddities of more ancient undead litter the field. You hope %objective2% will be easier to sort out, but you doubt it. | You step over the corpse of an ancient deadman. It's so different from yourself that it may as well be alien to all life you know of. The skull is ill-shaped, like a shrunken precursor to your own, and the armor and weapons appear out of this world.

 You prepare the men for the journey to %objective2%. | The earth is strewn with the ruinous corpses of the undead. You step over their bodies to find the ground beneath you returning to health, as if the soil was turning over from hiding, and the air itself is easier to breathe. Perhaps the evil truly has left the place? Regardless, it is time to go on to %objective2% and give it the friendly %companyname% treatment. | With the last of the undead slain, you look about the field. The dead are not of one source, judging by their variety of clothes and armors, but they are not of one timeline either. Some wear the armors of ancients and carry with them disturbing uniformity in their effort to kill.

 %randombrother% comes by, stating that the company is ready to move onto this %objective2% whenever you are.}

404d683f96ec273eff2d.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_46.png[/img]{这里的邪恶已经消灭。你深吸一口气，仿佛多年来第一次痛快呼吸，连空气也因胜利而暖了起来。现在，只剩那个叫%objective2%的地方了。 | 最后一个亡灵终于安息，你感觉空气也清新起来，仿佛烟霭散去，让位于春日的清爽气息。气味转变得如此迅速，无疑说明盘踞在这里的邪恶已经被你清除。现在去净化%objective2%，完成这份委托。 | 这里的邪恶已经安息。下一个目标还在等着你。 | 这片恐怖之地的邪恶已被清除，委托上只剩%objective2%了。 | 最后一具行尸倒下时，你忽然察觉空气变了。尽管四周尽是污泥烂沼，一股出乎意料的清新仍直沁肺腑。%randombrother%擦了擦额头。%SPEECH_ON%看来这里结束了。接着去%objective2%？%SPEECH_OFF% | 你们进入时，这里还是邪恶的领地。可随着最后一具行尸被斩杀，天光似乎更明亮了，脚下泥土的气息也恢复了自然。这里既已安息，就该继续前往%objective2%。 | 这一仗赢得不易。行尸和更加古老、怪异的亡灵横陈遍野。你希望%objective2%会好对付些，却又不太敢信。 | 你跨过一具远古死者的尸体。它与你迥然不同，仿佛根本不属于你所知的任何生命。头骨形状怪异，像是你的头颅缩小后的古老雏形，铠甲和武器也宛如来自另一个世界。

 你让弟兄们准备启程，前往%objective2%。 | 地上满是亡灵残破的尸体。你跨过它们，发现脚下的大地正在恢复生机，仿佛泥土从藏身处翻了出来，连空气都更容易呼吸了。也许，邪恶真的离开了这里？无论如何，该去%objective2%，让那里也享受一下%companyname%的“友善招待”了。 | 最后一个亡灵被斩杀后，你环顾战场。从各式衣甲来看，这些死者来自不同的地方，甚至不同的年代。有些身披远古铠甲，杀起人来却动作整齐得令人不安。

 %randombrother%走来报告，战团已经准备妥当，随时可以奉命前往%objective2%。}

9a4f36ddbacf286f39a8.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_46.png[/img]{%objective2% is in ruins, though from your perspective it's looking better than ever. It's probably best to head on back to %employer% now and get your reward. | You gave %objective2% a righteous corrective measure, swinging it out of the grips of the undead and back into the world of the living. Already, you see the grass and trees grow livelier, and a breeze comes with refreshing briskness. %employer% would be best told of these doings so you can go on and get your payday. | The darkness that resided within %objective2% has been destroyed. Well, except for those pockets of existence beneath the rubble. Still got a little bit of darkness there, but that's more because of the lack of light than the presence of evil. Either way, you should go and tell %employer% of what you've done. | %objective2% looks a lot better with the %companyname% standing victoriously over its ruins. The way you see it, a painter should go and do a little getup of your achievement. %randombrother% looks especially good crushing wiederganger skulls with his boots. Getting paid by %employer%, however, would look even better. Probably best to get back to him. | %objective2% is destroyed and with it the evil has departed these lands. Hopefully it is gone for good, but there's a good chance it has simply gone to another place of weakness. Speaking of which, you'd best get back to %employer% for your pay. | %objective2% has been laid flat and all the evil that inhabited it has gone. The air is lighter, more fresh. %employer% should be happy to see you and the results you've to report. | The %companyname% stands victorious, the evils of %objective2% laid to rest, or perhaps driven out to inhabit some other place. A cynical part of you hope it's the latter, because in that case some other nobleman will want you to root it out and you'll earn yourself another payday. As thoughts of an evil-driving circle-scam fill your head, %randombrother% comes up and asks if it's time to return to %employer%. You nod. One step at a time. | %objective2% and all its grim, cruel inhabitants have been put to the blade. It's strange seeing a battlefield littered with dead that range from the freshness of a wiederganger's corpse, to the dusty armor shell of an ancient. The corpses carry more diversity than an antique shop.

 Once the company has its fill of loot, it should get on back to %employer% for your pay. | Dead wiedergangers and ancients are strewn across the ground. Dead-undead, a strange verbiage to account for the slaying of evil beyond your measure. But slain they are, proving that the monsters can be stopped. You ready the company to make a return to %employer% for a right proper payday. | %objective2% is destroyed, proving that even the reanimated dead cannot avoid the thorough destruction the %companyname% brings to the battlefield. With the evil cleared out, you get a sense of civility and nature returning to the place. The air hits your nose with welcomed briskness. Overhead, birds are zipping across the sky. Little ones, too, not just buzzards looking for a meal.

 You tell the company to loot what they can and get ready for a return to %employer%.}

9a4f36ddbacf286f39a8.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_46.png[/img]{%objective2%已成废墟，不过在你看来，它比以往任何时候都顺眼。现在最好回去见%employer%，领取报酬。 | 你给%objective2%来了一次正义的整治，把它从亡灵手中夺回，重新送回生者的世界。草木已经显出活力，微风也带来清爽的气息。最好把这些成果告诉%employer%，然后把钱领了。 | 盘踞%objective2%的黑暗已被消灭。嗯，废墟底下的角落除外。那里还残留一点黑暗，不过主要是因为没有光，而不是还有邪恶。无论如何，该去告诉%employer%，你们做成了什么。 | %companyname%胜利地站在废墟之上，让%objective2%看起来顺眼多了。在你看来，该请个画师，把这番功绩画下来。尤其是%randombrother%用靴子碾碎行尸头骨的样子，格外上相。不过，从%employer%手里领钱的景象，还要更好看些。还是赶紧回去吧。 | %objective2%已被摧毁，邪恶也随之离开这片土地。希望它永不再来，不过更可能只是转移到了另一个薄弱之处。说到这个，你最好回去找%employer%领钱。 | %objective2%已经夷为平地，盘踞其中的邪恶尽数散去。空气更轻盈，也更清新。见到你，听到你带回的成果，%employer%应该会很高兴。 | %companyname%赢得胜利，%objective2%的邪恶已经安息，或者只是被赶去别处栖身。你心里那点愤世嫉俗的念头，倒希望是后者。这样，又会有另一个贵族请你去清除它，你便能再挣一笔。脑海里正盘算着这套把邪恶赶来赶去、循环收钱的把戏，%randombrother%走来，问是否该回去见%employer%了。你点头。一步一步来。 | %objective2%及其中所有阴森残酷的居民，都已被刀剑扫荡。战场上横陈的死者，从尚且新鲜的行尸，到只剩积灰甲壳的远古亡灵，应有尽有。这景象真怪，尸体的种类比古董铺里的货还丰富。

 等战团搜刮够了，就该回去找%employer%领钱。 | 倒下的行尸与远古亡灵遍布地面。死掉的亡灵——用这种古怪的说法，来描述斩杀了超乎理解的邪恶。可它们终究被杀死了，这证明怪物也能被阻止。你让战团准备返回%employer%那里，领取一笔实实在在的报酬。 | %objective2%已被摧毁，证明即使死而复生，也逃不过%companyname%在战场上带来的彻底毁灭。邪恶清除之后，你感觉文明与自然都在重返此地。清爽的空气沁入鼻腔，令人舒畅。飞鸟掠过头顶，其中还有小鸟，不再只是觅食的秃鹫。

 你叫战团尽量搜集战利品，准备返回%employer%那里。}

8c64e2d1809f1d921f27.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_31.png[/img]{You arrive at %commander%'s camp to find his soldiers seemingly relaxed. They're playing dice on a wooden board strewn across the mud, exchanging jokes, and singing songs. All around are banners flying in the wind, most having long lost their once bright colors. A few are tethering the poles of a catapult back together. %commander% himself personally guides you to his command tent. He gives you a drink that tastes like a rat had bathed in it. He explains the situation.%SPEECH_ON%As I'm sure you know, we've been here awhile and are about to make a breakthrough. I need you on hand and at the ready. Once the time to attack comes, I'll give the order to begin the assault.%SPEECH_OFF% | %commander%'s camp has ruined the earth around %objective%. The day-to-day presence of so many men has churned the ground into mud. A few of the men crank the spokes of a shoddy, shaky catapult. They slam a wormy cow's head into the bucket and slacken the rope spring until the pole of the war machine shoots forward, launching a spinning, bleeding black head toward the fortifications. It caroms off a crenelated bastion before rolling a sick stain down the walls. One of the defenders yells back.%SPEECH_ON%Nice shot, ya twats!%SPEECH_OFF%%commander% claps you on the shoulder. He's grinning.%SPEECH_ON%Welcome to the front, sellsword. The presence of you and your men is much appreciated. %objective% is cut off, but they refuse to surrender and remain feisty despite the hunger in their bellies. But that hunger... it weakens them. When the time is right, I will begin an assault, all I need is for you to be ready.%SPEECH_OFF% | %commander% welcomes you to the front. He informs you that the defenders of %objective% are tired, running low on supplies, and are about ready to break. Given these facts, he is preparing a final assault and simply needs the men of the %companyname% to be ready when the time comes. | The siege at %objective% looks more like the recreation in a large play than the efforts of a concentrated war effort. Both sides are in a state of miserable inadequacy, hurling insults back and forth over the walls, and in between quietly cursing the fact they had the poor luck to be stuck in this hellish situation. %commander%, though, comes to you with a cheery spark in his eyes.%SPEECH_ON%Ah, mercenaries. Let me fill you in on what is going on. We have cut off the food supplies to %objective% and a few nights ago one of our agents managed to burn their granary to the ground. They are hungry and soon they will be dying. Because we are so pressed for time, I'm organizing an all-out assault to bring this siege to a quick end. Just be ready when the time comes.%SPEECH_OFF% | You come to %objective% to see the fortifications standing silhouetted against the horizon and %commander% staring through a pair of leather-wrapped ocular lenses, grimacing angrily at what he's glassing. He hands you the device and you take a look.

 The first thing you see is a man's ass bobbing up and down as he pats it with both hands. The soldier beside him is slackjawed and crosseyed as he yanks at his bits. You put the scope down, not bothering to see what else is going on. %commander% shakes his head.%SPEECH_ON%We cut off their food supplies and now they're going crazy. They think they are being funny, but soon we'll see who is laughing. I'm planning an assault. I need you and the men of the %companyname% to be ready when the order comes.%SPEECH_OFF% | %commander% welcomes you to the outskirts of %objective% where his siege camp has been built. Rows of tents are filled with tired and grumbly men. They cook stews out of pots that have never been cleaned, and exchange jokes that were never clean to begin with. In the distance, diligent defenders of %objective% stare over their crenelations. The commander brings you to his tent and explains the situation.%SPEECH_ON%%objective% is out of food and starving. Unfortunately, I'm out of time. We need to assault this damned place soon and I mean real farkin' soon. When the time comes, and it will come sellsword, I need you to be ready.%SPEECH_OFF% | The outskirts of %objective% has become littered with tents. One of %commander%'s bodyguards marches you through the siege city. Grumbly professional soldiers eye you with suspicion. %commander%, however, cheerily welcomes you to his tent. As you step in, you see a man hanging by both hands, his feet dangling off the ground. A second man is cleaning a knife in a bucket of reddened water. %commander% throws his hand toward the prisoner.%SPEECH_ON%Ah, sellsword. You just missed the action.%SPEECH_OFF%You ask what he was doing. The commander walks to the prisoner and cups him by the chin, lifting a tired and exhausted head.%SPEECH_ON%I was getting answers. %objective% is about to fall, but I don't have the time to sit around and wait for that to happen. I will be assaulting the fortifications soon and when I do, I need you and your men at the ready.%SPEECH_OFF% | You come to %commander%'s siege camp to find soldiers loading a net of heads into a catapult and launching it over %objective%'s fortifications. The commander himself comes to your side, soaking in the scene with a wide and satisfied smile.%SPEECH_ON%You know, some of those heads were of our own, but I figured the gits over the walls wouldn't be able to tell the difference. It's not about whose head, but how many, ya know? Come, sellsword.%SPEECH_OFF%He guides you to his command tent and there lays out a map.%SPEECH_ON%The defenders are tired and recent information tells me that they are almost out of food and beginning to fight over scraps. But I do not have the time for them to realize the futility of their situation, I must force it upon them. We are to begin an assault sometime soon. You need to be there when the order comes.%SPEECH_OFF% | As you enter %commander%'s camp, a few of his soldiers spit on one of your men and a brawl quickly breaks out. Thankfully, the commander himself appears to put things at ease. He quickly guides you to his tent and there you talk while your men stand outside.%SPEECH_ON%I must apologize for the actions of my men. Tempers run razor thin after you've been standing and sleeping in mud, day after day, while your enemies sleep in beds and hurl insults over their walls.

Luckily, one of my agents managed to burn down %objective%'s granary and stocks and the fort is without supplies. The defenders have been going hungry, but I fear my men will hardly bother to stand out here for long. I also worry that reinforcements might be coming to try and lift the siege. All of this means one thing... I'm going to order an assault. The plans are currently being drawn, I just need you ready for when the order comes.%SPEECH_OFF%}

8c64e2d1809f1d921f27.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_31.png[/img]{你来到%commander%的营地，发现士兵们似乎挺放松。他们把木板搁在泥地上掷骰子，互相讲笑话，唱着歌。四周旗帜随风飘动，大多早已褪去鲜艳的颜色。几个人正在重新绑紧投石机的木杆。%commander%亲自领你前往指挥帐篷，递来的饮料尝着像有老鼠在里面洗过澡。他说明了局势。%SPEECH_ON%想必你也知道，我们在这里待了一阵子，很快就能打开局面。我要你随时在旁待命。进攻时机一到，我就会下令发起强攻。%SPEECH_OFF% | %commander%的营地把%objective%周围的土地糟蹋得不成样子。这么多人日复一日地踩踏，地面早已成了烂泥。几个士兵转动着一架粗陋而晃荡的投石机，将一颗长虫的牛头砸进投斗，松开蓄力的绳索，投臂猛地甩向前方。黑色牛头旋转着、淌着血，飞向防御工事，撞上带垛口的堡台后弹开，沿墙滚下一道恶心的污痕。一个守军高喊着回敬。%SPEECH_ON%打得真准啊，你们这帮蠢货！%SPEECH_OFF%%commander%笑着拍了拍你的肩。%SPEECH_ON%欢迎来到前线，佣兵。你和弟兄们能来，我们十分感激。%objective%已经被切断补给，可他们就是不投降，肚子饿着，嘴还挺硬。不过，饥饿……会削弱他们。时机一到，我就发动强攻。你只需要做好准备。%SPEECH_OFF% | %commander%欢迎你来到前线。他告诉你，%objective%的守军疲惫不堪，物资即将耗尽，已经快要撑不住了。因此，他正在筹备最后一次强攻，只需要%companyname%的弟兄在时机到来时做好准备。 | %objective%的围城战，看着更像一出大戏里的战争场面，而不像一场真正集中力量展开的战事。双方都被折腾得狼狈不堪，隔着城墙互相叫骂，停下喘气时，又暗自咒骂自己倒霉，竟被困在这种地狱般的处境里。然而，%commander%走向你时，眼里却闪着快活的光。%SPEECH_ON%啊，佣兵。让我说说眼下的情况。我们已经切断%objective%的粮食补给，几夜前，一名密探又成功烧毁了他们的粮仓。他们正在挨饿，很快就会开始死人。可我们时间紧迫，所以我正组织全面强攻，好让围城尽快结束。到时候做好准备就行。%SPEECH_OFF% | 你来到%objective%，看见防御工事的轮廓矗立在天际。%commander%正透过一副皮革包裹的望镜观察，脸上满是恼怒。他把望镜递给你，你举起来一看。

首先映入眼帘的是一个上下晃动的屁股，主人正用双手拍打它。旁边的士兵张着嘴、对着眼，拉扯着自己的下体。你放下望镜，懒得再看还有什么花样。%commander%摇了摇头。%SPEECH_ON%我们断了他们的粮，他们就开始发疯。他们自以为很好笑，可过不了多久，就知道谁笑得出来了。我正在筹备强攻。命令一到，我要你和%companyname%的弟兄立刻投入战斗。%SPEECH_OFF% | %commander%在%objective%外围的围城营地欢迎你。一排排帐篷里，挤满疲惫而牢骚不断的士兵。他们用从未洗过的锅煮炖食，交换着从一开始就不干净的笑话。远处，%objective%的守军尽职地从垛口后监视着。指挥官把你带进帐篷，说明局势。%SPEECH_ON%%objective%已经断粮，正在挨饿。可惜，我也没时间了。我们必须尽快攻下这个鬼地方，我是说，真他妈越快越好。佣兵，进攻的时候一定会到。到那时，我要你准备妥当。%SPEECH_OFF% | %objective%外围布满帐篷。%commander%的一名亲卫领你穿过这座围城营垒组成的城镇。满腹牢骚的正规军士兵怀疑地打量你，%commander%却兴高采烈地把你迎进帐篷。刚进去，你便看到一个人双手被吊起，脚悬在地面上方。另一个人正把刀浸在一桶泛红的水里清洗。%commander%朝囚犯一挥手。%SPEECH_ON%啊，佣兵，你刚好错过了好戏。%SPEECH_OFF%你问他在做什么。指挥官走到囚犯面前，托住下巴，抬起那颗疲惫不堪的脑袋。%SPEECH_ON%我在问话。%objective%就快陷落了，可我没时间坐着干等。我很快就会强攻工事。到时候，我要你和弟兄们做好准备。%SPEECH_OFF% | 你来到%commander%的围城营地，看见士兵把一网兜人头装进投石机，抛过%objective%的工事。指挥官本人来到你身旁，望着这一幕，露出心满意足的笑容。%SPEECH_ON%你知道吗，其中有些脑袋是我们自己人的。不过我寻思，墙上那帮蠢货也分不清。要紧的不是谁的脑袋，而是有多少，明白吧？来，佣兵。%SPEECH_OFF%他领你进入指挥帐篷，铺开一张地图。%SPEECH_ON%守军已经疲惫不堪。最新情报说，他们快断粮了，开始为一点残羹剩饭打架。但我没时间等他们自己明白已经无路可走，我得逼他们认清现实。强攻很快就会开始。命令一下，你必须在场。%SPEECH_OFF% | 你刚进%commander%的营地，几个士兵便朝你的一个弟兄吐唾沫，斗殴随即爆发。幸好指挥官亲自出现，平息了事态。他很快把你领到帐篷里交谈，弟兄们则留在外面。%SPEECH_ON%我的士兵做出这种事，我必须道歉。天天站在泥里，睡在泥里，而敌人却睡着床，还隔着城墙朝你叫骂，谁的脾气都会变得一点就着。

幸好，我的一名密探烧掉了%objective%的粮仓和库存，要塞已经没了补给。守军正在挨饿，可我怕自己的兵也不肯在外面耗太久了。我还担心会有援军赶来解围。所以，结论只有一个……我要下令强攻。计划正在拟定，你只要在命令到来时准备好。%SPEECH_OFF%}

d4c4407668d3b4534f56.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_31.png[/img]{%objective%'s fort has fallen. You watch as %commander%'s men scrounge about, pulling dead bodies out from the nooks and crannies the frantic living had crawled to in the last of their desperations. Corpses come burnt, beheaded, missing limbs, trailing viscera as they're dragged, and a select few looked as though they'd simply died in their sleep. One of the professional soldiers leans out from a tower's crenelations, tears down the fort's banner, and hoists the %noblefamily% sigil in its place to much cheering. | Dead bodies litter the courtyard and they're folded over the walls like wet clothes and some are in the corners with looks of shock on their faces and you see some blackened shapes wiry and crooked in the ruins of a burnt stable and amongst these dead men are horses and pigs and dogs and even fray feathered birds that all managed to get sucked into the violence which visited this place with unstoppable inertia.

 %commander% is going about his surviving men to congratulate them on a job well done. One of the soldiers hoists the %noblefamily% banner atop one of the towers. The wretched place has new owners. | The assault is over, the defenders of %objective% all cleared out. If anyone of them survived this place, they did so by departing it altogether. %commander% orders one of his men to hoist the sigil of %noblefamily% atop one of the towers and, just like that, ownership of %objective% changes hands, with all the finality of a banner wagging limply in the wind. | It was costly, but the assault has come to an end. %commander% steps over the dead bodies to order his men to start cleaning the place up immediately. One of his men raises the banner of %noblefamily% so that all may see who won the battle this day. | All around you are the bodies of %objective%'s defenders. They fought hard, but history won't remember that. Their names will be forgotten and their existence a futile one. You watch as one of %commander%'s soldiers unfurls their banner over one of the towers so at least that's nice. | A few pockets of fighting remain. You watch as %commander%'s men throw defenders off a nearby tower, sending the poor men screaming to their deaths. When they're all gone, one of the soldiers flies the sigil of %noblefamily%. The banner flaps loudly in the newfound silence. | Healers rush into the fortification to tend to %commander%'s men. A few of %objective%'s defenders are also wounded, but they are left to fend for themselves. Any cry for help is met with a sword. The survivors soon learn no wound, no cry.

 %noblefamily%'s banner is unfurled over the front gate. | %commander%'s men go picking through the remains of %objective%'s courtyard. A woman is found and she is taken into a tower. Young children rush after her, unfettered and howling and yet nobody pays them any mind. %commander% himself congratulates you on the job well done. He points to a soldier unfurling %noblefamily%'s banner over the front gate.%SPEECH_ON%See that sigil? It spells victory.%SPEECH_OFF%You thought mounds of dead enemies provided a powerful lexicon for victory declarations, but a flapping piece of cloth suffices too. | The courtyard is hill-fleshed with dead bodies and there's blood dripping down the surrounding walls. %commander%'s men go around collecting all the weapons they can and finishing off any wounded enemies they find. Their own wounded are tended to by frail, old healers with bags of leaves and mortar and pestle remedies. %noblefamily%'s banner is unfurled over the walls to make sure, in case the evidence wasn't already abundantly clear, that %objective% has new owners. | Citizens from %objective% are made to march through its fortifications, to see its dead defenders, and its utterly defeated defenses. %commander% is standing astride them, thumbs jacked into his belt line with a smug smile on his face. When a soldier unfurls %noblefamily%'s banner, he points to it.%SPEECH_ON%See that? That is who you bow down to now. Understand?%SPEECH_OFF% | You watch as citizens are marched through %objective%'s defenses. %commander% seems interested in making explicitly clear how absolute his victory was and there is no room for further fighting. You can't blame him: defeat fosters a rebellious urgency within a conquered man, an urgency which is often deadlier than the man who takes up a sword and makes his intentions so clear that his enemies have no other way to thank him than immediately cutting him down. | %commander% has the citizens of %objective% lined up and marched through the fortifications. They are made to see the defeat of their defenders, blood still fresh and dripping. A beautiful and lathe woman is in the line and the commander pulls her out. He asks if she knows any of the dead. She points to a man whose face has been caved in. She recognizes the shriveled rose pinned to his uniform - she had given it to her husband that morning. %commander% apologizes for her loss then carefully ushers her back in line. He addresses the crowd with almost fatherly sternness.%SPEECH_ON%You people will be taken care of. We will rebuild and you will be fed. However, make no mistake, %objective% belongs to %noblefamily%. As long as we can agree on that, then all will be well for you.%SPEECH_OFF%}

d4c4407668d3b4534f56.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_31.png[/img]{%objective%的堡垒陷落了。你看着%commander%的士兵四处搜寻，从各处犄角旮旯拖出尸体。那些角落，曾是绝望的人在最后关头拼命爬向的藏身处。尸体有的烧焦，有的断头，有的缺了四肢，拖行时内脏在地上曳出长痕，只有极少数看起来像是睡着后再未醒来。一名正规军士兵从塔楼垛口探出身子，扯下堡垒的旗帜，升起%noblefamily%的徽旗，换来阵阵欢呼。 | 尸体铺满庭院，有的像湿衣服般折挂在城墙上，有的缩在角落里，脸上还留着惊恐。烧毁的马厩中，可见几具焦黑、干瘦而扭曲的人形。死人之间还夹着马、猪、狗，甚至羽毛凌乱的鸟。这场暴力以无可阻挡的势头降临，把它们全都卷了进去。

%commander%正在幸存的士兵间走动，祝贺他们干得漂亮。一名士兵在塔顶升起%noblefamily%的旗帜。这个惨不忍睹的地方，有了新主人。 | 进攻结束，%objective%的守军已被肃清。倘若还有谁活下来，那也一定是早已逃出了这里。%commander%命令一名士兵在塔顶升起%noblefamily%的徽旗。就这样，%objective%易了主。一面旗帜在风中无力地摆动，这事便算尘埃落定。 | 代价高昂，但进攻总算结束了。%commander%跨过尸体，命令士兵立刻开始清理。一名手下升起%noblefamily%的旗帜，让所有人都看清，今天是谁赢得了这场战斗。 | %objective%守军的尸体横陈在你四周。他们奋力战斗过，但历史不会记住这些。他们的名字将被遗忘，一生的存在仿佛徒劳无功。你看着%commander%的一名士兵在塔楼上展开旗帜。好吧，至少旗子挂上去了。 | 零星的战斗还在继续。你看见%commander%的士兵把守军从附近的塔楼上扔下去，可怜的人惨叫着坠向死亡。等人全被清理干净，一名士兵扬起%noblefamily%的徽旗。四下刚刚归于寂静，旗帜便猎猎作响。 | 医者们赶进要塞，照料%commander%的士兵。%objective%的守军也有一些伤员，却只能自生自灭。谁开口求救，等来的就是一剑。幸存者很快学会了：有伤也当没伤，有痛也别出声。

%noblefamily%的旗帜在正门上方展开。 | %commander%的士兵在%objective%庭院的残骸中翻找。他们发现一个女人，将她带进塔楼。几个年幼的孩子哭喊着追上去，没人拦他们，也没人理会。%commander%本人则祝贺你干得漂亮。他指着一个正在正门上方展开%noblefamily%旗帜的士兵。%SPEECH_ON%看见那个徽记了吗？它写着“胜利”。%SPEECH_OFF%你原以为，堆积如山的敌军尸体，已经足够把“胜利”二字解释得明明白白。不过，一块飘动的布也行。 | 庭院里的尸体堆成血肉小丘，四周城墙还在滴血。%commander%的士兵四处搜集武器，能拿多少就拿多少，遇到敌方伤员便补上一刀。己方伤员则由年老体弱的医者照看，药袋里的叶片被放进研钵，捣成治伤的药。%noblefamily%的旗帜在城墙上展开，好让所有人都知道——如果眼前的证据还不够充分的话——%objective%已经换了主人。 | %objective%的居民被迫列队走过防御工事，亲眼看看死去的守军，以及彻底崩溃的防线。%commander%昂然站在旁边，拇指插在腰带里，脸上挂着得意的笑。一名士兵展开%noblefamily%的旗帜，他便伸手指去。%SPEECH_ON%看见了吗？从今往后，你们就向它低头。明白吗？%SPEECH_OFF% | 你看着居民们被押着走过%objective%的防线。%commander%似乎想让所有人彻底明白，他赢得有多么干净利落，再战下去毫无余地。你不能怪他：战败会在被征服者心中催生一种急切的反抗欲望，而这往往比正面举剑的人更危险。后者把意图摆得清清楚楚，敌人唯一能做的回应，就是立刻将他砍倒。 | %commander%命令%objective%的居民排成长队，走过防御工事，亲眼见证守军的败亡，血还新鲜，仍在滴落。队伍里有个美丽纤细的女人，指挥官把她拉了出来，问她认不认识这些死者。她指向一个脸被砸塌的人。她认出了他制服上那朵枯萎的玫瑰——那是她今早送给丈夫的。%commander%为她的遭遇表示哀悼，随后小心地把她送回队伍。他用近乎父亲般严厉的口吻，对人群说道。%SPEECH_ON%你们会得到照顾。我们会重建这里，也会让你们吃饱。但有一点必须明白：%objective%如今属于%noblefamily%。只要大家认清这一点，往后的日子就会安稳。%SPEECH_OFF%}

37470368ecbdbbc458ae.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_68.png[/img]{Flushing %objective%'s defenders out worked like a charm. You and the %commander% walk through the now undefended gate to see what's left of the place. Unfortunately, the fires burnt most of the place right to the ground. No matter, one of the professional soldiers hoists a banner of %noblefamily% atop one of the towers. You can hardly recognize the sigil through the cloud of swirling ash and smoke. | The battlefield is littered with the dead and dying. %commander%'s men pass through the mounds of corpses, occasionally stabbing their spears down into the ground and silencing what noise had been mewling there.

 You and the commander head through %objective%'s gate. The fires turned every wooden building to bony and charred frameworks. There are burnt farm animals all over the courtyard. %commander% shrugs and orders one of his men to raise the flag of %noblefamily% atop one of the towers so that all may know who won this day. | The battle is over. Flushing %objective%'s defenders out with fire more than likely saved many lives, but the beyond the gates everything has been cleansed by flames. It will take time to rebuild to its former glory, whatever that was. %commander% seems happy enough as he orders one of his men to raise the flag of %noblefamily% atop one of the towers. Its colorful linens snap crisply amongst shades of floating ash and smoke. | %commander% steps through the ashes of %objective%'s fortifications.%SPEECH_ON%Well, we got it. What's left of it anyway. I'm not going to complain, though. Good job, sellsword.%SPEECH_OFF% | %objective%'s citizens come out to see the remains of their defenses. The women pick through the charred bodies, looking for any sign of their loved ones. Instead, they just find their men burnt to charred and wiry skeletons, faces melted into grim visages that captured their final moments. One of %commander%'s men unfurls %noblefamily%'s banner over the front gate and the commander quickly points to it.%SPEECH_ON%Listen up! See that right there? That is who we are. Now, all you have to do is respect that and everything can go back to normal! Disrespect that, and I will bring you a new normal, got it?%SPEECH_OFF%The crowd of citizens quietly nod their heads. %commander% smiles and it is scarily genuine.%SPEECH_ON%Good! Now, does anyone here make a mean scrambled eggs?%SPEECH_OFF% | You and %commander% enter %objective%'s fortifications to find the coda of a fight for air itself. Blackened shapes, either man or beast, are found having clambered over one another. One man's hand is pulling back the charred remains of another man, his grip stretching back a rope of seared flesh. You cover your mouth to keep from vomiting. %commander% orders his men to raise %noblefamily%'s banner over the front gate. He claps you on the shoulder.%SPEECH_ON%Hey, good job out there, sellsword. You should breathe that stench in, though. It'll help you get used to it faster.%SPEECH_OFF% | You pass through %objective%'s walls holding a cloth to your nose. %commander% walks beside you, holding his head up high with a smugness that is of a stench of its own. Inside %objective%, you find bodies wired together through melted bone and flesh, reared teeth flashing out in gritty grimaces resonating the horrid finality of a burning death. %commander% slaps you on the shoulder.%SPEECH_ON%This was quite a victory, you know that? You should get on back to %employer%, unless you want to help cleanup.%SPEECH_OFF% | You and %commander% enter %objective% with swords raised, but there is nothing to fight: the inferno consumed every living thing. If they weren't burned to death, they can be found caked in the ash and smoke they choked on. %commander% kicks some rubble around, a charred body tumbling over as he does so.%SPEECH_ON%Hell, there ain't much here but the walls.%SPEECH_OFF%He looks at you sternly.%SPEECH_ON%But walls are everything.%SPEECH_OFF%You crouch down and look at the dead man.%SPEECH_ON%Do you think he thought the same?%SPEECH_OFF%The commander shrugs. He quickly turns away and orders one of his men to unfurl %noblefamily%'s banner over the front gate. | You step foot into %objective% and immediately regret it. There are bodies everywhere and not a one is remotely identifiable. The fire turned everything black, even the mud itself. %commander% uses his foot to try and turn over a corpse. Fleshen chips crunch and splinter as though he'd stepped on a thin layer of ice. The man scrunches his nose.%SPEECH_ON%Now that is unsightly, don't you think?%SPEECH_OFF%He turns and lets out a sharp whistle before pointing at one of his soldiers.%SPEECH_ON%You! Raise the %noblefamily% banner over the gates and towers!%SPEECH_OFF%The soldier salutes and rushes off to his duty. %commander% slaps you on the shoulder and says %employer% should be most happy with these results. | There isn't much to recover from %objective%'s fortifications: the fires consumed damn near everything. Those who stayed, burned. Those who rushed to the towers for safety, suffocated. The faces of the dead tell both stories in explicit terms - it was not a good way to go. But %commander% seems happy, ordering his men to start cleaning up and unfurling the %noblefamily% banners. | You pick through the remains of %objective%. The dead bodies draw your eye because you've never seen so many burnt corpses in one place. One is clutching a tiny shape that, upon a closer look, is revealed to be an infant. %commander% walks up and claps you on the shoulder.%SPEECH_ON%Ah, that's a shame. Hey, you did a good job, sellsword. Don't think twice about nothing, got it?%SPEECH_OFF%You nod. The commander smiles briefly before ordering his men to start flying %noblefamily%'s banners everywhere they can. Best to let strangers know that this burnt husk of a fort has new owners. | Inside %objective%, you find all manner of charred chaos. Dead dogs that were set aflame, their chains smoldering them long before the fires could. Horses stuck in stables with their blackened legs stiff in the air. Pigs that broke through their fences and ran wild, no doubt on fire the whole time. A faint aroma of bacon barely undercutting the otherwise horrid stench. There was no escape for any of these creatures.

 You open the door to a storage room and find a pile of defenders that suffocated to death. %commander% comes to stand behind you, looking in.%SPEECH_ON%Poor blokes. They look young. Probably stable hands, squires. What a shame.%SPEECH_OFF%The commander leans into the room and knocks some straw off a loaf of bread. He peels the outer layer away to reveal a fresh core.%SPEECH_ON%Hey, you hungry?%SPEECH_OFF%You politely decline the offer.}

37470368ecbdbbc458ae.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_68.png[/img]{把%objective%的守军逼出来，这一招果然奏效。你与%commander%穿过如今无人防守的城门，查看里面还剩下什么。遗憾的是，大火把大部分建筑都烧成了平地。不过没关系，一名正规军士兵仍在塔顶升起了%noblefamily%的旗帜。灰烬和浓烟翻卷，你几乎看不清上面的徽记。 | 战场上到处都是死人和将死之人。%commander%的士兵穿过一堆堆尸体，偶尔把长矛向下一刺，让脚边微弱的哀鸣归于寂静。

你与指挥官走进%objective%的城门。所有木制建筑都被烧成了焦黑的骨架，庭院里散落着烧死的家畜。%commander%耸耸肩，命令一名士兵在塔顶升起%noblefamily%的旗帜，让所有人知道，今天是谁赢了。 | 战斗结束了。用火把%objective%的守军逼出来，很可能少死了许多人，但城门后的一切也都被烈焰扫荡干净。要恢复往日的模样——不管以前究竟什么样——都得花上不少时日。%commander%倒颇为满意，命令一名士兵在塔顶升起%noblefamily%的旗帜。鲜艳的布面在飘浮的灰烬与烟影中猎猎作响。 | %commander%踩过%objective%工事的灰烬。%SPEECH_ON%好吧，拿下了。至少，剩下的部分拿下了。不过我没什么可抱怨的。佣兵，干得好。%SPEECH_OFF% | %objective%的居民走出来，查看防线的残骸。女人们在焦尸间翻找，想认出亲人的痕迹，却只看到自家男人烧成焦黑干瘦的骨架，融毁的面孔定格着临死前的狰狞。%commander%的一名士兵在正门上方展开%noblefamily%的旗帜，指挥官立刻伸手指去。%SPEECH_ON%听好了！看见那个了吗？那就是我们。现在，你们只要尊重它，一切就能恢复正常！要是不尊重，我就给你们换一种“正常”，懂了吗？%SPEECH_OFF%居民们默默点头。%commander%笑了，那笑容竟真诚得令人害怕。%SPEECH_ON%很好！那么，这里谁炒鸡蛋拿手？%SPEECH_OFF% | 你与%commander%进入%objective%的工事，看见人们争抢最后一口空气后留下的结局。焦黑的躯体，分不清是人还是兽，彼此攀压着堆在一起。一个人的手扯住另一具焦尸，拉出一绺烧烂的皮肉。你捂住嘴，强忍呕吐。%commander%命令士兵在正门上方升起%noblefamily%的旗帜，随后拍了拍你的肩。%SPEECH_ON%嘿，佣兵，刚才干得不错。不过这臭味，你该多吸两口，习惯得会快些。%SPEECH_OFF% | 你用布捂着鼻子，穿过%objective%的城墙。%commander%走在身边，昂着脑袋，那股自鸣得意几乎也散发着臭气。在%objective%里面，尸体被融化的骨肉黏连在一起，龇露的牙齿从焦黑狰狞的脸上闪出，诉说着被烈火吞噬的可怕结局。%commander%拍了拍你的肩。%SPEECH_ON%这可是场大胜，你知道吗？除非你还想帮忙打扫，不然就该回去见%employer%了。%SPEECH_OFF% | 你与%commander%举剑进入%objective%，却已无敌可战：烈火吞没了一切活物。没被烧死的，也裹满了令他们窒息的烟灰。%commander%踢开一些碎石，顺带踢翻一具焦尸。%SPEECH_ON%见鬼，这儿除了墙，真没剩多少东西。%SPEECH_OFF%他严肃地看着你。%SPEECH_ON%但城墙就是一切。%SPEECH_OFF%你蹲下身，看着那个死人。%SPEECH_ON%你觉得，他也是这么想的吗？%SPEECH_OFF%指挥官耸耸肩，迅速转身，命令一名士兵在正门上方展开%noblefamily%的旗帜。 | 你一脚踏进%objective%，便立刻后悔了。到处都是尸体，没有一具还能辨认。大火把一切都熏黑，连泥土也不例外。%commander%试着用脚翻动一具尸体，焦脆的皮肉咔嚓碎裂，仿佛踩破一层薄冰。他皱起鼻子。%SPEECH_ON%这可真难看，你说呢？%SPEECH_OFF%他转身吹了一声尖利的口哨，指向一名士兵。%SPEECH_ON%你！把%noblefamily%的旗帜升到城门和塔楼上！%SPEECH_OFF%士兵行礼，匆匆领命而去。%commander%拍了拍你的肩，说%employer%一定会对这个结果十分满意。 | %objective%的工事里已没多少东西值得抢救，大火几乎吞掉了一切。留下的人被烧死，逃上塔楼避难的人被浓烟窒息。死者的面孔清清楚楚地讲着这两种遭遇——都绝非好死法。但%commander%似乎很高兴，命令士兵开始清理，展开%noblefamily%的旗帜。 | 你在%objective%的残骸中搜寻。那些尸体攫住了你的目光，你从未在一个地方见过如此多的焦尸。其中一具紧抱着一个小小的躯体，仔细一看，竟是个婴儿。%commander%走过来，拍了拍你的肩。%SPEECH_ON%啊，真可惜。嘿，佣兵，你干得很好。什么都别多想，明白吗？%SPEECH_OFF%你点点头。指挥官短暂地笑了笑，随即命令士兵把%noblefamily%的旗帜插到所有能插的地方。最好让外人都知道，这座只剩焦壳的堡垒，已经有了新主人。 | %objective%内尽是烧焦的混乱。狗被烈火吞没，拴住它们的铁链早在火焰烧到之前，就已注定它们无路可逃。马困死在厩中，焦黑的腿僵直地朝天伸着。猪撞破围栏，四处狂奔，想必一路都燃着火。可怕的恶臭里，隐约混着一丝熏肉味。这些动物没有一个逃得掉。

你打开一间储藏室，里面堆着窒息而死的守军。%commander%站到你身后，朝里望去。%SPEECH_ON%可怜的家伙，看着还年轻。大概是马夫、骑士侍从。真可惜。%SPEECH_OFF%指挥官探身进去，拨掉一块面包上的稻草，剥去外层，露出里面尚且新鲜的部分。%SPEECH_ON%嘿，饿不饿？%SPEECH_OFF%你客气地谢绝了。}

263a67d52e5237980bea.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_31.png[/img]{The defenders of %objective% have been annihilated and the fortifications left wide open. You and %commander% walk through the open gates to find corpses, trash, and slaughtered animals all over the place, bloody signs of desperation. The commander nods and claps you on the shoulder.%SPEECH_ON%Good job, sellsword. You should get on back to %employer% now and tell him the news.%SPEECH_OFF% | The battle's over, the defenders of %objective% totally defeated and their fort left wide open for the taking. %commander% thanks you for your service before dismissing the %companyname%'s services from the field. You should go and see a very happy %employer% now. | It was a spirited effort on the part of %objective%'s defenders, but if they were going to make a play like this they should have done it weeks ago when their strengths matched their heroism. No matter now. A starving dead man looks very similar to a well fed dead man and, with enough time, they all look the same.

 %commander% comes and tells you that the services of the %companyname% are no longer needed. You agree and should head on back to %employer% for payment. | Sallying forth when you're starving and beleaguered by poor leadership is never the best of ideas. You're not sure if %commander% would have granted the defenders of %objective% mercy had they surrendered. As it is now, they're all dead in the mud and the world in which they gave up has long since passed. You gather the men of the %companyname% and order them to prepare for the march back to %employer%. Payday will be very sweet after this day. | With the defenders of %objective% out of the way, you and %commander% head into the fortifications. There's a reason the men were so desperate: the conditions are absolutely deplorable. Dead men had been stripped and piled into a corner. A spit holds the cooked remains of what could have been a pig, but it's hard to tell because they flat out consumed every single bit of that animal. A hanged man swings from one of the towers. They'd nailed a board to his chest with 'cannibal' written across it, possibly penned with the use of his own blood.

 %commander% laughs.%SPEECH_ON%Looks like a real party in here, don't it? Remember this scene the next time some belligerent lieutenant with a stick up his ass tells you to just keep holding out.%SPEECH_OFF% | The %companyname% and %commander%'s army have summarily defeated the sallying defenders of %objective%. With the fortifications left free, %commander%'s men quickly take it over. The commander himself tells you to go see %employer% for pay. | %objective%'s defenders died on a battlefield, but if anything it was a field of mercy. Behind the walls of their fort remains almost nothing of value and, in particular, a complete and total absence of food. It is as though the world which existed behind the walls never even knew of food, the defenders had so picked the place clean. You're sure mere mentions of food was a crime for even a torturous word of a flavor would be like a flogging across a man's growling stomach. %commander% comes to your side and laughs.%SPEECH_ON%I thought I knew what it was to be hungry, but I always had an answer for it, you know? I never went hungry with no hope to fix it. What a horrible thing. But then again, they fixed it, didn't they?%SPEECH_OFF%You nod as the man laughs at his dark humor.%SPEECH_ON%You did a good job, sellsword. Go on and see to it that %employer% pays you well.%SPEECH_OFF%}

263a67d52e5237980bea.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_31.png[/img]{%objective%的守军已被歼灭，防御工事门户大开。你与%commander%走过敞开的城门，发现尸体、垃圾和被宰杀的牲畜遍地都是，处处留下绝望的血腥痕迹。指挥官点头，拍了拍你的肩。%SPEECH_ON%干得好，佣兵。现在该回去见%employer%，把消息告诉他了。%SPEECH_OFF% | 战斗结束，%objective%的守军彻底溃败，堡垒敞开，任人接收。%commander%感谢你的效劳，随后宣布%companyname%的战场任务结束。现在，你该去见心情大好的%employer%了。 | %objective%的守军打得很有骨气，可真要使出这一招，就该在几周前动手，那时他们的体力还配得上这份英勇。现在说什么都没用了。饿死的人和吃饱后战死的人，看起来差不了多少；时间再久些，就全一样了。

 %commander%走来，告诉你不再需要%companyname%的服务。你同意，该回去找%employer%领报酬了。 | 饿着肚子，又被糟糕的指挥拖累，还要出城突击，从来不是什么好主意。你不确定，如果%objective%的守军投降，%commander%会不会饶他们一命。如今，他们全死在泥里，而那种可能已经永远消逝。你召集%companyname%的弟兄们，命令他们准备返回%employer%那里。熬过今天，领钱的滋味一定格外甘甜。 | 解决%objective%的守军后，你与%commander%进入要塞。那些人如此绝望，不是没有原因：里面的情形惨不忍睹。死者被剥光衣物，堆在角落。烤架上留着一副熟骨架，也许原本是猪，可实在难以辨认，因为那牲畜浑身上下，已经被吃得一丝不剩。一具吊死的人在塔楼旁晃荡，胸前钉着木牌，上面写着“食人者”，用的可能就是他自己的血。

 %commander%笑了。%SPEECH_ON%这里可真热闹，是吧？记住这副场景。下次要是哪个好战又顽固的副官，梗着脖子叫你继续死守，你就想想这里。%SPEECH_OFF% | %companyname%与%commander%的军队，已彻底击败%objective%出城突围的守军。工事再无人看守，%commander%的部下迅速将其接管。指挥官本人叫你去见%employer%，领取报酬。 | %objective%的守军死在战场上，不过真要说起来，那倒是一片赐予解脱的地方。他们城墙后的堡垒，几乎已没有任何值钱的东西，尤其是粮食，一点也不剩。他们搜刮得如此彻底，仿佛墙后的世界从不知食物为何物。你敢说，那里连提起食物都算罪过，因为哪怕只是说出某种滋味，也像在饥肠辘辘的肚子上抽了一鞭。%commander%来到你身旁，笑道。%SPEECH_ON%我本以为自己懂什么叫挨饿，可总还有办法解决，你明白吗？我从没饿到连一点希望都没有。多可怕的事。不过话说回来，他们现在也解决了，不是吗？%SPEECH_OFF%他为自己的黑色笑话发笑，你点了点头。%SPEECH_ON%你干得不错，佣兵。去吧，记得让%employer%好好付你报酬。%SPEECH_OFF%}

b6fe7180f49119606b2f.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_02.png[/img]{You order the man rescued. One of the soldiers draws his sword and is immediately cut down for his misplaced confidence. The other soldier, seemingly sharper of mind, has already run off. No doubt he'll tell %noblehouse% of what you have done here. The rescued prisoner comes to you personally, going to one knee as he bows.%SPEECH_ON%Thank you, sellsword. You have my blade for this day until my last.%SPEECH_OFF% | In your mind, it is unlikely that the two executioners would abandon their noble flags to join you. But it is quite probable that the prisoner would fight on your side, were you to free him. So you order his rescue. One of the soldiers draws his sword and pledges allegiance to the %noblehouse%. It's the last thing he does. The other soldier flees. Maybe you could have recruited him, but it's unlikely he'll come back given the prompt killing of his partner. Most likely he will tell his superiors of your actions here.

 You go to the freed prisoner. He hurriedly bows and offers to fight for the %companyname%. | You order the soldiers to let the man go. One laughs and simply tightens the noose about his neck and starts to hang him. %randombrother% jumps forward and knocks an executioner to the ground. He beats his face in with a rock while the second soldier runs off. No doubt he'll tell his commanders what you've done here.

 Freed, the prisoner comes to you personally and bows, offering allegiance in return for his rescue.}

b6fe7180f49119606b2f.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_02.png[/img]{你命令手下救人。一个士兵拔剑抵抗，立刻为这份不合时宜的自信付出了性命。另一个似乎聪明些，早已逃走，想必会把你的所作所为禀报%noblehouse%。获救的囚犯亲自走到你面前，单膝跪下，俯身致敬。%SPEECH_ON%谢谢你，佣兵。从今往后，直到生命最后一刻，我的剑都为你而战。%SPEECH_OFF% | 在你看来，这两个刽子手不大可能抛下贵族的旗帜加入战团。不过，如果救了囚犯，他倒很可能为你效力。于是你下令救人。一个士兵拔出剑，宣誓效忠%noblehouse%，随即便没了命。另一个转身逃跑。没准本来也能招揽他，可同伴刚刚被利落地杀死，他大概不会回头，反而更可能向上司告发你。

你走向获救的囚犯。他急忙鞠躬，表示愿为%companyname%战斗。 | 你命令士兵放人。一个士兵大笑，反而收紧了囚犯颈上的绞索，动手把人吊起来。%randombrother%跃上前，将一个刽子手扑倒在地，用石头砸烂他的脸。另一个士兵趁机逃走，定会向长官禀报你在此的所作所为。

获释后，囚犯亲自来到你面前，鞠躬致意，愿以效忠报答救命之恩。}

042e574a05b928116ee6.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_21.png[/img]{While marching along a path, you come across a soldier of %noblehouse%, your allies. He's on the ground, leaning against a rock wall, one arm draped over the top of it as if he'd just placed the last stone. Looking up at you, he sneers.%SPEECH_ON%Whatcha want, mercenary? You come to finish me off, huh? Take all I got and more?%SPEECH_OFF%He's wearing a nice set of armor and has a weapon on him. Not that he'll be defending himself with it in his current state, but it'd look good in the hands of one of your men. %randombrother% walks up.%SPEECH_ON%We can take him, sir, but we should make it quick. Who knows who could catch us for he wears the cloth of a nobleman's army.%SPEECH_OFF% | You come across a wounded soldier of %noblehouse%, your allies. Lying in the grass, he postures up to get a good look at you and you get a good look at him in return: the man is adorned with a decent armor piece and he's got a weapon balanced across his legs. You could take both, but the man does not seem willing to peacefully part with either. And there's a good chance the rest of the soldier's army is not far off... | A wounded soldier of %noblehouse%, your allies, lays in the path. He's dragging himself away, but upon hearing you he stops and turns around.%SPEECH_ON%Ah hell. You'd best turn 'round, mercenary. My men are not far yonder and if you come after me I'll scream.%SPEECH_OFF%You raise an eyebrow.%SPEECH_ON%You'll go out like a woman, eh?%SPEECH_OFF%The man spits.%SPEECH_ON%I'll go out knowing I won't have to wait long to meet ya again in the next world.%SPEECH_OFF%The snarky git has a nice set of armor and weapons on him, but %randombrother% does warn he is a member of a nobleman's army. | A wounded soldier of %noblehouse%'s army lies before you. On one hand, he does have a weapon and some armor you could take from him. On the other hand, he is no doubt party to a much, much larger force than yours. It just happens to not be watching at this very moment. If you decide to take his things, be sure to be quick about it. | Luck or impending disaster? You've found a wounded soldier dressed in reasonably nice looking armor. He's also got a weapon by his side that'd look even better by the side of one of the %companyname%'s men. Taking his things would be a cinch. No one's around to see and muffling him wouldn't be that hard.

Then again, if someone were to see it'd most likely be someone party to a very, very large army because this soldier happens to wear the cloth of %noblehouse%, your ally. Decisions, decisions... | You come across a wounded soldier wearing a shredded banner of %noblehouse%, your ally. Seeing you, he quickly scoots backward across the grass. He throws his hand out and tries to curse, but only blood spits from his mouth. %randombrother% walks up to you.%SPEECH_ON%Sir, he's got a nice set of armor and a weapon on him. We could take him out, if you want, but there is a risk that his army is not far off. We should be very careful about this.%SPEECH_OFF% | You find a soldier of %noblehouse% trying to kick in the door of an abandoned hovel. Hearing you, he quickly wheels around, lifting a sword up to defend himself. The blade, however, wobbles in an unsteady grip. Blood runs the length of his arm, dripping off at the wrist, and the man is struggling to stand.%SPEECH_ON%Stay back, the lot of you!%SPEECH_OFF%A fearful man backed into a corner. How unfortunate he isn't an animal, lest you'd think twice about...

 %randombrother% grabs you by the arm.%SPEECH_ON%Hold on, sir. If the rest of his army spots us we are going to be in some real trouble. Let's try and think this out, yeah?%SPEECH_OFF%}

042e574a05b928116ee6.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_21.png[/img]{行军途中，你遇见盟友%noblehouse%的一名士兵。他坐在地上，倚着石墙，一条胳膊搭在墙顶，仿佛刚放下最后一块石头。他抬头望着你，冷笑道：%SPEECH_ON%佣兵，想干什么？来给我补一刀？抢光东西，还嫌不够？%SPEECH_OFF%他穿着一身不错的盔甲，也带着武器。以眼下的状态，他显然用不了那武器自卫，不过放到你的弟兄手里，倒会很合适。%randombrother%走上前。%SPEECH_ON%团长，咱们能收拾他，不过动作得快。他穿的是贵族军队的衣服，谁知道会不会有人撞见。%SPEECH_OFF% | 你遇见盟友%noblehouse%的一名伤兵。他躺在草里，撑起身子想看清你，你也把他看了个仔细：盔甲不错，双腿上还横着一件武器。两样东西你都能拿走，可这人看起来并不愿安安静静地交出任何一样。而且，他所属的大军很可能就在不远处…… | 盟友%noblehouse%的一名伤兵倒在路上，正拖着身子爬行。听见你来，他停下，转过头。%SPEECH_ON%见鬼。佣兵，你最好回头。我的同袍就在附近，你敢靠近，我就喊。%SPEECH_OFF%你挑起眉毛。%SPEECH_ON%临死还要像个女人一样叫唤？%SPEECH_OFF%那人啐了一口。%SPEECH_ON%至少我会知道，去了那边，用不了多久就能再见到你。%SPEECH_OFF%这嘴硬的家伙身上有副好盔甲和不错的武器，不过%randombrother%提醒你，他毕竟是贵族军中的一员。 | %noblehouse%军中的一名伤兵躺在你面前。一方面，他身上有武器和盔甲，你大可夺走；另一方面，他所属的军队无疑比你庞大得多，只是此刻恰巧没人看见。若决定拿他的东西，最好快些。 | 好运，还是祸事将临？你发现一个伤兵，穿着颇为不错的盔甲，身旁的武器若挂在%companyname%某个弟兄身上，想来会更顺眼。拿走东西轻而易举，四下无人，堵住他的嘴也不难。

不过，若真有人撞见，那多半是来自一支庞大的军队——因为这伤兵恰好穿着盟友%noblehouse%的军服。真难抉择…… | 你遇见一名伤兵，身上裹着盟友%noblehouse%的破旗。他一见你，便赶紧在草地上往后蹭，抬手想骂，张口却只吐出鲜血。%randombrother%走到你身边。%SPEECH_ON%团长，他的盔甲和武器都不错。只要你想，我们就能干掉他，可他的军队也许就在附近。这事得格外小心。%SPEECH_OFF% | 一名%noblehouse%的士兵正试着踢开废弃破屋的门。听见你来，他急忙转身，举剑防身，可握剑的手并不稳，剑刃晃个不停。血顺着整条胳膊流下，从手腕滴落，他连站着都很吃力。%SPEECH_ON%都退后！%SPEECH_OFF%一个被逼入绝境、满心恐惧的人。可惜他不是野兽，否则你动手之前，或许还会再掂量掂量……

%randombrother%抓住你的胳膊。%SPEECH_ON%等等，团长。要是他的同袍看见，我们就真有大麻烦了。先想清楚，好吗？%SPEECH_OFF%}

a84de156581cc6e862ad.source:
{[img]gfx/ui/events/event_49.png[/img]You walk out of your tent and see a wasteland set ablaze. What isn't fire, is blackened by its passing, what isn't dead, is screaming as the flames eat their flesh. Amidst the smog of this ruin march a stream of burly orcs, chained human slaves dragged forward at their sides, a swarm of goblins skipping around to relish in the chaos. And... %randombrother%? The mercenary pokes you and this burning world disappears in an instant. All that's left is the sellsword standing over you.%SPEECH_ON%Sorry to wake you, sir, but your bedding caught fire by the waning candle there. I put it out before it could do any harm. Hey, you alright?%SPEECH_OFF%Nodding, you tell the man to clear out and prepare the men for another day's march. You try to put the memory of the dream out of your head, but it lingers as though it were not meant to be forgotten. | [img]gfx/ui/events/event_76.png[/img]A man comes barreling out of the treeline beside the path. He's wearing rags and half his cheek has been ripped open, his tongue bouncing aloll and with no shape to utter more than guttural screams and desperate pleas. %randombrother% jumps back as the man tries to glom on. You draw your sword, but the stranger merely falls to the ground, his back peppered with darts, the skin the points already pulsing green with poison.

 The company stays alert for a time, but nothing else comes. There's a general agreement that this had to have been the work of greenskins, though it appears that there's evidence of both orcs and goblins work here... | [img]gfx/ui/events/event_97.png[/img]A young fella comes by with his dog trotting beside him. He pauses before the company, patting his little mutt on the head.%SPEECH_ON%You soldiers after the greenies? Tall ones be hard to kill, way I hear it, and the shorties are a real crafty sort.%SPEECH_OFF%You ask the man where he's from. He shrugs.%SPEECH_ON%Far, far away from here. I'm a wanderer, sirs, me and m'dog. But I've seen a lot in my travels.%SPEECH_OFF%%randomname% barges forward.%SPEECH_ON%You're telling me you've seen orcs and goblins working together?%SPEECH_OFF%The boy nods.%SPEECH_ON%Yup! Why wouldn't they? Heh, well, you're not who I thought you were. May your days be long, your nights short, and your dreams as long as want.%SPEECH_OFF%He steps through some standing brush. You give chase, but when you break through to the other side the boy and dog are both gone. | [img]gfx/ui/events/event_94.png[/img]You heard the flies before seeing the chaos upon which they beset. A small hovel, simply shaped wooden supports, a nice thatched roof, some pots hanging from strings, a dreamcatcher spinning in the wind, wooden chimes to bring some delight to the air, and three mutilated bodies in the grass, a cloud of bugs swarming on the corpses. %randombrother% crouches before one, prodding at some bones sticking out of the gore.%SPEECH_ON%Must've been orcs. Footsteps there certainly make it seem so.%SPEECH_OFF%You nod, but notice that there's a few darts stuck to the hovel's door. You pick one off and smell it.%SPEECH_ON%Poison. More than just orcs were here.%SPEECH_OFF%%randombrother% sniffs one of the darts and nods.%SPEECH_ON%Aye, orcs and goblins. Working together? I sure as hell hope not.%SPEECH_OFF%It would be a disaster if they were, but for now you'll just sit happy in the idea that all the evidence here is merely coincidental. | [img]gfx/ui/events/event_02.png[/img]You look at your map then look at the scene before you.%SPEECH_ON%A hamlet was supposed to be here.%SPEECH_OFF%%randombrother% walks past, chowing down on an apple with a satisfying crunch.%SPEECH_ON%Mmhmm, might wanna pen in some edits then, sir.%SPEECH_OFF%The village is nothing but ash. Its inhabitants are hanging from wooden posts or any tree still standing. Bones of those not hanged are piled in the middle of what was probably the town square. Staring at the ground, you see footprints leading away from the carnage. Small ones, big ones. Goblins, orcs. %randombrother% shakes his head.%SPEECH_ON%Surely they are not working together, right?%SPEECH_OFF%You shrug and answer.%SPEECH_ON%I'm sure the orcs swept through and then the goblins came and picked the remains, or possibly the other way around.%SPEECH_OFF%The sellsword nods, assured by your explanation though you both know deep down that the collection of tracks are most likely not a coincidence. | [img]gfx/ui/events/event_97.png[/img]You come across a kid squatting beside a creekbed. He's using a stick to draw figures in the mud - little stick-men with great horned helms and little 'uns beside them, though even the smaller figures appear well-armed and armored. %randombrother% asks the runt what exactly he's doing.%SPEECH_ON%Drawin' the greenies. Been seeing them a lot, skittering and scattering the hills they are, like rats in an open pantry my pa says.%SPEECH_OFF%You ask where he lives. He points up the wooded slopes of a nearby hill.%SPEECH_ON%Yonder. Got a good view of what's coming. S'pose you will in time, too.%SPEECH_OFF%An old man yells out for the kid and he obeys, dropping his tools of atavistic artistry and heading for the hill.%SPEECH_ON%I gots'ta work. You fellas have fun! And don't step on m'drawings!%SPEECH_OFF%Now you realize the stick figures are orcs and goblins, but maybe the kid is just playing fantasy. | [img]gfx/ui/events/event_36.png[/img]You find a fella beside the road cradling his arms in his chest. Both the hands appear to be missing. He stares up at you and the momentum carries him backward, the poor man falling flat and staring up at the skies, pawing at it with nubby forearms.%SPEECH_ON%They're working together. Killed... Killed everyone. I couldn't believe the sight of it. I always said if they came, I'd be prepared, for one or the other. But there they were. Together.%SPEECH_OFF%You ask who or what he's talking about. The man's chest seizes up, pain crookedly crawls across his face, and he takes his last breath. A reflected sky arcs in the glisten of his opened eyes, all to see in death's blindness. %randombrother% checks the body, but there's nothing to take. | [img]gfx/ui/events/event_95.png[/img]A totem of skulls, leathered skins flapping off the segments, each head wearing a cape quite gruesomely of their own making. Blood speckles and fills the ground. More bones. Muscles and tendons, things unused or uneaten. Scorched earth where a campfire grew and scattered ash where it died. %randombrother% picks around the scene, looking for clues. He holds up the shaft of a crude weapon, and a couple of darts found in a goatskin bag.%SPEECH_ON%This is too big for a man's hand, and these are clearly gobbo arrows tipped with, hmm, yes, poison. Greenskins no doubt came through here and they did so working together.%SPEECH_OFF%Working together? That's a horrible thought, but it does appear to be true. Are the savage tribes up to something? | [img]gfx/ui/events/event_71.png[/img]You come to the burnt remains of a hovel. There are skeletons about the rubble, bones jagged and clambering in what was final, painful desperations. A lock lays in a pile of ash beside what should have been the door, suggesting the people held up inside, while the outsiders simply burned the place down.%SPEECH_ON%Sir, you should see this.%SPEECH_OFF%%randombrother% beckons you over. He's standing before a tree. There's a dead goblin leaning against the trunk, palms out, empty, an ugly look on its face, and a pitchfork in its chest. A dead orc is beside it with a shovelhead sticking out of its skull. %randombrother% wonders if they killed each other. You hope so, but their mortal wounds look a lot like a human's doing, and if it were a human's doing, it's possible these greenskins were working together. The thought frightens you deeply. | [img]gfx/ui/events/event_59.png[/img]Refugees on the road, a stream of them, women with babes swaddled and roped behind their backs and affront their bellies, men with pitchforks for walking sticks, discalced friars cutting religious rites through the air with their fingers and breathing prayers under their breath. You try and talk, but they shrink from you, wide-eyed. Finally, an elderly speaks to you quietly.%SPEECH_ON%Don't try, sir, they've seen too much. The greenskins... they came in the night. Orcs in the village, goblins outside it waiting to ambush all that ran. The militia was massacred. Only us cowardly folk survived, and even then only the fastest among us.%SPEECH_OFF%You ask the man if he just said goblins and orcs were working together. He nods and pats you on the shoulder.%SPEECH_ON%Aye, I did. Safe travels, stranger.%SPEECH_OFF% | [img]gfx/ui/events/event_76.png[/img]A man dressed for pomp and pleasure is standing beside the road. He's staring ahead, his hands out to his side, perhaps to balance out a little too much drink in the system. You grab and wheel the man around. His face rocks forward, eye sockets emptied, tendrils of his sight hanging down to his cheeks like rotten crawfish. Two handless arms slap your shoulders as he tries to grip you. His face contorts into a guttural scream that reflects the barbarities he's come to experience.

 %randombrother% quickly jumps to action and cuts the man down. The stranger falls backward, his fine mink coat opening up to show a brutalized naked body, and now you realize you'd rather see a man's parts than see them missing. As he hits the ground, his mutilations are his undoing, the cuts and slices opening his flesh up like a puzzle come apart. His organs burst through the gaps, unfurling in purpled ropes and bags. The man screams.%SPEECH_ON%Orcs! Goblins! Orcs! Goblins! Orcs! Gob... goblins...%SPEECH_OFF%His breath leaves him. He's dead, thank the old gods. Is there something to make of his final words?}

a84de156581cc6e862ad.translation:
{[img]gfx/ui/events/event_49.png[/img]你走出帐篷，看见一片燃烧的荒原。没有起火的地方，已被火焰熏黑；尚未死去的人，正因皮肉遭烈焰吞噬而惨叫。废墟的浓烟里，魁梧兽人源源而行，拖着身旁锁链拴住的人类奴隶，成群地精四处蹦跳，陶醉于混乱之中。还有……%randombrother%？佣兵戳了戳你，燃烧的世界骤然消失，只剩他站在你上方。%SPEECH_ON%抱歉吵醒你，团长。那边的残烛把你的铺盖点着了，还好没伤到什么，我就扑灭了。喂，你没事吧？%SPEECH_OFF%你点头，叫他出去，让众人准备新一天的行军。你想甩掉梦里的景象，可它始终萦绕不去，仿佛本就不该被忘记。 | [img]gfx/ui/events/event_76.png[/img]一个男人从路旁林缘猛冲出来，衣衫破烂，半边脸颊被撕开，舌头耷拉晃动，口齿已无法成言，只剩喉间惨叫与绝望哀求。他想抓住%randombrother%，吓得后者向后一跳。你拔出剑，陌生人却只是倒在地上。背上插满吹箭，中箭处的皮肤已因毒液泛起搏动般的绿。

战团警戒了一阵，却再无动静。众人都认定是绿皮下的手，不过，这里似乎同时留下了兽人和地精的痕迹…… | [img]gfx/ui/events/event_97.png[/img]一个年轻人走来，狗在身旁小跑。他在战团前停下，拍拍小杂种狗的脑袋。%SPEECH_ON%你们这些兵，是来找绿皮的？听说高个的不好杀，矮个的则特别狡猾。%SPEECH_OFF%你问他从哪儿来。他耸肩。%SPEECH_ON%很远很远的地方。诸位，我是个流浪人，只有我和狗，一路上可见了不少东西。%SPEECH_OFF%%randomname%挤上前。%SPEECH_ON%你是说，见过兽人和地精联手？%SPEECH_OFF%少年点头。%SPEECH_ON%是啊！为什么不呢？哈，看来你们不是我以为的那种人。愿你们白昼悠长，黑夜短暂，美梦想做多久就做多久。%SPEECH_OFF%他走进一丛灌木。你追了过去，可穿到另一头时，少年和狗都已消失。 | [img]gfx/ui/events/event_94.png[/img]你先听见苍蝇声，才看见它们盘旋的惨景。一座小屋，木架简单，茅草屋顶整洁；锅盆用绳吊着，捕梦网随风旋转，木风铃为四下添着悦耳的声音。草地里却躺着三具残破的尸体，虫群如云般覆盖其上。%randombrother%蹲在一具尸体前，拨了拨血肉间伸出的骨头。%SPEECH_ON%肯定是兽人。那边的脚印看着就是。%SPEECH_OFF%你点头，却注意到屋门还插着几支吹箭。拔下一支，闻了闻。%SPEECH_ON%有毒。来过这里的，不光是兽人。%SPEECH_OFF%%randombrother%也闻了支吹箭，点头道：%SPEECH_ON%嗯，兽人，还有地精。联手了？他妈的，但愿没有。%SPEECH_OFF%若真联手，必是灾难。不过眼下，你宁肯安心地相信，这些证据不过是巧合。 | [img]gfx/ui/events/event_02.png[/img]你看看地图，又看看眼前。%SPEECH_ON%这里本该有个村庄。%SPEECH_OFF%%randombrother%从旁走过，咬着苹果，咔嚓作响，吃得很满足。%SPEECH_ON%嗯，那可能得拿笔改改了，团长。%SPEECH_OFF%村庄只剩灰烬，居民吊在木桩或尚未倒下的树上。没被吊起的人，骨头则堆在一处，那里多半曾是村中广场。你看向地面，脚印从屠场一路延伸出去，有大有小。地精，兽人。%randombrother%摇头。%SPEECH_ON%他们总不会联手了吧？%SPEECH_OFF%你耸肩回答：%SPEECH_ON%一定是兽人先扫荡，地精再来捡残羹。也可能反过来。%SPEECH_OFF%佣兵点头，像是被这番解释安抚了。可你们心底都明白，这些脚印多半并非巧合。 | [img]gfx/ui/events/event_97.png[/img]一个孩子蹲在溪床旁，用树枝在泥里画小人：大的戴着巨大角盔，小的站在旁边，连小个子看着都武器齐备、盔甲俱全。%randombrother%问他在做什么。%SPEECH_ON%画绿皮。最近老看见它们，在山里窜来窜去。我爹说，像老鼠闯进了没关门的粮库。%SPEECH_OFF%你问他住哪儿。他指向附近林木覆盖的山坡。%SPEECH_ON%那头。什么要来，都看得清。过些时候，你们大概也看得清了。%SPEECH_OFF%一个老人喊孩子过去，他听话地丢下那根原始画笔，朝山上走。%SPEECH_ON%我得干活了。你们玩得开心！别踩坏我的画！%SPEECH_OFF%你这才看明白，那些小人是兽人和地精。也许孩子只是胡乱想象。 | [img]gfx/ui/events/event_36.png[/img]路旁一个男人把双臂抱在胸前，两只手似乎都没了。他仰头望你，身体也随之失衡，向后直挺挺倒下，望着天空，用光秃秃的前臂抓挠。%SPEECH_ON%他们联手了。杀了……把所有人都杀了。我不敢相信看见的东西。我总说，真来了，我也有准备，不管哪一种。可他们就在那儿，一起。%SPEECH_OFF%你问他说的是谁，或是什么。他胸口一僵，疼痛歪扭着爬上面容，最后一口气随之吐出。睁开的双眼映着一弧天空，死去的瞳孔已看不见它。%randombrother%检查尸体，可已没什么能拿。 | [img]gfx/ui/events/event_95.png[/img]一座头骨图腾，层层垂着皮革般的皮肤，每颗脑袋都披着用自身做成的可怕斗篷。血点洒满地面，汇成血泊。四下还有骨头、肌肉、筋腱，那些没用上或没吃掉的部分。篝火烧过的焦土，以及熄灭后四散的灰烬。%randombrother%翻查现场，寻找线索。他举起一根粗制武器的柄，还有从山羊皮袋里找到的几支吹箭。%SPEECH_ON%这东西太粗，不像给人手握的。这些则分明是地精的箭，箭尖抹着……嗯，没错，毒。绿皮肯定来过，而且是联手来的。%SPEECH_OFF%联手？这念头可怕，却似乎就是事实。那些野蛮部落在谋划什么？ | [img]gfx/ui/events/event_71.png[/img]你来到一间烧毁的破屋前。残骸间散着骷髅，骨头扭曲支棱，保留着最后痛苦挣扎的姿态。本该是门的位置，旁边灰里躺着一把锁，表明屋里的人曾紧闭门户，外面的人则干脆把整座房子烧了。%SPEECH_ON%团长，你该看看这个。%SPEECH_OFF%%randombrother%招呼你过去。他站在一棵树前，一个死地精倚着树干，双掌朝外，手里空空，丑脸扭曲，胸口插着草叉。旁边还有个死兽人，头骨里嵌着铲头。%randombrother%猜想，他们是否互相杀了对方。你希望如此，可致命伤怎么看都像人干的。若真是人干的，那这些绿皮就可能是联手行动。这念头让你深感恐惧。 | [img]gfx/ui/events/event_59.png[/img]难民沿路成流。女人们用襁褓和绳子把婴孩背在身后、缚在胸前；男人拄着草叉作手杖；赤脚修士用手指在空中比画仪式，口中低声祈祷。你试着交谈，他们却睁大眼睛，畏缩躲开。终于，一位老人轻声开口。%SPEECH_ON%大人，别试了。他们看见的太多。绿皮……夜里来的。兽人进村，地精守在外面，伏击逃出来的人。民兵全被杀了。只有我们这些胆小鬼活着，也只有跑得最快的那几个。%SPEECH_OFF%你问他，方才是不是说兽人和地精联手了。他点头，拍了拍你的肩。%SPEECH_ON%是啊，我是这么说的。陌生人，一路平安。%SPEECH_OFF% | [img]gfx/ui/events/event_76.png[/img]路旁站着一个衣着华贵的人，直望前方，双臂向两侧张开，仿佛喝多了，正努力保持平衡。你抓住他，将他转过来。他的脸向前晃下：眼窝空了，本该承载视线的东西拖到脸颊，像腐烂的螯虾。他想抓住你，两条没有手的胳膊拍在你肩上，脸扭曲着，喉中发出惨叫，把遭受的暴行尽数喊了出来。

%randombrother%立刻上前，将他砍倒。陌生人向后栽去，精美的貂皮外衣敞开，露出惨遭折磨的裸身。这一刻你才明白，比起看见一个男人缺了那些部位，你宁可它们都还在。他倒地时，遍身创伤成了最后的催命符，伤口将皮肉裂开，仿佛散架的拼图。内脏从缝隙涌出，摊成紫黑的绳索和囊袋。那人惨叫：%SPEECH_ON%兽人！地精！兽人！地精！兽人！地……地精……%SPEECH_OFF%气息断了。谢天谢地，感谢旧神，他终于死了。他最后的话，是否意味着什么？}

1d439935b7166e9b2a41.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_02.png[/img] {A wagon, tipped over. Dead horses by its side. One dead donkey with evidence of having put up a fight. Women. Children. A couple of older men. Most mutilated in a fashion unsuitable for being found by anyone, but you figure your company was probably the best fit to come across such ruin. You've got the stomach for it, for you have created worse. It is the innocence of the dead that turns the gut, though, and in a feeble effort to rectify that moral illness you go ahead and bury the dead. Sadly, nothing of value is found in their remains. | Blood in the ditch by the side of the road. Blood all across the road. Blood in the ditch on the other side of the road. Blood up on the canvas of the wagon. Blood in the dead's eyes and blood in their mouth. One poor farmer, deceased, seemingly happened upon by a band of thieves for nothing of value he carried remains in the ruin you've stumbled upon. | The birds were the first hint: cycling and turning over a distant calamity. You figured whatever they saw was still alive, but by the time you got to it the flock had landed and you stumbled across a dead man leaning up against a sidepost.

You try and scare the birds away. The black buzzards only hop a few steps in the opposite direction where they then turn to stare at you. The corpse is fresh, the means to its death a slow one: a few arrows stick out of his side. A rope on his hip suggests he had a purse there. Someone robbed him - twice. | You stumble across a few hanged criminals. They swing from a tree by the side of the road, their faces mere impressions beneath the woolsacks over their heads. A few of them show signs of torture: gashes here and there, the glaring muscles turning purple and some already grey. Blood beneath one's feet, suggesting someone had a go at him while he suffocated. Naturally, they have nothing of value so you get back on the road. | A goat with a bell cradled in the arms of a dead shepherd. You found the pair by the side of the road. The animal's throat is open, and the man's body has no wounds. Maybe he died of a broken heart. %randombrother% rifles through the dead man's pockets and comes up empty handed. You decide to leave the two where they were. | Two buzzards clasp a string of intestine between the two of them, slowly chomping it down until their beaks clack together. You'd be humored if it weren't for where this meal had come from: a dead child, he or she lying face down on the ground. The back had been torn away, a lurid ribcage glistening in the sun.

You scare off the birds - though they are quite reluctant to be scared at all - and then bury the body. Moving back onto the road, you see the two birds squatting over the grave, picking and prodding at the dirt {in some sort of avian angst | as if to somehow recreate the process they'd seen but in reverse}. Giving up, they eventually take flight, circling above your band of men for a mile or two before heading elsewhere. | The fires crackle and pop as they consume the last of the wagon. %randombrother% picks through the blackened mess, but comes up empty handed. A few hands can be found sticking up out of the ash and soot, their forms as equally black. The bodies are completely gone, buried or burned away or buried beneath that which was burned away. Seeing as how there is nothing to salvage, you quickly get the company back on the road. | A dead horse. Its rider is across the road, having crawled to his final resting spot. Broken arrows litter the path, the heads of them ripped off and salvaged. The man is missing his scalp, the cap of his head glinting and red. After a quick search you realize there's nothing here to take and decide to move on. | You come across a pile of naked bodies by the side of the road. Some of them look ghastly, as though they've been dead for a great long while, though rather fresh blood is in some of their mouths. A few of the corpses carry color in their flesh, but they have what look like bite marks here and there. Preemptive measures were taken, it seems, for every one of them has had his or her neck slashed. Naked as they are, you naturally find nothing but what is natural to nature itself. You move on. | You feel as though you are being stared at and stop, quickly turning to the side of the road with a hand on your sword. A head stares back at you with its eyes barely peeping over some grass. %randombrother% walks over and picks it up. The face carries the visage of a rather jarring death, being so slackjawed and slanted. You tell the sellsword to put the head down for you've better things to do.}

1d439935b7166e9b2a41.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_02.png[/img] {一辆翻倒的货车。旁边是死马，还有一头显然奋力反抗过的死驴。女人，孩子，几个上了年纪的男人。多数尸体被糟蹋得不该让任何人看见，不过你想，也许由战团撞见这片惨状最合适。你们受得住，因为你们制造过更糟的景象。可死者的无辜，仍让人胃里翻腾。你们于是埋葬尸体，试图以这点微薄的举动，缓解道德上的不适。可惜，遗骸中没找到任何值钱东西。 | 路边沟里是血，路面上是血，另一侧沟里还是血。货车篷布上有血，死者的眼里、嘴里也满是血。一个可怜的农民死了，似乎遭遇了一伙盗贼。你们撞见的残骸中，他带着的值钱物品已全无踪影。 | 最先的线索是鸟。它们盘旋转动，围着远处的一场灾祸。你原以为，它们盯上的东西还活着，可等赶到，鸟群已经落地，你发现一个死者斜靠在路旁的柱子上。

你试着赶走那些鸟。黑色秃鹫只朝反方向跳开几步，便转过身盯着你。尸体还很新鲜，可死亡来得缓慢：几支箭插在侧腹。腰间的一截绳子，表明那里原本挂着钱袋。有人抢了他——而且抢了两遍。 | 你撞见几个被绞死的罪犯，吊在路边树上摇晃。头上套着粗布袋，脸只剩袋下隐约的轮廓。有几人显然受过拷打，身上满是割伤，外露的肌肉已发紫，有些甚至灰白。一人脚下有血，说明他窒息时，还有人继续折磨。自然，没有什么值钱东西，你们便重新上路。 | 一只挂铃铛的山羊，被死去的牧羊人抱在怀里。你在路边发现了这一人一羊。羊的喉咙被割开，男人身上却没有伤。也许，他是伤心而死。%randombrother%翻遍死者的口袋，空手而回。你决定让他们留在原处。 | 两只秃鹫各叼着一段肠子的一头，慢慢吞食，直到鸟喙碰在一起，咔哒作响。若不是看见这顿饭来自哪里，你也许会觉得好笑：一个死去的孩子，分不清男女，脸朝下趴在地上，后背已被撕开，骇人的肋骨在阳光下发亮。

你赶走鸟——尽管它们极不愿被吓走——然后埋葬尸体。回到路上，你看见两只鸟蹲在坟上，啄弄泥土，{带着鸟类独有的焦躁 | 仿佛想把刚才目睹的过程倒着重做一遍}。它们终于放弃，飞到你们头顶盘旋，跟了一两英里，才转往别处。 | 火焰噼啪作响，吞噬货车最后的残骸。%randombrother%在焦黑狼藉中翻找，却一无所获。几只手从灰烬与煤烟中伸出，同样漆黑。尸体已经完全看不见，或被掩埋，或已烧尽，或被烧剩的残骸覆盖。既无物可救，你赶紧让战团重新上路。 | 一匹死马。骑手躺在道路另一边，那是他爬行后最终停下的地方。断箭散落路面，箭头已被拔走回收。男人的头皮不见了，颅顶鲜红发亮。匆匆搜查后，你发现此地没什么可拿，便决定继续前进。 | 你在路边发现一堆赤裸尸体。有些面色骇人，像是死了很久，可部分死者嘴里却还留着相当新鲜的血。有几具尸身尚带活人的颜色，却遍布疑似咬痕。看来，有人预先采取了措施：每具尸体，无论男女，都被割开了喉咙。既然一丝不挂，你自然只能看到大自然本身赋予他们的东西。你继续赶路。 | 你忽然觉得有人盯着自己，停下脚步，手搭剑柄，迅速转向路边。一颗脑袋正回望你，双眼刚刚露出草丛。%randombrother%走过去，将它捡起。那张脸嘴巴松垂、五官歪斜，保留着骇人死亡的模样。你叫佣兵放下脑袋，还有更要紧的事该做。}

184f29744b206947dc7a.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_114.png[/img]{You stand at the edge of a forest clearing and the sight therein beggars belief.

 A trunk of a human body runs up out of the earth like a slender tree, naked and bristling, goosebumps for bark, continuing upward until it is twice as tall as yourself. There are no branches. There are no hands. There are, instead, a series of human heads bound in a bunch where a tree crown should be. From left to right they are babyish and beautifully present, ambiguously sexless, malformed creations of time it seems, where the shadows they themselves author turn their faces from ones oddly familiar to strangely naive, as they stare about as though they knew not how they got there and seem ever ready to ask it of you. It reminds you of a drowning you happened upon, the face contorting beneath the running river water, the flesh suffering nothing short of constant conjecture as to what put it there.

 Whispers sift in from the trees. They riffle over the ground as if spoken by the bugs, and they clamber up your arms until they scratch at your very ears. They ask you to stay.}

184f29744b206947dc7a.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_114.png[/img]{你站在林间空地的边缘，眼前的景象令人难以置信。

 一截人的躯干像细树般从地里长出来，赤裸，汗毛竖立，鸡皮疙瘩仿佛树皮，一直向上伸到你两倍身高的地方。没有树枝，没有双手。本该长着树冠的位置，却挤着一簇人的头颅。放眼望去，那些脸都带着婴孩般的稚气，鲜活得近乎美丽，分不清男女，仿佛是时间造出的畸形之物。它们自己投下的阴影掠过面庞，让那些脸时而似曾相识，时而又显出异样的天真。它们四下张望，像是不知道自己为何身在此处，随时准备向你发问。这让你想起自己偶然见过的一场溺亡：那张脸在流动的河水下扭曲，仿佛每一寸血肉都在不停猜测，究竟是什么把自己送到了这里。

 低语从树林间渗来，贴着地面沙沙流动，仿佛出自虫子之口；又沿着你的手臂攀上来，一直搔到耳畔。它们要你留下。}

d0170af4ad8f8557c58d.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_114.png[/img]{You throw the waterskin aside and put your mouth into the puddle and drink. The world beneath the puddle's surface is empty and silent. Your lips move, your throat gulps, but there is nothing to drink here. You scream. There is nothing. Not even a feeling. Just the notion of fear, a tickle with no means to scratch it. When you put your hands to the earth to try and remove yourself, you find that you cannot leave the puddle.

 Faint faces wink in and out of the void. They are like the tree's, dramatically inanimate, painfully issued from past to present to future, and here they approach, gathering in number, bubbling and jostling forward, turning this black hell into a frothy white. As they near, you realize you've been not looking right. Individually, they are but faces without presence. Taken as a whole, as the great white sheet on the approach, you realize that they make up one large face: yours. And it is laughing.

 Screaming, you finally fall back out of the puddle. %randombrother% has you under his arm and he's looking at you with concern.%SPEECH_ON%Sir, are you alright? You was napping then your head slid into the water there.%SPEECH_OFF%You look up, thinking to see the grotesque tree and its awful faces. It is not there and no matter how many times you look or in how many places, it is never there again.}

d0170af4ad8f8557c58d.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_114.png[/img]{你丢开水囊，将嘴埋进水洼，大口喝起来。水面之下的世界空无一物，寂静无声。你的嘴唇动着，喉咙吞咽着，却没有任何东西可喝。你尖叫。仍是什么也没有，连感觉都没有。只有恐惧这个念头，像一处无从抓挠的痒。你伸手撑住地面，想把自己推开，却发现已经无法离开水洼。

模糊的面孔在虚空中忽明忽灭，与树上那些一样，僵得夸张，被痛苦地从过去推往现在，再推向未来。它们渐渐逼近，越聚越多，冒着泡，拥挤着向前，将这片漆黑地狱化成翻涌的惨白。等它们靠近，你才意识到，自己一直看错了。单独看，每一张都只是毫无实感的脸；可把迎面而来的整片白色放在一起看，你才发现，它们组成了一张巨大的脸——你的脸。而它正在笑。

你尖叫着，终于从水洼里向后跌出。%randombrother%将你夹在臂弯里，关切地看着你。%SPEECH_ON%长官，你没事吧？你刚才打盹，脑袋滑进水里了。%SPEECH_OFF%你抬头，以为会看见那棵怪诞的树，以及那些骇人的脸。它不在。无论再看多少遍，往多少地方找，它都再也没有出现。}

01c6cbf770e264dc27d4.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_119.png[/img]{The goblin vanguard vanquished, you march on the city to ransack it. Tiny goblins are slain and scalped or beheaded. More yet scurry around you like ants, each carrying something above their heads like human skulls or treasures and one sprints madly about toting a flagpole with its banner aflame and another dances with the decapitated head of a wolf. Your men turn over huts and shanties and kick out leaners and anything found breathing is put to an end.

 An ancient fortress the goblins used for a city core is set upon with a pillager's eye. You enter the halls yourself and there find a blind goblin crawling with a wreath of human femurs hanging from its neck. The greenskin chitters and chamfers in your general direction, no doubt sensing your presence, though a pained grimace on its face means it also senses the annihilation of its people. You gut the greenskin and leave it to die on the stone floor. Your mercenaries run on ahead and into a council room full of elders and cut them all down in a murderous frenzy that has limbs flying and fingers scattering and blood shooting up the walls and across the tables.

 You head outside to the castle yard. Here you find a pile of dead humans, some mutilated, others charged, one stuffed with a torch as though his ribcage were a brazier. Past the corpses you spot the wolfrider kennels. You have wolf cages burned and their trainers thrown in the fires to die with them. One of the wolves breaks free and sprints further into the city with a cape of flame for fur. It runs from abode to abode barking and howling for relief. You watch as the flames rapidly burn thatched huts and strawroofed shacks. Before you yourself are consumed in the fiery carnage, you order the men back out and watch the whole place burn to the ground. With the savages taken care of, you take inventory of the loot.}

01c6cbf770e264dc27d4.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_119.png[/img]{击溃地精的先锋后，你率军入城，大肆洗劫。矮小的地精被杀死、剥去头皮，或砍下脑袋。更多地精如蚂蚁般四下乱窜，头上各举着东西，有人的头骨，也有财宝。一只扛着旗杆疯狂奔跑，旗帜已烧成火团；另一只抱着砍下的狼头手舞足蹈。弟兄们掀翻棚屋，踹倒支架，凡是还喘气的，一律杀死。

地精占据了一座古老堡垒，作为城市核心，如今也成了掠夺目标。你亲自走进厅堂，见一只瞎眼地精在地上爬，脖子上挂着人类股骨串成的环。它冲你的方向咔哒作响，磨动牙齿，显然察觉到有人靠近；脸上痛苦的扭曲表情，则说明它也感受到了族人的毁灭。你剖开它的肚子，留它在石地板上等死。佣兵们冲进前方一间坐满长老的议事厅，杀红了眼，将它们悉数砍倒。断肢飞舞，手指散落，鲜血喷上墙壁，溅满桌面。

你来到堡垒庭院。那里堆着人类尸体，有的遭到肢解，有的烧得焦黑，还有一具被塞进了火把，仿佛胸腔是个火盆。尸堆后方，是狼骑兵的兽栏。你命人烧掉狼笼，把驯兽者也扔进火里，一同烧死。一头狼挣脱束缚，披着火焰般的皮毛，朝城市深处狂奔。它在房屋之间奔走，吠叫哀号，渴求解脱。你看着火焰迅速吞噬茅草棚与草顶陋屋。在这片火海将你们也卷入之前，你命弟兄们撤出，望着整座城市烧成废墟。解决了这些野蛮生物，你开始清点战利品。}

bf331c2b6c69f5012bce.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_119.png[/img]{%randombrother% shakes his head.%SPEECH_ON%May the old gods have mercy upon us for allowing such a sight.%SPEECH_OFF%The goblin city is sequestered between opposing mountains. Saying the goblins built their city around the mountains is like saying a soldier sheathed his sword in his enemy's chest. The gibbering greenskins didn't add to the terrain, they desecrated the place whole, putting mines where trees used to be, constructing a maze of rusted shanties and lean-tos, raising cultish totems and digging primitive sacrificial pits, piling unused timber as though the mutilation of the mountain was not truly finished without blatant waste.

 But beyond the goblin rubbish does stand a central core of the city, a number of towers unambiguously set apart from the riffraff. These are clearly ancient requisitions, the stonework being unlike anything you've ever seen and surely beyond the greenskin's scope of construct. The goblins walking amongst the walls are upright and boastful as though invigorated by being allowed to stride such hallowed grounds. Nestled inside the fortress seem to be of some sort of higher nobility, well dressed goblins with servants mucking about, which means the same thing it does when it comes to humans: there's good loot to be had.

 A rare sight are the little ones running about. Families, if that's what the greenskins truly have, will mean that a fight here will be a vicious one. The little maggots will have more to protect than just their savageness and greed, and that which must extend itself beyond its own vices is also that which has been weakened.}

bf331c2b6c69f5012bce.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_119.png[/img]{%randombrother%摇了摇头。%SPEECH_ON%但愿旧神怜悯，别让我们再看见这样的景象。%SPEECH_OFF%地精城隐在两山之间。说地精依山建城，就像说士兵把剑收进了敌人的胸膛。那些吱哇乱叫的绿皮并未为山川添彩，而是将此地彻底糟蹋了：原本长树的地方开成矿坑，锈迹斑斑的棚屋与简陋窝棚连成迷宫，邪教般的图腾高高竖起，原始的献祭坑遍布地面。没用过的木料堆得到处都是，仿佛不如此公然浪费，对山体的蹂躏便不算完成。

然而，越过这些地精的垃圾，城中还矗立着一片核心建筑。几座高塔与周遭破烂泾渭分明，显然是它们侵占的远古遗产。那石工技艺你前所未见，绝非绿皮所能造出。城墙之间行走的地精昂首挺胸，趾高气扬，仿佛获准踏入如此神圣的地方，就令它们精神大振。堡垒内住的似乎是更高等的贵族：衣着华丽的地精身旁，仆从忙个不停。这和在人类社会中意味着同一件事——里面有好东西可抢。

难得一见的是，还有些小地精跑来跑去。如果绿皮真有所谓家庭，那此地一旦开战，必然格外凶狠。这些小蛆虫要保护的，将不再只有野蛮与贪欲。而当一个生灵不得不顾及自身恶念以外的东西时，也就有了弱点。}

a10086052578f4e35f23.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_117.png[/img]{Fingerbones like fallen totems, thighs hewn free of the knees as though foresters had set upon a gloomy work, curved ribs scattered across the earth like they were under a shipwright's appraisal, and the skulls, tottering on the wedges of jawbones, held up like animistic abodes of shamans, molars the size of shields and any man could crawl through its eye sockets.

 Looking past the unhold's skeletal remains, you find plenty more fanning out into a valley. The heaviest of the bones stay where their owner's breath had last ushered them, while the smallest of the sort have long since rolled to the valley ditch and settled there in a wash of white wimpled with whatever flesh and fur remains.

You've no reason to believe that none other than the unholds themselves plotted their demise here. Violence is not in their shapes. They are sitting up or laying down in peaceful eternities, and indeed %randombrother% points out a great giant which seems to have recently laid itself to rest. It is nestled into an earthen nook with its hands wrapped over its knees and its head tilted on a shoulder. It watched the sunset, and will do so for many years to come. Not that you care. You order the men to fan out and collect what they can. Some of these bones or pelts or what else they've brought could be of great use to the company.}

a10086052578f4e35f23.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_117.png[/img]{指骨像倒塌的图腾柱，腿骨从膝部断开，仿佛伐木工刚做完一场阴沉的活计；弯曲的肋骨散落地上，像等着造船匠挑选的材料。头骨则支在楔子般的颌骨上，摇摇欲坠，像萨满供奉精灵的居所；臼齿大如盾牌，眼眶足以让整个人爬进去。

越过眼前的巨魔遗骨，你发现更多骸骨散布在山谷里。最沉的骨头仍停在主人咽下最后一口气的地方，细小些的早已滚进谷底沟壑，在那里汇成一道白色骨流，间或覆着残留的血肉与皮毛。

看不出有谁迫使这些巨魔死在此地，它们似乎都是自己选择了这里。遗骸的姿态里没有暴力的痕迹，或坐或卧，永恒地安息着。%randombrother%指向一头庞然巨物，看样子才刚刚长眠。它蜷在土窝里，双手环抱膝盖，头歪靠在肩上。它望着落日死去，往后许多年也仍将如此。不过，你并不在乎。你命令弟兄们散开，尽量收集材料。无论骨头、皮毛，还是别的东西，都可能对战团大有用处。}

17a781ec8e1e1a6ec30e.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_144.png[/img]{You followed the mysterious messenger's footsteps to a cave in the ice. This time it has not been recently trespassed as a thick gate of icicles keep your entrance well stayed. To the side of the cavern's maw is the old man face down in the snow, dead as can be, and with one arm stretched out pointing into the cave.

 Looking through the icy bars, you find the cave quickly declines down a steep slope and toward what may be an underground riverbank that has long since frozen. Something is huddled beside it hitting the ice with a pickaxe over and over again. The wind whistles as it grates against the teeth of the cave. You call out to the huddled man, but there is no response.

It will take some time to chop through this thick ice and get in there. Fortunately, one of the sellswords reports that there may be a rear entrance. It is blocked just as well, but a strong enough man just might be able to squeeze through and face any dangers within.}

17a781ec8e1e1a6ec30e.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_144.png[/img]{你循着神秘信使的足迹，来到一座冰窟。这回，洞口没有近日被闯入的痕迹，粗大的冰柱如同栅门，将入口牢牢封住。洞口一侧，老人脸朝下伏在雪中，早已死透，一条胳膊伸出，指向洞内。

透过冰柱望去，洞内是一道陡坡，尽头似乎是早已封冻的地下河岸。那儿蜷着一个身影，正拿镐子一遍遍敲击冰面。寒风掠过洞口的冰牙，发出尖啸。你朝那人喊话，却没有回应。

要凿穿这么厚的冰进去，得花不少工夫。好在一个弟兄来报，说洞后似乎另有入口。那里同样堵着冰，不过足够强壮的人或许能挤进去，独自面对洞中的危险。}

89717385b9accfb0813c.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_144.png[/img]{%chosen% cuts the madman down. His chest armor shatters and flies off his body, chunks of plate spinning and warbling into the air and yet tethered together by some strange blue tendrils.

 Your men finally break through the icy cavern's entrance and slide down the declination. %chosen% is quite alright, nodding smugly as he sheathes his weapon.%SPEECH_ON%Just a crazy fuck, captain.%SPEECH_OFF%You crouch beside the body. Ice contorts half the flesh, twisting it into nubs of black, and what isn't frozen is flaked by strangely sparkling rime. Despite his grisly state, the mad man died with a wild grin still on his face. The eyes are a bright blue and you see yourself in their gaze, a faceless silhouette. And then the color slowly slips away, not like you've seen before, but as though someone were dragging a curtain through a window, slowly sucking all color right into the sockets. The corpse grins at you, but you refuse to believe that is what you saw.

 One of the mercenaries picks up the mad man's bizarre armor and holds it at length.%SPEECH_ON%What do you figure this is?%SPEECH_OFF%The plates dangle from one another by some strange blue gelatin, and the insides of the metal slats are coated in bubbling, twirling blues as though it were the work of some celestial blacksmith. It is cool to the touch and gives beneath the slightest push of your finger. You've never seen or felt anything like it, but the armor itself is currently in an unusable state. You have the goop and armor put into inventory, scour the cave for more goods which there are none. Before you leave the cave, you glance at the corpse one last time. You think you saw it move again, but surely it is the cold of the frozen north that is playing tricks on you.}

89717385b9accfb0813c.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_144.png[/img]{%chosen%斩倒了疯子。他胸前的盔甲碎裂，飞离身体，一块块甲片在空中旋转震颤，却仍被奇异的蓝色细须牵连在一起。

弟兄们终于打通冰窟入口，沿斜坡滑了下来。%chosen%安然无恙，得意地点着头，将武器收起。%SPEECH_ON%不过是个疯透了的混蛋，团长。%SPEECH_OFF%你蹲在尸体旁。半边血肉被冰扭曲，缩成黑色的疙瘩，尚未冻住的部分则覆着一层闪烁异光的霜。虽然死状可怖，疯子脸上却仍挂着狂乱的笑。那双眼睛湛蓝明亮，你在目光中看见自己，像一道没有面目的剪影。随后，颜色缓缓褪去，却不同于你以往所见，更像有人将帘子拖进窗内，把所有色彩慢慢吸入眼窝。尸体冲你咧嘴一笑，可你拒绝相信自己真看见了这一幕。

一个佣兵捡起疯子那副古怪盔甲，远远提在身前。%SPEECH_ON%你觉得这是什么？%SPEECH_OFF%甲片之间靠某种奇异的蓝色胶质悬连着，金属片内侧覆着不断冒泡、旋动的蓝光，仿佛出自天界铁匠之手。触感冰凉，手指稍一按压便会凹陷。你从未见过，也从未摸过类似的东西，可这副盔甲眼下根本没法穿用。你让人把胶质和盔甲收进库存，又搜遍洞穴，却没找到别的东西。离开前，你最后回望一眼尸体。你觉得它又动了，可那一定只是冰封北境的寒冷在捉弄你。}

ca17a3204d67adb7f78f.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_146.png[/img]{With the killing blow well placed, the Ijirok clambers side to side gripping its final wound. It lets out a howl of pain and buckles at the knees and can only barely hold itself up with one hand as its body doubles over and vomits into the ground. But the whole thing seems like a charade and the beast at times looks over as though to make sure you are watching. It is a drama. A poorly acted show put on by that which does not know death in any sense. The eyes lock with yours and that unsettling grin returns, then the monstrosity flashes a blinding strobe of blue and when the natural light of the world returns the corpse is frozen solid and flakes of snow drizzle from the sky.

 That can't be it. You just know it. You walk up to the iced remains and start chopping away. As you hew into the ice, a blue ooze drips from channels and gaps. One final swing smashes the ice apart and a blob of goo runs every which way. As the men looked on rather concerned, you grab the shattered armor from the cave and throw it into the Ijirok's blood. The strange tendrils which held its pieces together instantly brighten and you watch as they begin to twist taut and pull the plates together. Matted elk fur conjoins with the metal as though they were one being coming to heal old wounds. Blood snakes over the plates like moss twirling beneath a riverbed, curling to and fro before flattening out and painting the armor a slick red. 

Picking it up, you feel a buzz on your fingertips.%SPEECH_ON%I hope you don't suggest I wear that, captain.%SPEECH_OFF%%randombrother% says, shaking his head with a nervous smile. You're not yet sure what the armor is capable of, but no doubt have the mind to keep it in inventory to see. As for the Ijirok, you've no doubt it is still out there somewhere. Its corpse is already decaying rapidly and the bones which remain are not that of a giant beast but simply that of a poor elk.}

ca17a3204d67adb7f78f.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_146.png[/img]{致命一击落定，伊吉罗克捂着最后那道伤口，踉跄着左右摇晃。它痛苦地嚎叫，双膝一软，勉强用一只手撑住地面，身体弓折，朝地上呕吐。可这一切都像一场戏，那野兽不时望过来，仿佛确认你有没有在看。这是表演，一场拙劣的表演，出自一个根本不懂死亡为何物的存在。它与你四目相对，那令人不安的笑又出现了。随后，怪物爆出刺眼的蓝色闪光。等世间原本的光线恢复，尸体已冻得坚硬，天空飘下细细雪屑。

事情不可能就这样结束。你心里很清楚。你走到冰封的残骸前，开始劈砍。随着冰层裂开，蓝色黏液从沟槽和缝隙中渗出。最后一击将冰块击碎，一大团胶质四处流散。弟兄们担忧地望着你，你却抓起洞穴中带出的碎甲，扔进伊吉罗克的血液里。原本牵连甲片的奇异细须瞬间亮起，随即扭转、绷紧，将碎片拉拢。纠结的麋鹿毛与金属融为一体，仿佛同一个生灵正在愈合旧伤。鲜血蜿蜒爬过甲片，如河底水草来回摇曳，随后摊平，将盔甲涂成光滑的红色。 

你将它拿起，指尖传来一阵嗡鸣般的震颤。%SPEECH_ON%团长，但愿你不是想让我穿这个。%SPEECH_OFF%%randombrother%一边摇头，一边紧张地笑。你还不知道这副盔甲有什么本领，但肯定要留在库存里，往后再看。至于伊吉罗克，你毫不怀疑，它仍在某处。尸体已经迅速腐败，留下的骨头也不属于什么巨兽，只是一头可怜的麋鹿。}

cd938d5fc6310531ea24.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_146.png[/img]{With the killing blow well placed, the Ijirok clambers side to side gripping its final wound. It lets out a howl of pain and buckles at the knees and can only barely hold itself up with one hand as its body doubles over and vomits into the ground. But the whole thing seems like a charade and the beast at times looks over as though to make sure you are watching. It is a drama. A poorly acted show put on by that which does not know death in any sense. The eyes lock with yours and that unsettling grin returns, then the monstrosity flashes a blinding strobe of blue and when the natural light of the world returns the corpse is frozen solid and flakes of snow drizzle from the sky.

 That can't be it. You just know it. You walk up to the iced remains and start chopping away. As you hew into the ice, a blue ooze drips from channels and gaps. One final swing smashes the ice apart and a blob of goo runs every which way.

You've no doubt that this thing is still out there somewhere. Its corpse is already decaying rapidly and the bones which remain are not that of a giant beast but simply that of a poor elk.}

cd938d5fc6310531ea24.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_146.png[/img]{致命一击准确命中，伊吉罗克捂住最后那道伤口，左右踉跄。它发出痛苦的长嚎，双膝一软，只能勉强用一只手撑住自己，弓着身子朝地上呕吐。可这一切怎么看都像在演戏，那怪物还时不时瞟过来，仿佛要确认你是否在看。这就是一出戏，一场拙劣的表演，由一个根本不知死亡为何物的东西演出。它的眼睛对上你的目光，那令人不安的笑容再度浮现。紧接着，怪物迸发出刺眼的蓝光。等天地恢复原有的光线，尸体已经冻得坚硬，雪花从空中缓缓飘落。

事情不可能就这么结束。你心里很清楚。你走近冻结的残骸，动手劈砍。冰层不断裂开，蓝色黏液从沟槽与缝隙里渗出。最后一击将冰块彻底砸碎，一团黏浆向四面八方流去。

你毫不怀疑，这东西仍在某处游荡。尸身已经飞速腐烂，留下的骨头却并非属于什么巨兽，只是一头可怜的麋鹿。}

9f26dbae778a5666b1fb.source:
%terrainImage%{You tell the monk to stand down. He shrugs and returns to your side. When you look back at the man you realize he's lit a fire and watch just as he leaps into the well.

 The explosion blows out your ears and puts you on the ground. The earth rolls beneath you in tremble that can be felt through the deafness which you are now submerged. A pluming cloud of fire spears into the sky and growls with the clinking and clanking of metals and the dull plops of leather and other goods, and you roll to your belly and cover your head as it all comes down like the scraps of some god's hellstorm.

 Absolutely none of the debris is of any use. As for the man himself, well, he got his wish. He no doubt died in the blink of an eye, all that remains are charred chunks here and there and broiled lungs and seared strips of sinews and more. You check to make sure your eyebrows are still there and, satisfied, prepare to move on.}

9f26dbae778a5666b1fb.translation:
%terrainImage%{你叫修士退下。他耸耸肩，回到你身旁。再望向那人时，你才发现他已经点起了火，紧接着便纵身跳进井里。

 爆炸震得你两耳失聪，扑倒在地。脚下大地翻腾，剧烈震动穿透了笼罩你的寂静。一柱火云直冲天际，咆哮中夹着金属的叮当碰撞，以及皮革和其他物资沉闷的拍响。你翻身伏地，护住脑袋，任碎片如某位神明降下的地狱风暴般纷纷砸落。

 残骸里没有一样还派得上用场。至于那人，他倒是如愿了。他无疑在眨眼间就已死去，只留下四散的焦黑碎块、烤熟的肺叶、烧卷的筋腱，以及更多难辨的东西。你摸摸眉毛，确认还在，满意地准备继续上路。}

d6f3a6dd1f77c9130846.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_154.png[/img]{A cataclysm as the world knows it comes from the earth herself. Volcanos, floods, earthquakes, plagues, these are things all men fear. The unwarned issuances that can instantly shatter the greatest of kingdoms and disrobe the royal color from the greatest of kings.

The great caldera before you, then, stands as a stark reminder that not only are you small, but you might not even know just how small you are: it is quite clear to even the simplest of minds that the enormous rock at the crater's center came from above. Perhaps very far above. Northerners believe it is the coda of the great war of the old gods. It is a literal mountain weaponized by the deities, thrown like a stone from a catapult before landing with such apocalyptic damage that the horrors wrought ceased all heavenly conflict. Southerners see it as the 'fiery tear' of the Gilder. Looking down upon a world without man, the God fell into deep sadness and cried upon the earth. At first He was fearful that he had destroyed all that lay below, but instead He watched as Man drew up from the fires and armored himself in the ashes. And it is then that He knew Man, living in every corner of the earth, was His chosen beings, and Man knew Him.

Whatever it is, the crater brings followers and believers from all directions. Here exists an amicable understanding that there shall be no impasses upon one another, though during times of religious war that unspoken agreement is oft shattered.}

d6f3a6dd1f77c9130846.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_154.png[/img]{世人所知的浩劫，往往来自大地本身。火山、洪水、地震、瘟疫，人人都为之恐惧。这些毫无预警的灾难，能在顷刻间击碎最强盛的王国，剥去最伟大君王身上的王袍。

因此，眼前这座巨坑便是一个刺眼的提醒：你不仅渺小，甚至不知道自己究竟有多渺小。即便再迟钝的人，也能看出坑中央的巨石来自上方，或许是极为遥远的上方。北方人相信，这是旧神大战留下的终章。一座真正的山被神明当作武器，像投石机中的石块般掷出，落地时造成末日般的破坏，其惨烈甚至令天界的争斗就此终结。南方人则将它视为镀金者的“火焰之泪”。神明俯瞰尚无人类的世界，悲从中来，将泪水洒向大地。起初，祂害怕自己毁掉了下方的一切，却见人类从烈火中站起，以灰烬披甲。于是，祂知道，遍布大地各角落的人类，就是祂选中的生灵，而人类也由此认识了祂。

无论真相如何，这座巨坑吸引着四面八方的信徒。人们在此和睦相处，默契地互不阻拦。然而，一到宗教战争时期，这份无言的约定便常被打破。}

728af5fb6b97cf183c08.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_151.png[/img]{Empire's End. Metropolis of Ash. The Annihilation.

Whatever its name, the ancient city is now a vast grey ruin. It sits beneath a mountain missing a peak, its once glorious shape obliterated in an enormous eruption. The explosion hit with such violence that shockwaves unfurled cobbled streets and sent the bricks showering over the city proper. Enormous granitic boulders cratered neighborhoods whole and boiling debris vaporized all in its way. The flow of lava came last, smoldering much of the city in a black sludge, the edges of which pillowed and toed in bulbous contours until it looked as though a cloud of black smoke had solidified. It is a horrid sight to behold, in part because the earthen rage also captured many victims in perpetuity: grey casts of ancient humans still stand to this day, posed in manners most lively like pairs shaking hands, one looking over a stove, another petting a dog.

Of course, it is wholly within man's nature to see such relics of destruction and, distant as they are from its reality, flock to its remains, and vicariously revivify the violence through means of faith. Followers of the Gilder see it as a warning to not fall for profligacy and greed. Northerners see it as a clash between old gods, a rarity since the dawn of man. One faith or the other, both reside here in mutual respect for those whose lives were lost... respectful for now, at least.}

728af5fb6b97cf183c08.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_151.png[/img]{Empire's End。Metropolis of Ash。The Annihilation。

无论叫什么，这座古城如今都只剩一片浩瀚的灰色废墟。它坐落在一座失去山巅的山脚下，昔日的辉煌模样，早被一场巨大的喷发彻底摧毁。爆炸猛烈得掀翻了石铺街道，将砖块抛洒到整座城里。硕大的花岗岩砸出巨坑，将街区整个夷平，滚烫的碎屑则让沿途万物化为蒸汽。最后到来的是熔岩，以漆黑的泥浆般吞没大半城市，边缘鼓起团团轮廓，像枕垫，又像脚趾，直到整片看上去仿佛凝固的黑烟。这景象骇人，还因为大地的暴怒将许多受害者永远留在了这里：古人的灰色铸形至今仍立着，姿态鲜活，有两人握手，有人俯身看炉灶，还有人正抚摸一条狗。

当然，看到毁灭的遗迹，既远离当时的真实苦难，又蜂拥而来，借信仰重温那场暴烈，正是人的天性。镀金者的信徒将这里视为警示，告诫世人别陷入奢靡与贪婪。北方人则认为，这是一场旧神之间的冲突，自人类诞生以来都罕有发生。无论哪派信仰，都在此共处，一同敬重那些逝去的生命……至少眼下，还算相敬。}

acdf35cf5f994b128a90.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_05.png[/img]{%anatomist% is given the go ahead and he hurriedly retreats to his tent with a bag of tools and %ironlungs% in tow. You wander into the tent to find %anatomist% sitting upright with immaculate posture, and he then bends like an old man with a spine crumpled from old age, then straight again.

Suddenly, he takes one of his tools and punctures himself with it. %ironlungs% reels backward, a bit shocked at such a self-destructive act. He reaches out to help the anatomist, but the man waves him off. Gritting his teeth, %anatomist% starts writing notes as blood spits out of his mouth and onto the pages. Then he repeats the process again, this time from another angle.

Even from a distance you can now see the blood pumping out in ropes of dark red, then now and again spraying in bright crimson. He grits his teeth and commits to another strike. This time a great gush of red spews out. You've seen enough, but before you can finally intervene the anatomist's eyes roll to the back of his head and he passes out %ironlungs% looks shocked.%SPEECH_ON%What the fark? Did you okay this, captain? What did he hope to learn?%SPEECH_OFF%You don't get paid enough to put with these morons. Looking at the anatomist's notes, you can see through the bloodied page that he simply wrote 'not working' again and again.}

acdf35cf5f994b128a90.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_05.png[/img]{得到许可后，%anatomist%拎起一袋工具，带着%ironlungs%匆匆回到帐篷。你溜达进去，见%anatomist%正坐得笔直，姿势端正得无可挑剔；随后又弯下腰，像个被岁月压垮脊背的老人，接着重新挺直。

突然，他拿起一件工具，刺进自己身体。%ironlungs%惊得向后一退，显然没料到会看见如此自残的举动。他伸手想帮忙，解剖学者却挥手拒绝。%anatomist%咬紧牙关，开始记笔记，鲜血从嘴里喷出，溅在纸页上。随后，他换了个角度，又来了一次。

即便隔着一段距离，你也能看见暗红的血一股股涌出，时不时又喷出鲜亮的猩红。他咬着牙，再刺一下。这回，大股鲜血猛地喷了出来。你看不下去了，可还没来得及阻止，解剖学者已双眼一翻，昏了过去。%ironlungs%满脸震惊。%SPEECH_ON%搞什么鬼？团长，这也是你答应的？他到底想学到什么？%SPEECH_OFF%你拿的这点钱，可不够受这群蠢货的气。查看解剖学者的笔记，透过血污，你看见他只是一遍遍写着：“不奏效”。}

af87052159aa0329345f.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_64.png[/img]{%bro% enters your tent with a scroll at his side. He unfurls it, revealing a literal list of things he has killed. You inquire as to what he wants you to do with that. The scroll is tossed onto your desk and he responds.%SPEECH_ON%Compensate me. Higher pay starting right now. %newpay% crowns a day.%SPEECH_OFF% | %bro% apparently wants higher pay, %newpay% crowns a day instead of the %oldpay% crowns he earns now, stating that he has slain a great deal of enemies while in the company of the %companyname%.

Killing lots of things is a good bargaining chip when that's the business you are in, you'll give him that much. | It appears that %bro% wants more pay on account of killing lots of, well, everything on your behalf. You tell him that none of it was on your personal behalf, just that you simply paid him to do it. He nods.%SPEECH_ON%Right. And now I want more pay. %newpay% crowns a day.%SPEECH_OFF% | %bro% feels as though his services for the company aren't being well compensated. He's asking for more pay, %newpay% crowns a day instead of the %oldpay% crowns he earns now, on account of how good he is at that whole mercenary business. | %bro% is demanding you pay him more, %newpay% crowns a day instead of the %oldpay% crowns he earned so far, now that he has proven himself more than capable of fighting for the %companyname%.

He's got a bit of a point, though you're not sure you're ready to hand the crowns over quite yet.}

af87052159aa0329345f.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_64.png[/img]{%bro%夹着一卷纸走进你的帐篷。他展开纸卷，上面竟真是一份清单，列着他杀过的东西。你问，拿这个来想让你做什么。他把纸卷扔到你的桌上，回答道。%SPEECH_ON%给我应得的报酬。从现在起涨薪，每天%newpay%克朗。%SPEECH_OFF% | %bro%显然想涨薪，从眼下每天%oldpay%克朗涨到%newpay%克朗。他说，加入%companyname%以来，自己已经杀了许多敌人。

干的就是杀人的营生，杀得多确实是讨价还价的好筹码。这一点，你得承认。 | 看来，%bro%想涨薪，理由是替你杀了很多——嗯，什么都杀了不少。你告诉他，那可不是为你私下办事，只是你付钱请他干活。他点头。%SPEECH_ON%没错。所以现在，我想多拿点钱。每天%newpay%克朗。%SPEECH_OFF% | %bro%觉得自己为战团效力，拿到的报酬却不够。他自认干佣兵这行颇有本事，要求涨薪，从现在每天%oldpay%克朗涨到%newpay%克朗。 | %bro%要求你多付些薪水，从以往每天%oldpay%克朗涨到%newpay%克朗。他已经充分证明，自己有能力为%companyname%征战。

他说得有些道理，不过，你还没想好是否真要多掏这笔克朗。}

00532125c9d9028e580e.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_02.png[/img]You order the man hanged. Half the company cheers and %killerontherun% screams a shriek rather suitable for seeing death ordered to his side. They drag the man beneath a tree. Ropes are thrown up over the branches, again and again, looping and drawing taut. One man ties a noose while the others cheer and clap and drink beer. A stool is placed and the condemned man is forced to stand on it. As %killerontherun%'s head is put into the noose, he says he has a word for all of you, but whatever he has to say is cut off when %otherguy1% kicks the stool out from beneath him.

This is not a good way to die. It is by an executioner's hand or means. Ordinarily a man dropped from a platform breaks his neck, or is even decapitated. This man hangs choking and kicking. You hear some screams in his lungs, but they struggle to get past his throat. A few minutes pass and he is still fighting. %otherguy2% steps over to the dying man, grabbing one of his jerking feet to keep him still, and with his free hand he stabs %killerontherun% in the heart. And that was that.

{Surprisingly, the brothers agree to cut the man down and bury him. | The man is left hanging there when the company's march begins anew.}

00532125c9d9028e580e.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_02.png[/img]你下令将他吊死。半个战团欢呼起来，%killerontherun%则发出凄厉的尖叫，倒很符合一个刚听见自己死刑判决的人。他们把他拖到树下，一遍遍将绳子抛过树枝，绕好，拉紧。一人打着绞索，其他人则欢呼、鼓掌、喝酒。凳子摆好，受刑者被强迫站上去。%killerontherun%的脑袋套进绞索时，他说还有话要对你们所有人讲，可话还没出口，%otherguy1%便踢飞了他脚下的凳子。

这死法很不好受。刽子手的手段通常利落得多：人从高台坠下，不是折断脖子，便是连脑袋也被扯掉。而他却吊在那里，窒息着，踢蹬着。你能听见肺里挤出的惨叫，却很难穿过喉咙。几分钟过去，他仍在挣扎。%otherguy2%走到垂死之人身边，抓住一只抽动的脚，将他稳住，另一只手拔刀刺进%killerontherun%的心脏。至此，一切结束。

{出乎意料，弟兄们同意把他放下来，好生埋葬。 | 战团重新上路时，他仍被留在那里，吊在树上。}

bfce795918f57b47b7ef.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_178.png[/img]{A recently destroyed village... with no bodies. Only a breeze swirls through, kicking up ash and hissing it through the ruins. But there survives one element: an enormous stone statue masterfully sculpted in the image of a man. Or at least you think it is a man. Its face has been removed with the sort of accuracy that suggests careful intention and not mere vandalism.

Suddenly, mud-squelching footsteps approach from all corners. Bulbous silhouettes limp into the light: slouching hunchbacks formed of most dishonest stitching, torsos haphazardly sewn together with organs vaguely gated behind strands of flesh, additional arms attached with hands wiggling wildly from all sides, and atop the puttied horrors groan multiple heads like some fleshen totem that knows itself, the maws slackened open and gargling at the realized horrors, eyes aplenty and eyes agog, staring at you and the ground and at each other. Your men gasp and arm themselves. The monsters growl and start picking tools and weapons off the ground. One monster reaches down and picks up two cleavers. It trundles forward and faces smeared across its skin turn their misshapen gazes upon you and their mouths open and yell, their shrieks sucking in and out from one mouth to the next, air howling through their internal chambers as the faces take turns breathing so that another may scream.

You've still a chance to run - it is unlikely that these things can keep pace with any man, but what would you be leaving behind, aside from your dignity and pride?}

bfce795918f57b47b7ef.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_178.png[/img]{一座刚被毁掉的村庄……却没有尸体。只有微风盘旋，扬起灰烬，沙沙穿过废墟。但有一样东西幸存了：一尊巨大的石像，精雕细琢，塑成一个人的模样。至少，你认为那是个人。脸部已被凿去，手法精确，显然经过刻意谋划，并非胡乱破坏。

突然，四面八方传来踩踏泥泞的脚步。臃肿的轮廓一瘸一拐地走入光中：佝偻塌背的身体，用违背常理的针线拼缝而成；躯干胡乱接合，内脏仅靠几缕血肉勉强拦住；多余的手臂接在各处，手掌四下乱摆。堆砌般的恐怖形体顶端，几颗脑袋一齐呻吟，像有自我意识的血肉图腾。嘴巴松松张开，为已经意识到的可怖处境发出咯咯声；一双双惊惶圆睁的眼睛，有的看你，有的看地，有的看向彼此。弟兄们倒吸凉气，抓起武器。怪物低吼，开始拾取地上的工具和兵刃。一只俯身捡起两把切肉刀，摇晃着向前。仿佛涂抹在皮肤上的面孔，将歪曲的目光转向你，张嘴尖叫。声音从一张嘴吸入，又从另一张嘴呼出，气流在体内的腔室间呼啸；这些脸轮番呼吸，只为让别的嘴能继续尖叫。

你还有机会逃跑——这些东西恐怕追不上任何正常人。可除了尊严和骄傲，你还会把什么留在身后？}

918cfb2de01db1e3a874.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_62.png[/img]You roll the dice, landing a total of %playerdice%.

%gambler% goes next, rolling a total of %gamblerdice%.

{Well, you lost. The gambler snatches the dice back up - as well as your twenty-five crowns - and aks if you wish to have another go. | The dice were not in your favor and the gambler takes his earnings. He looks up to you, grinning.%SPEECH_ON%Wish to have another go?%SPEECH_OFF% | The numbers are counted up and, alas, you have lost. The gambler asks if you wish to go again. | Lost! But maybe if you roll again... | You lose! A simple roll of the dice, and simple loss. But this one hurts a lot less than which you've seen on the fields of battle. The gambler asks if you wish to have another go. | The gods have shunned you and your silly dice. Losing the game is a minor setback, but your pride costs a little more than twenty-five crowns. Should you roll again? | The odds have betrayed you for a measly twenty crowns. Maybe if you roll again you can win them back? | You watch your dice tumble, seeing for but a moment the winning numbers before it tilts and falls to another side, revealing a losing total. The gambler laughs and asks if you wish to throw again. | Your throw was perfect! How could you lose? He needed just those numbers to win! Shaking your head, you wonder if you should roll again.}

918cfb2de01db1e3a874.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_62.png[/img]你掷出骰子，总共%playerdice%点。

接着轮到%gambler%，他掷出了%gamblerdice%点。

{好吧，你输了。赌徒一把收回骰子，连同你的二十五克朗，问你要不要再来一局。 | 骰子没有眷顾你，赌徒收下赢来的钱，抬头咧嘴一笑。%SPEECH_ON%还来一局吗？%SPEECH_OFF% | 点数一算，唉，你输了。赌徒问你是否再来。 | 输了！不过，要是再掷一次…… | 你输了！简单掷一把骰子，简单输一场。只是这回的损失，比战场上见过的那些轻多了。赌徒问你是否还来一局。 | 诸神抛弃了你，连同你那愚蠢的骰子。输场赌局只是小挫折，可你的面子不止值二十五克朗。要再掷一次吗？ | 运气背叛了你，只为区区二十克朗。也许再来一把，就能赢回来？ | 你盯着翻滚的骰子，能让你获胜的点数只朝上停了一瞬，便又倾倒过去，最终凑成一手败局。赌徒笑着问你，还要不要再掷。 | 你这一掷明明完美极了！怎么会输？偏偏他就掷出了唯一能赢你的点数！你摇摇头，琢磨着要不要再来一次。}

d861ba6593c8ecd99845.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_62.png[/img]You roll the dice, landing a total of %playerdice%.

%gambler% goes next, rolling a total of %gamblerdice%.

{You won! The gambler claps his hands.%SPEECH_ON%Beginner's luck!%SPEECH_OFF%You cross your arms.%SPEECH_ON%I thought it was all luck?%SPEECH_OFF%The gambler laughs and asks if you wish to test that theory. | The gambler leans back.%SPEECH_ON%Well I'll be damned. Let's throw again!%SPEECH_OFF% | The gambler leans back.%SPEECH_ON%{Well I'll be a horse's fartin' arse | I'll be damned if the gods haven't turned their backs on me | Now that right there is a poor showin' of lady luck | I'd bedded a lady by the name of Luck, what good it's done me though | That right there is a misfortune, for me that is | Oy, that's a winning roll | I'll be a ragamuffin | Son of a gelded horse | Shits on a wet a pig | As damned as a nun on her back | The throw of a master I say | Yer a robber with such a throw and yeah | May %randomtown% join the orcs | And they say a blind squirrel can't find a nut | Tickle m'anus with a rosebush and call me Sally Siegfried}, ya won! Let's roll again!%SPEECH_OFF% | You've won! Laughing, you take your earnings and the gambler asks if you wish to have another throw.}

d861ba6593c8ecd99845.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_62.png[/img]你掷出骰子，总计%playerdice%点。

接着轮到%gambler%，他掷出了%gamblerdice%点。

{你赢了！赌徒拍了拍手。%SPEECH_ON%新手的运气！%SPEECH_OFF%你抱起双臂。%SPEECH_ON%我还以为这本来就全靠运气？%SPEECH_OFF%赌徒笑着问，要不要再验证一下这个说法。 | 赌徒往后一靠。%SPEECH_ON%真是见鬼。再掷一把！%SPEECH_OFF% | 赌徒往后一靠。%SPEECH_ON%{真他娘的马屁眼 | 诸神肯定全都背弃我了 | 幸运女神这回可真丢人 | 我倒是睡过一个叫幸运的女人，可屁用都没有 | 真是倒霉——我是说我 | 好一个赢定了的点数 | 我可真成了穷光蛋 | 阉马养的 | 真是屎糊了落汤猪 | 跟张腿的修女一样该下地狱 | 要我说，这一手真是大师本事 | 你这么一掷，简直跟抢钱没两样 | 愿%randomtown%投奔兽人 | 谁说瞎松鼠找不着果仁 | 拿玫瑰丛挠我屁眼吧，再叫我莎莉·齐格弗里德}，你赢了！再来一把！%SPEECH_OFF% | 你赢了！你笑着收下赢来的钱，赌徒则问，你要不要再掷一把。}

f85f9125e45c975dd182.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_12.png[/img]{Obviously, this isn't an ordinary sight for you so, curious, you call out to the weary travelers. Words barely leave your lips before the entire line of men stops in an instant and bolts upright. Their cloaks unravel and droop from their heads, and their tomes and sticks and religious imports fall aside in a uniform clatter. The men look around, wide eyes more alive than ever. One screams. Then another. And soon they are all screaming, and some crumple to the ground, clutching their ears as though to silence the horrid howls their mouths had to give, while others wheel in circles, arms out, begging for answers.

 Your mere utterance has seemingly broken a spell that was so long over their heads it had brought them here, impoverished, hungry, and insane. Step by step, they were governed by a malicious higher power, and step by step they felt the control in their lives slip away, and with it the sanity all men require to be themselves. Unfortunately, you can hardly ask them what or who did this to them, for some fall over dead while others make naked sprints into the forest. | A curious sight such as this begs questioning, but the second a word leaves your lips the entire troop of religious men bolt upright, the sudden shuffle of clothes and gear clattering in such uniformity it as if a door was slammed shut. The men drop their things and begin screaming. It is a raspy chorus. They all begin to collapse, either buckling on bony knees or clutching their stomachs in pained hunger.

 %randombrother% comes up, shaking his head.%SPEECH_ON%Were they cursed? What could have done this?%SPEECH_OFF%You won't ever get an answer for a minute later every single man is dead, looking no better than corpses having recently been thawed out of the mountains. The spell must have forcibly piloted their pilgrimage here, straining the human body while keeping it alive by the mere strand of ethereal malevolence. Although they are all dead, you do not regret freeing them of such a horrid curse.}

f85f9125e45c975dd182.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_12.png[/img]{这显然不是你常见的景象。出于好奇，你朝疲惫的旅人们喊了一声。话音刚出口，整列人便骤然停步，挺直身体。斗篷从头上散落垂下，书本、手杖与宗教器物一齐掉落，发出整齐的碰撞声。他们四下张望，双眼圆睁，比先前鲜活得多。一人尖叫，随后又一个。很快，所有人都在尖叫。有些瘫倒在地，捂住耳朵，仿佛想堵住自己嘴里发出的可怕哀号；另一些伸着胳膊，原地转圈，乞求答案。

你仅仅一声呼唤，似乎就打破了长久笼罩他们的咒语。它把他们带到这里，穷困、饥饿、疯狂。一步又一步，他们被恶意的更高力量操控；一步又一步，感到自己对人生的掌控溜走，连同作为一个人所需的理智。可惜，你几乎无从询问，是谁，或是什么，将他们变成这样。有人倒地死去，还有人赤身裸体地冲进森林。 | 如此古怪的景象，自然令人想问个究竟。可你才吐出一个字，整队虔信者便猛然挺直，衣物与装备一齐响动，整齐得仿佛有人砰地关上了一扇门。众人丢下东西，开始尖叫，组成嘶哑的合唱。随后纷纷倒下，有的枯瘦双膝一软，有的因饥痛抱住肚子。

%randombrother%走来，摇着头。%SPEECH_ON%他们被诅咒了？什么东西能干出这种事？%SPEECH_OFF%你永远也不会知道答案。片刻之后，所有人都死了，模样与刚从山中冻层里化出的尸体无异。那咒语想必强行驱使他们朝圣至此，榨干身体，仅凭一缕虚无恶意维持生命。虽然他们全死了，你仍不后悔，至少让他们摆脱了如此可怕的诅咒。}

af905cd30426606a428b.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_137.png[/img]{You walk the stands of a jousting arena. Moldy fruits and vegetables litter the floor. Dried blood freckles the seats. And silence fills the air. When you sit, the wood of the place seems to groan in unison as though discomfited by the haunt of a rare visitor.

In your hands is a note. 'Looking fer hardy men, knowledge of the sword pref'rred but all welcome.' It is an old note, its purpose long since served. But what draws your eye is the price offered to the task: more crowns than you could muster in five tournaments.

 If this is the coin to be earned, then to hell with the jousts and the sparring. But you're not one to suit up for some other captain's orders. With all that you've earned over the years you imagine you could start your own mercenary band just fine.}

af905cd30426606a428b.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_137.png[/img]{你走过马上比武场的看台。霉烂的瓜果蔬菜散落一地，干涸血迹斑斑点点地沾在座位上，四下寂静。你一坐下，整片木结构仿佛都在一同呻吟，像是被这位罕见的访客惊扰了。

你手里捏着一张告示：“招结实汉子，会使剑最好，不会也收。”告示已经很旧，上头的差事早已结束。可吸引你的，是开出的价钱：比你连打五场比武能挣的克朗还多。

 若真能挣到这么多，那就让骑枪比武和切磋较艺见鬼去吧。但你也不是甘心披挂上阵、听另一个团长发号施令的人。这些年攒下的钱，想必足够让你拉起自己的佣兵团了。}

e85a9969b5a09818fc9d.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_172.png[/img]{Constant conflict between nomads, city states, and vagabonds makes for good business: deserters, criminals, prisoners of war, and indebted alike flee across the land, and you with manacle in hand give chase.

Despite the barren wastes upon which they rule, the Southern Realms are home to large and ever shifting populations which makes personhood itself a resource worth harvesting. The riverlike flow of persons is as natural an economy as any raw material.

Prisoners of war make up the bulk of your outfit, beaten men who must submit to and fight for another force: your own. Criminals and general riff raff fill in here and there, easy pickings from smaller villages who don't have the means to handle their resident reprobates. And then there are the indebted... hellfire-doomed souls who must work their way back into the Gilder's gleam, and find salvation through blood, sweat, and tears. While most must work as laborers, you favor pressing them into your company. The indebted will not protest, for even the priests state it must be within the Gilder's sublime vision that they will find penitence in the %companyname%.}

e85a9969b5a09818fc9d.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_172.png[/img]{游牧民、城邦与流浪者之间冲突不断，正是做生意的好时机：逃兵、罪犯、战俘和负债者四处逃亡，而你手握镣铐，紧追在后。

南方诸邦虽统治着贫瘠荒漠，却拥有庞大且不断流动的人口，于是，人本身也成了值得收取的资源。人流如河，与任何原料一样，自成一门顺理成章的生意。

战俘构成了你队伍的主体。这些战败者必须臣服于另一股势力，并为之作战——也就是你。罪犯和各路杂碎则填补余下的人手，小村庄无力处置本地的恶棍，很容易就能从那里将他们带走。还有负债者……这些注定受地狱烈火折磨的灵魂，必须用劳作重新走回镀金者的光辉里，以血、汗与泪求得救赎。大多数负债者都得做苦工，你却更愿意将他们编进战团。他们不会抗议，因为连祭司也说，能在%companyname%中赎罪，必然也是镀金者崇高旨意的一部分。}

5788c8e08aff029a505e.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_141.png[/img]{Hunt down bandits. Ward off raiders. Trap wolves attacking the farmsteads. All in a militiaman's work. And if more is asked then there is simply more to answer. All to keep your home of %home% safe.

 When a nobleman called on you, you and a group of ad hoc fighters took to the field in a battle between highborn. You didn't know their names or their quarry, only that one mustered you and your men to the field. And so there you went. Unfortunately, a lowborn man with spear and shield is little more than a peasant with misgivings of warriorship. Your militia was used to hold a contingent of enemy knights in place while your own side's archers rained hell from above, hitting knight and peasant alike.

 After the battle, you and your men fled the fields for good. You took up arms as sellswords and swore to one another by blood pact that you'd never have a highborn in your company. A mercenary band of motley men and that is that.}

5788c8e08aff029a505e.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_141.png[/img]{追剿强盗，抵御劫掠者，设陷阱捕杀袭击农庄的狼。这都是民兵的分内之事。若还有别的差遣，那就再多尽一份力。一切都是为了守护你们的家乡%home%。

 一名贵族征召你们时，你和一群临时凑起来的战士便奔赴战场，卷入高门贵族之间的争斗。你不知道他们姓甚名谁，也不知道他们争的是什么，只知道其中一人征召了你和你的弟兄，于是你们就去了。可惜，出身低微的人即便拿上长矛和盾牌，也不过是些自以为成了战士的农民。你们的民兵被用来拖住一队敌方骑士，好让己方弓箭手从上方倾泻箭雨，骑士和农民一概不放过。

 战斗结束后，你和弟兄们逃离了战场，再也不愿回头。你们拿起武器当了佣兵，歃血立誓，绝不让任何贵族出身的人加入战团。你们就是一群平民杂兵组成的佣兵团，仅此而已。}

39a37253e05866b09aec.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_180.png[/img]{You knew the game well, and like any good game you got burned out on the rules and the rule setters. Oaths for this, Oaths for that. All you knew is you never got to hold Young Anselm's skull, and last you saw some Oathbringer had stolen off with the lad's preeminent jaw. Leaving the Oathtakers was the best decision you ever made, if only to preserve what little sanity you had left.

Unfortunately, the faithful have a strong nose for the apostate's scent. When you opened the door this morning it was like looking at two piles of shite some prankster kid had left you: %oathtaker1% and %oathtaker2%, in the flesh. The former an older man who simply never shook his beliefs, and the latter a talented squire who reminds you of yourself. No doubt the more mawkish talker, it was the younger lad who made his plea: the Oathtakers need a man familiar with the land to help them around, completing quests and oaths. You shut the door only to find the older man's foot in it. He held up a pile of gold, and your nose must have wrinkled or wiggled because both men lit up.

Now, you're only going along because times are tough, and because mercenary work – even under the guise of religious duty – can make some outstanding coin. And if someone is willing to bankroll you into such an opulent task, then so be it. There is only one condition: you will take the Oath of Captaincy, which means all the battling and rough roading will be done by others. Without pause, the Oathtakers agree, and then they show you Young Anselm's skull. You've lost touch with the organization, but seeing that lad's dumb dome still brings a stir in your heart. %oathtaker2% nods.%SPEECH_ON%Let us scour these lands for the honorable, and be diligent in our tasks, and may we ever make Young Anselm whole again from the rat bastard Oathbringers who broke him!%SPEECH_OFF%}

39a37253e05866b09aec.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_180.png[/img]{你很熟悉这套玩法，而再好的游戏，玩久了也会厌倦规则，以及制定规则的人。这个要发誓，那个也要发誓。你只知道，自己从没轮到捧小安塞尔姆的头骨，最后一次听说，还有个誓言使者偷走了那位小伙子最受敬重的下颌骨。离开立誓者，是你做过最明智的决定，哪怕只为了保住所剩无几的理智。

可惜，虔信者嗅得出背教者的气味。今早打开门，你仿佛看见哪个恶作剧的小孩留下两堆屎：%oathtaker1%和%oathtaker2%，活生生站在面前。前者年岁已长，信仰却从未动摇；后者是个有天分的骑士侍从，让你想起当年的自己。年轻小伙显然更擅长煽情，便由他出面恳求：立誓者需要一个熟悉各地的人，带他们四处奔走，完成任务，践行誓言。你关上门，却被老人的脚卡住了。他举起一堆金子，而你的鼻子想必皱了皱，或动了动，因为两人的眼睛都亮了。

如今，你答应同行，只因日子艰难，而佣兵生意——即便披着宗教义务的外衣——仍能挣来大笔钱财。既然有人愿意出资，让你接下如此肥差，那就这样吧。你只提一个条件：自己要立下团长之誓，也就是说，战斗与艰苦奔波都由别人来做。立誓者毫不犹豫地答应，随后拿出了小安塞尔姆的头骨。你虽与组织久无往来，可再看见那小子傻乎乎的脑壳，心里仍泛起一阵波动。%oathtaker2%点头。%SPEECH_ON%让我们遍寻此地的荣耀，勤勉履行使命，再从那些亵渎遗骨的誓言使者混账手里，把小安塞尔姆拼回完整的模样！%SPEECH_OFF%}

98d8035d33ccd11727ec.source:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_156.png[/img]{You could have stayed home. Never left town. Just lived out your days laboring for some Vizier. Instead, you took up the sword, scrounged what little money the Gilder had shone upon you, and started a band of mercenaries.

Life as a Crownling has taken you places that most others never see. In a sense, you've carved open doors and avenues through violence. But the years have slowly weighed down your neck with a nasty truth: you're barely a step above being a brigand. You get hired by locals to do simple things for simple pay and then sent on your way. You want the %companyname% to be bigger than that. You want your company shown to the Vizier's offices, you want it to gain the glory it deserves, and maybe you want it to even travel north to faraway lands. Hell, maybe in the north they treat a mercenary with respect!

Of course, it won't be easy. You've just a few men on hand. But those men are %bro1%, %bro2%, and %bro3%, the finest fighters you've ever known. With them at your side, the whole world shall come to know the %companyname%!}

98d8035d33ccd11727ec.translation:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_156.png[/img]{你本可以留在家乡，一辈子不出城，为某个维齐尔做苦工，直到终老。可你选择拿起剑，凑齐镀金者赐予你的那点微薄积蓄，组建了一支佣兵团。

克朗客的生涯带你走过许多人终其一生都无缘踏足的地方。从某种意义上说，你用暴力劈开了一扇扇门，也闯出了一条条路。但岁月渐长，一个难堪的事实也越来越沉重地压在你肩上：你其实只比强盗强上那么一点。当地人雇你们干些简单的活，付些工钱，然后便打发你们离开。你希望%companyname%能有更大的出息。你希望战团能成为维齐尔府上的座上宾，赢得应有的荣光，或许还要远赴北方，闯荡遥远的异乡。见鬼，说不定北方人还懂得尊重佣兵呢！

当然，这条路并不好走。你手下只有寥寥几人。但他们是%bro1%、%bro2%和%bro3%，是你见过最优秀的战士。有他们并肩作战，整个世界都将记住%companyname%的名字！}

ae4d5da09fe9786bff86.source:
%terrainImage%{You eye a traveler in the distance bobbing forth, slouched and crooning like a wingless gargoyle. His walking stick bobs and prods in front of him and even far away you hear the snicker and snacker of stones being tapped. You give an order for your men to hold and wait, letting the stranger come to you.

When he finally nears, he looks up. At first, his nose is all that you see, the rest of him hidden in a cloak. He sniffs gingerly like a blind mole come across a bizarre impasse. Just as you begin to ask if the man is alright, he throws the cloak back, revealing himself. That which faces you is a tired figure. Hobbled. Sleepless days pinch creases about his eyes. Reddened cheeks spread as he smiles. He asks if he might stay with your party for a time. | A traveler hails your party from the roadside. He says he's on his way to %randomtown% but that he wouldn't mind a rest. The next question he has is an obvious one: he wonders if it'd be alright to stay with your party for the night. | A traveler carrying a cart of personal goods heads your way. You let him approach, holding your hand up to warn him to go no further. He states that he is a simple wanderer and that he's only looking to get to %randomtown%. First showing that he is completely unarmed, he asks if maybe he can stay the night with your company. | A whistling man ambles down the road, a cheery dog huffing at his side with its tongue aloll. Seeing your troop, he stabs his walking stick into the dirt and tents his hands atop it. Some small talk is made of the weather, notably that rain is in the belly of some oncoming clouds. He asks if mayhaps he could dodge the rain in the company of sellswords. A strange request, not one usually made to men who earn blood money. | A man walks the road with a shovel bobbing over one shoulder and a sack of dirt swinging in the other hand. When you inquire as to what he is doing, he says he's just buried his brother and he's on his way back to %randomtown%. The sack holds some of the dirt where his kin was laid to rest. Respectable. The man looks weary, as weary as a man who has buried his sibling would understandably be. Perhaps sensing your pitying gaze, he asks if maybe he can stay with your company for a time. | You spot a strange man hobbling along the road. He's dressed in a long cloak and he's got a knapsack yoked over one of his shoulders. His eyes stare at the ground until they come to your feet at which point he finally looks up. Seeing your company, the man is surprisingly unalarmed. In fact, he's quite receptive of your presence and asks if maybe he could spend the night with sellswords before continuing his journey to %randomtown%. | A man with a pitchfork is crossing a field where the crops have failed. His feet scuff up the deadened ground and you see tufts of ash being pitched wind-wise. When he gets to the road, you hail him down and ask where he's coming from. The man is a daytaler only trying to get back home. All the work around here is dried up, literally. Licking his cracked lips, the man wonders if maybe he could stay the night with your company. He certainly looks like he could use some rest, anyway. | A man carrying a bucket of tools crosses paths with your company. The roads seem ill-fit to place one man against a company of sellswords, and this stranger appraises the situation correctly by placing his wares down and putting his hands up.

You tell him to calm and ask where he is going. He explains that he is a mason from %randomtown%, but that his work there is done. He's only on his way back to his family located on a homestead a good day's walk from where you stand. Looking rather thirsty and tired, the man asks if maybe he could spend the night with your company to help him rest for the coming walk. | A figure appears on the horizon, blurred and shimmering in a heat haze. It appears to have paused, no doubt having seen you, too. With little fear, you press the men onward and soon come across a man toting a few bags of this or that. He's sitting down on the ground and doesn't bother getting up when you near. He explains he's been on the road for days and could use a good night's rest. Naturally, he asks if he can spend that rest in the company of your men. | You come across a man who is weak and weary. He explains that he has been searching for his lost dog, but that he's just about given up. Before he heads home, he wonders quite loudly if maybe a night's rest in your company could help him find the energy to seek out his mutt for one more day. | A man tracked by buzzards is found on the side of the road. He's not hurt or wounded, just exhausted. He asks with a cracking voice if maybe he could spend the night in the company of your men.}

ae4d5da09fe9786bff86.translation:
%terrainImage%{远处，一个旅人一颠一颠地走来，弓着背，低声哼吟，像只没翅膀的石像鬼。拐杖在身前起落探路，隔着老远，你都听得见敲击石头的咔哒声。你下令停步等候，让陌生人走近。

终于来到面前，他抬起头。起初，你只能看见鼻子，其余都藏在斗篷里。他小心地嗅了嗅，像盲眼鼹鼠遇上了古怪障碍。你刚想问是否安好，他便掀开斗篷，露出真容。眼前是一个疲惫、跛行的人，失眠的日子在眼周挤出皱纹。一笑，泛红的脸颊便舒展开。他问，能否与你们待上一阵。 | 一名旅人从路边招呼战团，说自己正要去%randomtown%，不过也想歇歇。接下来的问题不出所料：今晚能否跟你们一起过夜？ | 一名旅人拉着小货车，装着个人物品，朝你们走来。你让他靠近，随后抬手示意，到此为止。他说，自己只是个普通游荡者，只想赶到%randomtown%。先证明身上完全没有武器后，他问，能否与战团借宿一晚。 | 一个男人吹着口哨，沿路闲步，身旁的狗欢快地吐着舌头喘气。看见队伍，他将拐杖插进泥里，双手拢在杖顶。双方闲聊天气，尤其提到将至的云腹中藏着雨。他问，是否能与佣兵们一道避雨。真是古怪的请求，通常没人会向挣血钱的人开这个口。 | 一个男人走在路上，肩上铁锹一起一落，另一只手提着一袋土。你问在做什么，他说，刚埋葬自己的弟兄，正在返回%randomtown%。袋里装着些亲人安息之处的泥土。值得敬重。那人看起来十分疲惫，一个刚埋葬手足的人，自然会如此。也许察觉到你同情的目光，他问，能否与战团待上一阵。 | 你看见一个古怪男人沿路跛行，披着长斗篷，一只肩上挂着背囊。双眼一直盯地，直到看见你的靴子，才终于抬头。面对战团，他竟毫不惊慌，反而颇为欢迎你们在场，问是否能与佣兵们共度一夜，再继续前往%randomtown%。 | 一个拿着草叉的男人，正穿过歉收的农田。双脚拖过枯死的土地，扬起灰屑，随风飘散。来到路上，你叫住他，问从哪里来。那人是个短工，只想回家。附近的活儿全都“干”没了，确实是干旱的干。他舔舔裂开的嘴唇，问能否跟战团过一夜。不管怎样，看起来确实需要休息。 | 一个提着工具桶的男人，与你们迎面相遇。这条路可不适合让孤身一人撞上整支佣兵战团，而陌生人判断得很准，立刻放下东西，举起双手。

你叫他别慌，问往哪儿去。他解释，自己是从%randomtown%来的石匠，在那里的活儿已经做完，正回家与家人团聚。家在一处农舍，离这里还得走足足一天。那人又渴又累，问能否在战团借宿一晚，休息好了再赶路。 | 地平线上出现一道身影，在热气中模糊闪烁。它似乎停了下来，无疑也看见了你们。你没什么畏惧，催弟兄们继续走，很快遇见一个提着几袋杂物的男人。他坐在地上，见你们靠近，也懒得起身。他解释，自己已赶了好几天路，很想好好睡一觉。自然，他问，是否能在你们身旁度过这一夜。 | 你遇见一个虚弱疲惫的男人。他解释，自己一直在找走失的狗，可几乎已经放弃。回家之前，他大声琢磨着，若能跟你们好好歇一晚，也许还能恢复点力气，再找自己的杂毛狗一天。 | 路边，一个男人被秃鹫盯上了。他没有受伤，只是累得筋疲力尽。他用沙哑破裂的嗓音问，能否在弟兄们身旁过夜。}

0d3b172ba0198cbd5cfa.source:
{Oathbringers. Oathbringers. Oathbringers. Oathbringers. Oathbringers. Oathbringers. Oathbringers. Oathbringers. Oathbringers. Oathbringers. Oathbringers. Oathbringers!

Oathbringers Oathbringers Oathbringers Oathbringers Oathbringers Oathbringers!!!

OATHBRINGERS OATHBRINGERS OATHBRINGERS!!! | %name% is a diligent follower of the famed founder of the Oathtakers, Young Anselm. He believes himself blessed to be in the company of likeminded men who, thought not without fault, will try and do right in the world. | Some say %name% was an Oathtaker the moment he was born. It is the man himself who says this most often, though, which leads to some speculation that he was almost assuredly a terrible degenerate and he's just now making up for a horrific past. | When you think of an Oathtaker, %name% is about as clean as they come. Keeps his uniform and armor nice and tidy. Respects his superiors but is never mawkish. And he's absolutely excellent at directing steel through an Oathbringer's face. An outstanding Oathtaker if there ever was one. | Living in a faraway land, chasing honor and bringing death to Oathbringers, %name% heard of the %companyname%'s prestigious past and just had to find it and join up. He is a man of incredible resolve and most importantly he does not truck with Oathbringers. | Young Anselm's spirit has brought %name% to the %companyname%. Or so he says. Whatever brought him into the company, he is no doubt a talented fighter and will serve the outfit well. | The majesty of Young Anselm's spirit cannot be taken for granted. At least that is what %name% believes. He states that he is fights on behalf of the dead Oathtaker. Young Anselm must have been a spirited fellow indeed for this man is a wicked talent with any steel.  | Like many Oathtakers, %name% knows three divine elements: Young Anselm's spirit is to be cherished, Oaths are to be taken seriously, and all Oathbringers must die. Earning some coin on the side is also nice, which is why he has made his 'fourth' element fighting for outfits like the %companyname%. | It is a little peculiar for an Oathtaker to earn a sellsword's coin fighting, but %name% states that it was never forbidden by Young Anselm's teachings. Instead, it is the personal responsibility of the individual Oathtakers to maintain their oaths, which he can readily do cleaving enemies for the %companyname%. | %name% carries a ledger dedicated to only one kind of inventory: how many Oathbringers he's killed. He even has a list of when and where he did the deed, and of course how. The "how" entries even get a little extra dedication, with lines and lines meticulously describing how he dispatched his hated foes. Frankly, you like the man's enthusiasm. | %name%, a Oathtaker, is of such a singular mind it has you almost worried what he'd do without Young Anselm's directives. Now, that said, a part of you is curious how he'd fare dedicating himself to another craft. With his resolve and drive, he could probably weave an unbelievable basket, possibly even do it underwater like those learned experts. | %name% is everything one would want in an honorable man: smart, fit, and quite good swinging some steel. His dedication to the Oaths is only matched by his ability to absolutely demolish those who stand in his way. A perfect fit for the %companyname%, truly. | With the %companyname% gaining renown, it is becoming one of the more notable outfits in the land. Naturally, a talented and honorable man like %name% would seek to join up, albeit at a cost. His services to Young Anselm's cause mean his attention is no doubt split, but even being consumed by righteousness he is still an indefatigable fighter worth having in the %companyname%.}

0d3b172ba0198cbd5cfa.translation:
{誓言使者。誓言使者。誓言使者。誓言使者。誓言使者。誓言使者。誓言使者。誓言使者。誓言使者。誓言使者。誓言使者。誓言使者！

誓言使者 誓言使者 誓言使者 誓言使者 誓言使者 誓言使者！！！

誓言使者 誓言使者 誓言使者！！！ | %name%虔诚地追随立誓者那位赫赫有名的创始人——小安塞尔姆。他觉得，能与志同道合的人为伍，是自己蒙受的恩赐。这些人虽非完人，却都愿意在世上行正义之事。 | 有人说，%name%生来就是立誓者。不过，说得最多的恰恰是他本人，因此也有人怀疑，他过去八成是个无可救药的混账，如今才想弥补那段骇人的往事。 | 若要想象一个立誓者的模样，%name%几乎无可挑剔：衣甲整洁，尊敬上级，却从不谄媚。还有，他极擅长把刀剑捅进誓言使者的脸。真是个出类拔萃的立誓者。 | %name%原本生活在遥远的地方，追求荣誉，也为誓言使者送去死亡。听闻%companyname%的辉煌往事后，他非要找到这支战团并加入不可。他的意志坚定得惊人，更重要的是，他绝不与誓言使者为伍。 | 是小安塞尔姆的英灵，将%name%引向了%companyname%。至少他自己是这么说的。不论他究竟为何而来，毫无疑问，这是个武艺出众的战士，会好好为战团效力。 | 小安塞尔姆英灵的威严，不容轻视。至少%name%深信如此。他说自己正代这位已故立誓者作战。小安塞尔姆想必确实英武过人，因为眼前这人，无论拿起什么兵器，都使得厉害。  | 和许多立誓者一样，%name%坚守三条神圣的准则：敬重小安塞尔姆的英灵，严守誓言，以及杀光所有誓言使者。顺便挣点钱也不错，因此他又添上了“第四条”：替%companyname%这样的队伍作战。 | 立誓者像佣兵一样拿钱打仗，多少有些古怪。不过%name%说，小安塞尔姆的教诲从未禁止此事。守住誓言本就是每个立誓者自己的责任，而他替%companyname%斩杀敌人时，照样能履行这一点。 | %name%带着一本账册，只记一种数目：他杀了多少誓言使者。他甚至逐一列明何时、何地，当然还有如何下的手。说到“如何”，他尤其用心，一行接着一行，仔仔细细地描述自己怎样送那些仇敌上路。说实话，你挺喜欢他这股热情。 | 立誓者%name%心思如此专一，几乎让你担心，若没有小安塞尔姆的指引，他会做出什么。不过话说回来，你又有些好奇，要是他把这股劲头投入别的手艺，会做得怎样。凭他的决心和干劲，大概能编出个了不得的篮子，甚至能像那些学艺有成的专家一样，在水下编。 | %name%具备一位正直之士该有的一切：聪明、强健，挥舞刀剑也颇有本事。他对誓言的忠诚，只有他彻底击溃挡路者的本领能够相比。说真的，他与%companyname%再合适不过。 | %companyname%声名日隆，已成为这片土地上颇受瞩目的队伍之一。像%name%这样有本事又重荣誉的人，自然想来加入，当然，价钱也少不了。他还得为小安塞尔姆的事业效力，难免分心，但即便满脑子都是正义，他仍是个不知疲倦的战士，值得%companyname%将他收入麾下。}

656f617cbeb72764648e.source:
{Taking over the %companyname%, you had a vision for the company and its men, a vision that ended with you sitting on a king's throne and the world's most expensive wine sloshing around a golden goblet. That part didn't come true, but you did manage to lead the company to great heights in the civil war amongst the nobles.

 Such struggles are inevitable amongst the highborn and you took great advantage of the conflict to earn the %companyname% renown and riches. Of course, the brutality of the fighting also taught you that life was short and fickle for a fighting man. Once things settled down, you realized that, to the nobility, it didn't matter in the least who you were and what part you played in the conflict. You were just a cog, and you would always be just a cog. Taking that moment of reflection seriously, you decided to retire, leaving the company in about as good of a state as you could. | When you took over the %companyname%, you truly believed you could lead it to greatness. Those goals were probably a bit too lofty, but you did manage to at the very least build a company of incredible renown. As the nobles inevitably slid toward war, it didn't surprise you in the least to see that the company's services were the most popular in the land. The war proved itself as brutal and horrific as any you'd ever seen, but at least this time you walked away with more coin than you knew what to do with.

 Retiring with your pile of gold, you left the company in the command of the bravest mercenary still alive to take the job. The band continues its success to this day.}

656f617cbeb72764648e.translation:
{接手%companyname%时，你曾替战团和弟兄们描绘过一幅远景：最终，你会坐上国王的宝座，晃着金杯，品尝世上最昂贵的美酒。这一幕虽未成真，但在贵族之间的内战中，你确实带领战团攀上了新的高峰。

权贵之间的争斗在所难免，你也充分利用这场纷争，为%companyname%挣得了财富与声望。当然，残酷的战斗也让你明白：对一个靠厮杀吃饭的人而言，生命既短暂，又无常。待到局势平息，你才看清，在贵族眼里，你是谁、在战争中立过什么功，根本无关紧要。你只是一枚零件，也永远只会是一枚零件。想通了这一点，你决定退隐，趁战团还处于最好的时候，把它交了出去。 | 接手%companyname%时，你真心相信，自己能带它成就一番伟业。这个目标或许高了点，但你至少打造出了一支名声响亮的战团。当贵族们不可避免地走向战争，你毫不意外：全天下的佣兵里，就数你们最受欢迎。这场战争与你见过的任何一场一样残酷可怕，但至少，这一次你带着多得不知该怎么花的金子活了下来。

你拿着这笔财富退隐，把战团交给还活着、也愿意接班的最勇敢的佣兵。直到今天，他们仍然捷报频传。}

7816f7b41360aeb2f8c8.source:
{Having built the %companyname% to notable name recognition in the realms, the lords would bid against one another for your services, not only so you'd fight for them, but so they'd know at the very least they would not have to fight against you! With the crowns rolling in, and faith that the company would do well without you, it just seemed the proper time to put the sword away and retire to a life outside of war and killing.

Unfortunately, such popularity comes at a cost. The company kept falling into war-time contracts and, over time, was ground down. Brothers started to leave lest they become victim to the next nobleman who thought they knew best how to command the mercenaries. | After you left the company, seeking out a more docile life in the hills, you heard that the %companyname% grew in popularity amongst the nobility. With every war, counts and barons would seek out the company's services. However, with such popularity comes a price. Every new conflict, every new war, they would not come without losses. Slowly, but surely, the company's power dwindled, its numbers depleting either through casualties or men leaving to strike out like you did before it was too late. Last you heard, the company was almost wholly destroyed when a highborn commander used it for a frontal assault. | When you took over the %companyname%, it was a mere handful of men scrambling to survive. Now it's more akin to a boisterous business adventure. But staying the business of killing was never your goal in life. With enough money, you retired away and left the company in charge of %successor%, one of your most trusted men.

 Unfortunately, your successors didn't quite have the knack for keeping the men safe. Last you heard, they took contract after contract, forever seeking more and more crowns with no regard for their own safety. This aggressive pursuit of the coin eventually lead to the company's destruction in a battle between noble houses. Despite the %companyname%'s reputation, a noble baron had no problem using it as bait to draw out a much larger force. Thankfully, a few men did manage to retire just before this battle.}

7816f7b41360aeb2f8c8.translation:
{%companyname%在你的经营下声名鹊起，各地领主争相加价请你出战，不光是想让你为他们效力，也为确保至少不必与你为敌！克朗源源不断地流入钱箱，你又相信战团即使没有你也能过得不错，于是觉得，是时候收起剑，过一种远离战争与杀戮的日子了。

可惜，如此受欢迎也有代价。战团接连卷入战时委托，日渐损耗。弟兄们开始离去，免得成为下一个自以为懂得指挥佣兵的贵族手中的牺牲品。 | 离开战团、到山间寻求安稳生活后，你听说%companyname%在贵族中愈发吃香。每逢战事，伯爵和男爵都争着雇用他们。可这样的名气也有代价。每一场新冲突、每一次新战争，都免不了折损人手。战团的力量一点点衰退，人数不断减少：有人伤亡，有人学着你的样子，趁还来得及，抽身另谋出路。你最后听到的消息是，一名贵族指挥官命令他们正面强攻，战团几乎因此全军覆没。 | 你接手%companyname%时，它不过是一小撮挣扎求生的人。如今，倒更像一门红红火火的买卖。可你从没打算一辈子靠杀人谋生。钱赚得够多，你便退了下来，把战团交给最信任的弟兄之一——%successor%。

可惜，你的接班人并不擅长保全手下的性命。听说他们接完一个委托又接一个，只想着多挣些克朗，全然不顾风险。这种不知收手的贪心，最终让战团毁在一场贵族家族之间的战争里。一位男爵丝毫没把%companyname%的名声当回事，照样拿他们作诱饵，引出人数远胜己方的敌军。好在，至少有几个弟兄在那场仗之前及时退了下来。}

display_fallbacks.[img]gfx/ui/events/event_60.png[/img]{Yo:
[img]gfx/ui/events/event_60.png[/img]{你啐了一口，清清嗓子，随即拔剑，将商队护卫砍倒。%randombrother%见状，立刻大声命令%companyname%的其余人一同动手。杀戮短促而混乱，弟兄们已经扑到面前，商队护卫还没弄清发生了什么。

你解开囚犯的锁链。他千恩万谢，随即让你带路。%SPEECH_ON%只要到了%noblesettlement%，让他们看见我这张活蹦乱跳、笑容满面的脸，你就等着被克朗淹没吧！%SPEECH_OFF% | 你拔剑划过护卫的脸。他转过身，你又一剑劈开他的头颅，脑浆从斜插的碎骨之间涌出，像破裂的酥点。%randombrother%看见这一幕，立刻招呼其余弟兄投入战斗。他们很快解决了剩下的商队护卫。你放开%noble%时，他指向大路。%SPEECH_ON%去%noblesettlement%！我的家人会给你难以想象的重赏！%SPEECH_OFF% | 商队护卫刚转过身，你便把匕首从他腋下捅入，直刺心脏。他含混地哼了一声，倒在地上。另一个护卫绕过来，看见这一幕，紧接着便被你的长剑开膛破肚。他的惨叫可一点也不含糊。战斗很快打响，却完全一边倒，%companyname%轻易便杀光了商队护卫。

尘埃落定后，%noble%恢复了自由。他揉着青紫的手腕，指向%noblesettlement%。%SPEECH_ON%出发吧，送我回家！你们如此英勇，我一定要把你们的钱袋塞得满满的！%SPEECH_OFF%}

